{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T16:47:38.361644Z","id":"3ef08663454a28332affb94c726ac28cf46eedfc07bcd36a1f368fad4e941681","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1324},"end":{"line":1368},"content_hash":"ddf90a27cffb9eae9f415b9f193ba4f15b3c221446be555e0e4c03e03e2abb50"},"summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","supersedes":"ccb6b8f30bcf6872c0a5fa98243cedabd0a2175c84015da6e6120955c255bbba","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:30.047085Z","id":"7cba5514a453d4b465d89b59e4853e4108ddc681d6e30a4f8aba438d5f94726c","body":{"detail":"Store::register_session_restoring returns the note (spec 2026-10-08 §6.7) and FeedbackWaiters::set_note keeps it in a map until the session's first feedback poll; nothing in the database records it. The watches are restored either way; only the note is lost.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":78},"end":{"line":85},"content_hash":"4d34e0a7296ea8660cd602c9300047b0e20c46410bd0aec30d2f7a513618e2e6"},"summary":"A restored session's note is kept in daemon memory, so a daemon restart before its first poll drops it","tags":["revisit:a session column or table for one-shot notes","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:30.047908Z","id":"5e5e1b6f1441eada3498fb34443b262cf0899406d9704cb95a79cb322ff815f9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4f6952d","summary":"Fixed: session ends make ended items, and their view is {name, reason, text, questions, requests, threads: [{id, artifact_id, title, url}]} (ended_view in crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs); api_agents::reregistering_after_an_idle_end_restores_watches_and_says_what_ended reads it from Sam's inbox and passes.","supersedes":"f5901d5045603d245dcfb54e966bb4e85c71f89234e341040adb04e37a521461","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:48.882578Z","id":"9c5c196ec2163b8cf5eb8bb316e1c727a3ed659637182ac166bab1794ef2a54f","body":{"detail":"holds_surface(person) (holds_owner_topics() for the owner) is true while any stream of that person holds questions or inbox, and those topics stay subscribed while the tab is hidden (web/shell/src/stream.ts:23-27). crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create() uses it, for the asking agent's person, to decide whether a hook question waits in Clax or is released to the terminal at once. So a Clax tab left open in the background makes every AskUserQuestion of that person's agents wait in Clax until it is answered there, released, timed out, or Esc is pressed (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:289-302). Decision needed: should 'open' instead mean a tab seen or focused recently, or the extension's side panel being open?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1026},"end":{"line":1051},"content_hash":"ef0267ee57042e6f58c4b3ab575dbe015b81d840852637892266f23d038afb03"},"summary":"A hidden tab counts as an open Clax surface, so the AskUserQuestion hook waits in Clax","supersedes":"9862a052b84d69269b0c489938b6ac8807fb15aa89c2d4ddb3c29a3d20bfd25e","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:48.883128Z","id":"fced511a559bf6667ba182a011321f477054ec281aabd76c35f360480cb20493","body":{"detail":"api_agent_auth::the_extractor_refuses_a_persons_agent_on_an_owner_agents_route now asserts that every Filtered need in ROUTES is live. The not_yet branches (agent.rs Agent<N> extraction and the body gate) stay for a Filtered route added later; remove them, with FILTERED_LIVE, once no task plans one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":503},"end":{"line":503},"content_hash":"e07bad372e55913af9df7b2c800d2741a700fd885fb02cc043d3e30bf32f99fd"},"summary":"Every Filtered need is now in FILTERED_LIVE, so the 503 not_yet path serves no route","supersedes":"c33df3c09ad0e7e887f99e246f06d0bd8f0dfa7cd85c97afe2343a9f39574710","tags":["people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:48.883671Z","id":"b6a13e3d6b72b59d4689d106e1d8a84cd77acf03a583712dcb09cc406b1c7e00","body":{"detail":"Every handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":948},"end":{"line":948},"content_hash":"95e634966fc956bcf03f44fdf7131faa6bc9307f6e163a961719bf6f762fe602"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve Person/Viewer lazily in Agent<N> (only a person's agent needs the store), or fold the read into the handler's own store_call.","summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","supersedes":"8f0b1f881b0455bf779731bd46ac244b3d3db1229d5a1c848e39bf0ccfe7bdec","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:48.884209Z","id":"7c7b9439a7f86fb70143b48438b101db5d13d25f2a70167314cd2cc1f8b7df67","body":{"detail":"Withhold::approval runs Store::request_state once per thread that withholds anything, so a listing of N such threads makes N indexed reads (plus st.owner() when the owner is withheld). Versions and names are cached per call. vis_threads_ms (Task 25) will show whether it matters.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1293},"end":{"line":1320},"content_hash":"05c56d201c29c0092d6039e9c09166c4bdf07ea63e935e45f87326bf15b12593"},"summary":"Each thread with withheld content costs one approval_requests query in a listing","supersedes":"ec36dc70f09ff80b1a17efb6cf244dad0bbb9cd5bc4b823b0e4a8ca46d44f9a7","tags":["perf","visibility","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:48.884736Z","id":"a654f0ac848ca965ef1bc04bc18719530b907dd2ec3ea595a331e14049789b86","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1343},"end":{"line":1387},"content_hash":"ddf90a27cffb9eae9f415b9f193ba4f15b3c221446be555e0e4c03e03e2abb50"},"summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","supersedes":"3ef08663454a28332affb94c726ac28cf46eedfc07bcd36a1f368fad4e941681","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:51:18.818348Z","id":"2fcc21657db2138d6dcbd74c316197e82f2f7c159e3ddb61948dbf2e2cb4d73d","body":{"detail":"Withhold::approval runs Store::request_state once per thread that withholds anything, so a listing of N such threads makes N indexed reads (plus st.owner() when the owner is withheld). Versions and names are cached per call. vis_threads_ms (Task 25) will show whether it matters.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1366},"end":{"line":1393},"content_hash":"05c56d201c29c0092d6039e9c09166c4bdf07ea63e935e45f87326bf15b12593"},"summary":"Each thread with withheld content costs one approval_requests query in a listing","supersedes":"7c7b9439a7f86fb70143b48438b101db5d13d25f2a70167314cd2cc1f8b7df67","tags":["perf","visibility","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:51:18.818947Z","id":"1802405d86056c0cd5fbd71b130426e9aae2272e383322e7cb76a86aecbc697f","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1416},"end":{"line":1460},"content_hash":"ddf90a27cffb9eae9f415b9f193ba4f15b3c221446be555e0e4c03e03e2abb50"},"summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","supersedes":"a654f0ac848ca965ef1bc04bc18719530b907dd2ec3ea595a331e14049789b86","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/extension.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:51:18.822513Z","id":"449ccf4e83b2f6febd0c3e07c531d5f3e34d6457e7feb9053abe8c8406d973e5","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e63a6a28fafb18a57f9f09db75ebb6066e303494f17c2e62fab3f0b9ffff7d51","summary":"35cec880 admits GET /api/approvals/requests for the extension credential (Rule::Any, as spec 2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person §15 names: the panel's count and links). Request views carry author, artifact, thread, count and state, never the withheld content, for gallery artifacts too, so this widens the live-only posture in the same way as /api/inbox and /api/questions. Deciding, approving, revoking, GET /api/approvals and every /api/people route stay refused (the_allowlist_names_each_route_and_the_artifact_it_needs_live; api_people::the_extension_lists_the_owners_approval_requests_and_decides_nothing). The decision this record asks for is unchanged and still the owner's; if the owner restores the live-only posture, this route needs the same filtering.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:21:42.607369Z","id":"f559d622c6bcca21daf23cead0ae2af5ffde2cb634ed222851bccf366f273aed","body":{"detail":"Withhold::approval runs Store::request_state once per thread that withholds anything, so a listing of N such threads makes N indexed reads (plus st.owner() when the owner is withheld). Versions and names are cached per call. vis_threads_ms (Task 25) will show whether it matters.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1422},"end":{"line":1449},"content_hash":"05c56d201c29c0092d6039e9c09166c4bdf07ea63e935e45f87326bf15b12593"},"summary":"Each thread with withheld content costs one approval_requests query in a listing","supersedes":"2fcc21657db2138d6dcbd74c316197e82f2f7c159e3ddb61948dbf2e2cb4d73d","tags":["perf","visibility","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:21:42.610104Z","id":"0bff06035fe29526cc9380b595d01a3df710809f0f1822b6cddbb5f5dce777ff","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1472},"end":{"line":1516},"content_hash":"ddf90a27cffb9eae9f415b9f193ba4f15b3c221446be555e0e4c03e03e2abb50"},"summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","supersedes":"1802405d86056c0cd5fbd71b130426e9aae2272e383322e7cb76a86aecbc697f","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:37:47.228538Z","id":"5fba35e066ade9ae8248535a92abd0b44289ef926db10e40f8ece1a20464ec78","body":{"detail":"person() falls back to clax_core::feedback::display_name, which gives 'Viewer' for an empty name. A connected person's People (web/shell/src/people/People.svelte:142) lists the approval they gave at connect as 'Viewer · everywhere'; the owner can also invite a person named 'Viewer' (POST /api/people/invites {name: 'Viewer'} is 201), whose approval reads the same. The owner's row has no display name on a fresh install.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":15},"end":{"line":21},"content_hash":"c53aab52c14fcc81f8e6cdebe3c3862cf26f6f3e033c4f50c18d3ca780200410"},"suggested_fix":"Give the owner's author view an owner flag (or the name 'the owner' when unnamed), and have People render it as the owner.","summary":"An approval or request whose author is the owner names them 'Viewer' when the owner has no display name, indistinguishable from a person named Viewer","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:02:20.886728Z","id":"dd492480928b694a94fc375fce91623cbcd3c5deef6e2228b134d95f19a558e9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:8b8a8051","summary":"approval_view and request_view now carry author.owner and name an unnamed owner 'The owner' (crates/clax-server/src/approvals.rs person). Evidence: cargo test -p clax-server --test integration approvals_name_the_owner_as_such_and_their_page passes (author.owner true, name 'The owner' for the owner; owner false, name 'Mia' for a person); People shows it ('The owner', or '<name> (the owner)'), covered by web/shell/src/people/People.test.ts 'marks a named owner as the owner'.","supersedes":"5fba35e066ade9ae8248535a92abd0b44289ef926db10e40f8ece1a20464ec78","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:10:15.786496Z","id":"83810fedd6a750637b449b77443a262f55d2b2dc836826409ce2299c2da4c590","body":{"detail":"Failure: Sam approves Mia's content in one thread (scope thread) on the owner's artifact 'Quarterly Review', and Sam has not approved the owner. Sam's agent's GET /api/artifacts/<aid> answers title null with withheld.authors naming the owner; the same agent's GET /api/approvals answers artifact_title 'Quarterly Review'. A thread-scoped approval does not cover an artifact's title (spec 2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person §8.1 rule 3, §8.2: a title's authors are artifacts.text_authors_json), and the title's author need not be the approval's author at all. §7.5 makes GET /api/approvals Own: only fields written by the caller's own person or Clax's own fields; a title is neither (M10, O9). The owner's agents (OwnerAgent) reach the same route. Reproduced with a temporary test in crates/clax-server/tests/api_approvals.rs built on Two::new, mia_thread, mia_sends_to_sam and sam_decides(rid, \"thread\"), then t.sam_agent GET of both routes. The integration test approvals_name_the_owner_as_such_and_their_page passes only because sam_approves_the_owner covers the owner's title everywhere.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":33},"end":{"line":38},"content_hash":"a1aa128af91019fd5e4145b9a5a0a5ac24c9950a33136972239b29188730b65d"},"suggested_fix":"Give artifact_title only to browser callers (People is the only reader: web/shell/src/people/PersonCard.svelte scopeOf, People.svelte scopeOf), or filter it with the caller's Visibility as GET /api/artifacts does (null with withheld authors). Add a test where an agent's approval list names a page whose title its person has not approved.","summary":"approval_view's artifact_title is not run through Visibility, so GET /api/approvals hands an agent the title of a page whose title is withheld from it","tags":["review","visibility","spec:7.5","spec:8","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:10:15.786835Z","id":"f8c3c4ee08fe3807804f06c3a36c3b808d1c558351cee441ee211442100514d0","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/approvals.rs person() now names an unnamed owner 'The owner' with author.owner true, but WithheldAuthor here still takes clax_core::feedback::display_name(\"\"), which is 'Viewer'. A person's agent reading the owner's artifact without an approval gets withheld.authors [{name: 'Viewer', public_id: <owner>}], indistinguishable from a person named Viewer (POST /api/people/invites {name: 'Viewer'} is accepted). crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs:793 builds the placeholder text from the same name.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1397},"end":{"line":1410},"content_hash":"0b622d8d52ac38e574fa84a9f714a893f935bb9c6f94ceaae66bedd96a89713b"},"suggested_fix":"Share one owner-aware naming helper between approvals.rs person() and the withheld authors (and the placeholder text).","summary":"A withheld field's authors still name an unnamed owner 'Viewer'","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:03:27.819077Z","id":"f1bd99be34df7e6314bea21079f531b5e2ba0b79799712c506bfdd8357d2555b","body":{"detail":"require_seat is called by the thread write routes in crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs (create, comment, send, send_batch, resolve, reopen, delete). The db routes (crates/clax-server/src/routes/docs.rs) and the room socket (crates/clax-server/src/routes/room.rs) act for the viewer through the page and do not ask it, so a spectator's page still writes documents and room messages. Publish and PATCH take TokenOrAgent, so only the owner (reserved) or agents (never spectators) reach them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":307},"end":{"line":322},"content_hash":"62b7cd5410aab02c14acb57ceb1db7491fc7000c3d8019e8a1d7065146ed850d"},"suggested_fix":"Decide whether a page's db writes and room messages count as the viewer writing (spec 2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design §7 lists comment, send, resolve, publish and rename); if so, call require_seat from the docs write handlers with the page's viewer caller and refuse room sends from an unseated viewer.","summary":"A spectator's page writes (db documents) and room messages are not refused; only thread writes are","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:03:27.819403Z","id":"d3825226cf112efcfc36a387d51f80b930bda0962b48c1247c80c7cb9e805e01","body":{"detail":"The native daemon has no per-artifact live socket like the hosted prototype's /api/artifacts/:id/live (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts fetch); the shell's one shared stream subscribing an artifact's artifact, presence or working topic holds the seat (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs use_seats, crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs update). A live relay of pointers, selections and typing on another connection asks LiveSeats::is_seated, or holds a seat itself with LiveSeats::take and leave under its own connection key and hears idle releases through LiveSeats::on_idle; nothing natively takes an agent seat yet, as agents hold no live connection here.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":190},"end":{"line":195},"content_hash":"32ceb5fbc1090c840186b68a86c8d81947c5c3f81c3c2528455f8ab93d97ec23"},"summary":"Seats are held by /api/stream subscriptions, not by a live socket of their own","tags":["revisit:a live relay socket lands beside /api/stream","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:03:27.819640Z","id":"25fd5c9fa3003694faf9c161ac86675963c5b7a71ffe3608877bfef96ce8ab58","body":{"detail":"Hub::detach parks the stream's seats when its Conn is dropped, which happens when hyper sees the connection close (immediate for a closed tab or context in the tests: crates/clax-server/tests/api_seats.rs load_150_people_on_100_seats, web/e2e/seats.spec.ts). A connection that hangs without closing holds the seat until the next keep-alive write fails, or until the idle release (3 minutes without a here presence report).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1118},"end":{"line":1122},"content_hash":"7b970f113a2cab27cc4b859d11385b56033f15cf3a164b9e2cd759395dba038c"},"summary":"A closed browser's seat frees only once the daemon notices its stream's connection dropped","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:04:39.285020Z","id":"68aaf7c77543aaeaf86df52598963b8359305e197d29689cfd1d0533043f055e","body":{"detail":"holds_surface(person) (holds_owner_topics() for the owner) is true while any stream of that person holds questions or inbox, and those topics stay subscribed while the tab is hidden (web/shell/src/stream.ts:23-27). crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create() uses it, for the asking agent's person, to decide whether a hook question waits in Clax or is released to the terminal at once. So a Clax tab left open in the background makes every AskUserQuestion of that person's agents wait in Clax until it is answered there, released, timed out, or Esc is pressed (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:289-302). Decision needed: should 'open' instead mean a tab seen or focused recently, or the extension's side panel being open?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1161},"end":{"line":1186},"content_hash":"ef0267ee57042e6f58c4b3ab575dbe015b81d840852637892266f23d038afb03"},"summary":"A hidden tab counts as an open Clax surface, so the AskUserQuestion hook waits in Clax","supersedes":"9c5c196ec2163b8cf5eb8bb316e1c727a3ed659637182ac166bab1794ef2a54f","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:38:27.008878Z","id":"b43750f609de3c253082a0e1fb7dde8593bea15cb7b2186c839fe89954f088bb","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"f1bd99be34df7e6314bea21079f531b5e2ba0b79799712c506bfdd8357d2555b","summary":"Decided by the owner's requirement for live seats: \"the degraded users are read only and get a perhaps delayed cached version\". A spectator writes nothing as a person: db writes and room messages are refused like thread writes (403 spectator), and the shell shows them as unavailable.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:38:27.008957Z","id":"4ecc07d2124d3cba1fb33287f3864b149874447634b1b6067629e7f29ed6a69e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ae98d606","summary":"Fixed in ae98d606 (server) and 5cfb8765 (shell). Every db write route in crates/clax-server/src/routes/docs.rs (put, patch, delete, batch, str_replace, acquire) calls require_seat; the room socket nacks a spectator's emit with spectator and drops their presence (crates/clax-server/src/routes/room.rs Conn::spectator). The shell's db, comments and room capabilities reject a spectator's writes without a request (unavailable; upstream_error for room) and map a daemon spectator refusal to the same codes. Evidence: cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_seats: a_spectators_page_writes_no_documents_and_sends_no_room_messages ok (8 passed); npx vitest run shell/src/caps: db, comments and room spectator tests pass (1500 passed in all).","supersedes":"f1bd99be34df7e6314bea21079f531b5e2ba0b79799712c506bfdd8357d2555b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:49:19.122871Z","id":"f6296fb72cf1a973606e71b99878501a3f59985239091066bebfc91cc6a273e9","body":{"detail":"The host is chosen by cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\") alone, with native-only dependencies under target tables, so `scripts/check-wasm.sh -p clax-server` needs no flags and a native build cannot select Worker code by mistake. A `native` default feature plus a `worker` feature would let a native build compile the Worker paths (for instance to test the Durable Object glue natively) at the cost of a second axis to keep consistent.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":3},"end":{"line":12},"content_hash":"366d7f0d9c9e9d1892f6d6a5d44e0a8d1834c02323ffe6ae08b59ba8e7caaa10"},"summary":"A `worker` cargo feature to pick the host, beside the target","tags":["wasm","revisit:the Worker glue needs native tests","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:49:19.122952Z","id":"9af7ab09a0d0675c48c817c8d7a5327c64ec147406ad73e422d39a80c74a1e0d","body":{"detail":"With rmcp's local feature, serve_directly spawns with tokio::task::spawn_local, which could run inside a LocalSet polled by the Worker's event loop; rmcp's own timeouts would still need tokio's timer, which has no driver there. Not taken: it relies on tokio internals working without a runtime context. The adapter calls the tools' methods directly (they take no RequestContext; rmcp's Peer::new is pub(crate) in rmcp 3.5's service.rs).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":102},"end":{"line":114},"content_hash":"ae6c2ada9c1d603a2bdb8bf280c66640be7f8f807c57d0d117c50720e5142a1c"},"summary":"Drive rmcp's serve_directly on a tokio LocalSet inside the Worker instead of a JSON-RPC adapter","tags":["wasm","revisit:rmcp offers a runtime-agnostic stateless handler","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:17:05.464768Z","id":"a9869be6987d1f2b6a51276cda1a106a6d66c980f5e2e8aa7394759981032b3e","body":{"detail":"Identity::caller makes the token an OwnerAgent whenever a session is named (path or X-Clax-Session), known or not; audit_actor records an agent only for a known session of the token's, the agent marker, or x-clax-via mcp, else the owner. Measured through GET /api/_test/audit/ctx: Authorization Bearer + X-Clax-Session 01JB9S00000000000000000099 (no session) and X-Clax-Session not-a-ulid both give {\"type\":\"owner\"}. Today's clients send the marker, so this bites only an older or third-party agent side; it breaks audit spec section 5.2's rule that one request is never an agent to Caller and the owner to the journal.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":461},"end":{"line":468},"content_hash":"75fc91286c48244768b0a0e9a1d2af39937a039081897bf71644933e706cbb12"},"suggested_fix":"When the token names any session that is not known, record the sessionless agent (channel as named, else mcp) instead of the owner; add the case to the_agent_channel_marker_makes_the_token_an_agent.","summary":"The token naming an unknown or non-ULID session without the agent marker is recorded as the owner, while Caller counts it as OwnerAgent","supersedes":"aad27e37c6fc12484dd639d56fdd0b30bd06e13e6870f9d185cc2bd8f085b86f","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:17:05.466629Z","id":"87a97144d0f52632a3922b0b25f75c0bb8a819534306d4a142d54d01024b4fed","body":{"detail":"Hub::detach parks the stream's seats when its Conn is dropped, which happens when hyper sees the connection close (immediate for a closed tab or context in the tests: crates/clax-server/tests/api_seats.rs load_150_people_on_100_seats, web/e2e/seats.spec.ts). A connection that hangs without closing holds the seat until the next keep-alive write fails, or until the idle release (3 minutes without a here presence report).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1119},"end":{"line":1123},"content_hash":"7b970f113a2cab27cc4b859d11385b56033f15cf3a164b9e2cd759395dba038c"},"summary":"A closed browser's seat frees only once the daemon notices its stream's connection dropped","supersedes":"25fd5c9fa3003694faf9c161ac86675963c5b7a71ffe3608877bfef96ce8ab58","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:17:05.468454Z","id":"166165c60e8eaac9977db1ddc18cabb0452f82ce17fa50345babbbad831451fa","body":{"detail":"holds_surface(person) (holds_owner_topics() for the owner) is true while any stream of that person holds questions or inbox, and those topics stay subscribed while the tab is hidden (web/shell/src/stream.ts:23-27). crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create() uses it, for the asking agent's person, to decide whether a hook question waits in Clax or is released to the terminal at once. So a Clax tab left open in the background makes every AskUserQuestion of that person's agents wait in Clax until it is answered there, released, timed out, or Esc is pressed (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:289-302). Decision needed: should 'open' instead mean a tab seen or focused recently, or the extension's side panel being open?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1162},"end":{"line":1187},"content_hash":"ef0267ee57042e6f58c4b3ab575dbe015b81d840852637892266f23d038afb03"},"summary":"A hidden tab counts as an open Clax surface, so the AskUserQuestion hook waits in Clax","supersedes":"68aaf7c77543aaeaf86df52598963b8359305e197d29689cfd1d0533043f055e","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:17:05.470235Z","id":"994422fe5a491ffacb022ee7de02fb59f5c2e088b8acdb610fd19f739f5bfe3f","body":{"detail":"With rmcp's local feature, serve_directly spawns with tokio::task::spawn_local, which could run inside a LocalSet polled by the Worker's event loop; rmcp's own timeouts would still need tokio's timer, which has no driver there. Not taken: it relies on tokio internals working without a runtime context. The adapter calls the tools' methods directly (they take no RequestContext; rmcp's Peer::new is pub(crate) in rmcp 3.5's service.rs).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":105},"end":{"line":117},"content_hash":"ae6c2ada9c1d603a2bdb8bf280c66640be7f8f807c57d0d117c50720e5142a1c"},"summary":"Drive rmcp's serve_directly on a tokio LocalSet inside the Worker instead of a JSON-RPC adapter","supersedes":"9af7ab09a0d0675c48c817c8d7a5327c64ec147406ad73e422d39a80c74a1e0d","tags":["wasm","revisit:rmcp offers a runtime-agnostic stateless handler","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:17:05.482865Z","id":"7ebee36b357f3d98637196f41bb5cc47b4bef1b886c015c83406ff7a34d041d7","body":{"detail":"crate::seats::subscribe (called by POST /api/stream/<id>, crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs update) takes the artifact's seat for connection stream:<id> when the stream holds none of its live topics yet. If two calls add live topics of the same artifact at once and one then fails (TooMany, Hidden), its rollback leaves the seat the other call's topics rely on. The shell's hub sends one change at a time per stream, so this needs a hand-made client.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":383},"end":{"line":404},"content_hash":"d1bde61f01852bf26b409a8e492815bad85c59a044543e416aeee2aa7d62106e"},"summary":"Two concurrent subscription changes of one stream can leave it on an artifact's live topics without its seat","tags":["live-seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:21:12.878488Z","id":"3f93e950a2480d6dbea8f1f94889b24c0f49b24ff731ec5e91c8e8e1d2fdfeab","body":{"detail":"Event::Drafts goes to Chan::Working with Gate::Any, and GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/drafts answers any caller DeniedToGrants lets through, so every browser that reaches the daemon (which reads every artifact it serves) gets each revision's token. Hosted spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design.md §16.4 sends drafts to signed-in people only (members and guests), never to anonymous link viewers. Narrowing to the owner and connected people (Caller::Person, a named viewer) would need a gate on the stream channel and on the listing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":501},"end":{"line":501},"content_hash":"b62828095bb3ed67ea1038d11d81f2bd9240262eb59dc098aba6b03645c34d72"},"summary":"Drafts reach every stream subscriber of working:<id>, unnamed LAN viewers included","tags":["drafts","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:29:02.662104Z","id":"a0367be36216f8709f164acb2554bbca8f8a5a65a37630d6675a44f48fa2d932","body":{"detail":"api_agent_auth::the_extractor_refuses_a_persons_agent_on_an_owner_agents_route now asserts that every Filtered need in ROUTES is live. The not_yet branches (agent.rs Agent<N> extraction and the body gate) stay for a Filtered route added later; remove them, with FILTERED_LIVE, once no task plans one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":519},"end":{"line":519},"content_hash":"e07bad372e55913af9df7b2c800d2741a700fd885fb02cc043d3e30bf32f99fd"},"summary":"Every Filtered need is now in FILTERED_LIVE, so the 503 not_yet path serves no route","supersedes":"fced511a559bf6667ba182a011321f477054ec281aabd76c35f360480cb20493","tags":["people","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:29:02.663759Z","id":"196bd6512118a6f1fc57629c67ab742ca64b6d2fac21180afe3b36618c0738e4","body":{"detail":"Every handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":964},"end":{"line":964},"content_hash":"95e634966fc956bcf03f44fdf7131faa6bc9307f6e163a961719bf6f762fe602"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve Person/Viewer lazily in Agent<N> (only a person's agent needs the store), or fold the read into the handler's own store_call.","summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","supersedes":"b6a13e3d6b72b59d4689d106e1d8a84cd77acf03a583712dcb09cc406b1c7e00","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:29:02.665309Z","id":"424c90c6e6637f18fc8a5ec97a4ecc708479be82d93628d9b7dff079b81d4a5c","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/approvals.rs person() now names an unnamed owner 'The owner' with author.owner true, but WithheldAuthor here still takes clax_core::feedback::display_name(\"\"), which is 'Viewer'. A person's agent reading the owner's artifact without an approval gets withheld.authors [{name: 'Viewer', public_id: <owner>}], indistinguishable from a person named Viewer (POST /api/people/invites {name: 'Viewer'} is accepted). crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs:793 builds the placeholder text from the same name.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1402},"end":{"line":1415},"content_hash":"0b622d8d52ac38e574fa84a9f714a893f935bb9c6f94ceaae66bedd96a89713b"},"suggested_fix":"Share one owner-aware naming helper between approvals.rs person() and the withheld authors (and the placeholder text).","summary":"A withheld field's authors still name an unnamed owner 'Viewer'","supersedes":"f8c3c4ee08fe3807804f06c3a36c3b808d1c558351cee441ee211442100514d0","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:29:02.666882Z","id":"08a77c123acb2ba1176c0041fb5713a6435022ad3b93b2bf1a598b81901c9641","body":{"detail":"Withhold::approval runs Store::request_state once per thread that withholds anything, so a listing of N such threads makes N indexed reads (plus st.owner() when the owner is withheld). Versions and names are cached per call. vis_threads_ms (Task 25) will show whether it matters.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1427},"end":{"line":1454},"content_hash":"05c56d201c29c0092d6039e9c09166c4bdf07ea63e935e45f87326bf15b12593"},"summary":"Each thread with withheld content costs one approval_requests query in a listing","supersedes":"f559d622c6bcca21daf23cead0ae2af5ffde2cb634ed222851bccf366f273aed","tags":["perf","visibility","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:29:02.668338Z","id":"e5630b5298781b0e651ec41353d08b673b45072704b7d5bda4d4ff05ac5a7a52","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1477},"end":{"line":1521},"content_hash":"ddf90a27cffb9eae9f415b9f193ba4f15b3c221446be555e0e4c03e03e2abb50"},"summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","supersedes":"0bff06035fe29526cc9380b595d01a3df710809f0f1822b6cddbb5f5dce777ff","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:29:02.669819Z","id":"9a99e3200976c8f66e6c57ae68bb0e2315e4dd557a463b23bca2c4442780b394","body":{"detail":"holds_surface(person) (holds_owner_topics() for the owner) is true while any stream of that person holds questions or inbox, and those topics stay subscribed while the tab is hidden (web/shell/src/stream.ts:23-27). crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create() uses it, for the asking agent's person, to decide whether a hook question waits in Clax or is released to the terminal at once. So a Clax tab left open in the background makes every AskUserQuestion of that person's agents wait in Clax until it is answered there, released, timed out, or Esc is pressed (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:289-302). Decision needed: should 'open' instead mean a tab seen or focused recently, or the extension's side panel being open?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1028},"end":{"line":1053},"content_hash":"ef0267ee57042e6f58c4b3ab575dbe015b81d840852637892266f23d038afb03"},"summary":"A hidden tab counts as an open Clax surface, so the AskUserQuestion hook waits in Clax","supersedes":"9c5c196ec2163b8cf5eb8bb316e1c727a3ed659637182ac166bab1794ef2a54f","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:49.645857Z","id":"7862d2943821d190ddd9f51d5c81dda1cf926a676a0492ef5b93c5c6db1cd7d7","body":{"detail":"Event::Drafts now goes to Chan::Drafts(aid), which Topic::Working joins only for a stream opened for a person (stream.rs Topic::chans, the person argument that also gates Chan::Agents). GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/drafts answers Caller::Owner and Caller::Person and 403 forbidden to Caller::Viewer and Caller::Anonymous (routes/drafts.rs list). The draft URL stays token-only beside refuse_agents, since a frame on the artifact origin carries no clax_viewer cookie; the token reaches no one else.","kind":"comment","references":"3f93e950a2480d6dbea8f1f94889b24c0f49b24ff731ec5e91c8e8e1d2fdfeab","summary":"Settled by docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design.md §16.4: drafts reach signed-in people only, here the owner and connected people (Caller::Owner, Caller::Person); unnamed viewers and agents get no listing, no event and no token","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:49.645955Z","id":"91a267f8a1d95bc8414d5bedce7b6c3fc46f1d3aae85c671acab582cae39fde9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:37b5fb6b","summary":"Fixed in 37b5fb6b: `cargo test -p clax-server --test integration drafts` passes drafts_reach_the_owner_and_connected_people_only_and_keep_the_agent_working (the owner's and Mia's streams hear [drafts, working], an unconnected LAN viewer's and a no-credential stream hear [working]; the listing answers 403 forbidden to both)","supersedes":"3f93e950a2480d6dbea8f1f94889b24c0f49b24ff731ec5e91c8e8e1d2fdfeab","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:49.653844Z","id":"36b65d11b1971000e3cdb0f20ae9e7040c808d93cc74786c1c3b91464e419fb4","body":{"detail":"holds_surface(person) (holds_owner_topics() for the owner) is true while any stream of that person holds questions or inbox, and those topics stay subscribed while the tab is hidden (web/shell/src/stream.ts:23-27). crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create() uses it, for the asking agent's person, to decide whether a hook question waits in Clax or is released to the terminal at once. So a Clax tab left open in the background makes every AskUserQuestion of that person's agents wait in Clax until it is answered there, released, timed out, or Esc is pressed (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:289-302). Decision needed: should 'open' instead mean a tab seen or focused recently, or the extension's side panel being open?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1035},"end":{"line":1060},"content_hash":"ef0267ee57042e6f58c4b3ab575dbe015b81d840852637892266f23d038afb03"},"summary":"A hidden tab counts as an open Clax surface, so the AskUserQuestion hook waits in Clax","supersedes":"9a99e3200976c8f66e6c57ae68bb0e2315e4dd557a463b23bca2c4442780b394","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/live_layers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:23:02.667004Z","id":"4faa527c83f7d5ae9d5c47728a18c6b3746bf498e83ab629137a1f2e312c3063","body":{"detail":"seated() always answers true, so every person who reaches GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/live gets and sends the live layers; nothing caps the sockets per artifact (spec 2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design §16.1: 100 people seats, guests at most 20, reserved seats for the owner and named shares, idle seats released after 3 minutes). It is called in one place, crates/clax-server/src/routes/live_layers.rs session(), before the socket joins the hub; a refused socket closes 4429, which web/shell/src/view/live-layers.ts LiveSocket treats as final. Seat counting replaces this function's body.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":24},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"bd814d52356eae867a16f57017f2f3b54040c8196c1a8bc3f1f0f876dace8a61"},"summary":"Live seats are a stub: every person's live socket is seated","tags":["live-layers","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/live_layers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:16:01.912724Z","id":"851438fc29f8056d397e31f89f926dc03f658aeff7839cc10ed762df7dce90e7","body":{"detail":"A batch carries every changed sender whole for a receiver that is behind: with 30 detailed senders each holding a cursor near MAX_LIVE_MESSAGE_BYTES (16 KiB) and a 2000-character draft, one batch is several hundred KiB, and SOCKET_QUEUE (16) of them can wait behind a receiver whose socket does not drain, so a few MiB per stalled socket, per artifact, before try_send drops the next one and marks it for a whole resend. Bounded, but more than needed: a lost batch is already answered with full state (Relay::resend).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":21},"end":{"line":22},"content_hash":"152e995d6c246399649d0054fe7ebb59abc2d37fc3a650bfabec7652df161c8a"},"suggested_fix":"Lower SOCKET_QUEUE to a few batches (the full-state resend covers what is dropped), or cap a batch's bytes and resend the rest at the next flush.","summary":"A stalled receiver may hold up to 16 queued batches, each up to about 30 senders' largest cursors and drafts","tags":["live-layers","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/live_layers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:55:35.891276Z","id":"2ce521877e80f639123777dba6ba81c6e1c46c92a12a91a11555a5f6dae390a2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:8e6f7e7e","span":{"start":{"line":24},"end":{"line":26},"content_hash":"2e4cf0084d57303785e0795c627704249a65e1910d6e1d9f85d85812f9cdbf81"},"summary":"The stub is gone: crates/clax-server/src/routes/live_layers.rs session() takes the person's seat (crate::seats::claim_for, LiveSeats::take) under its own connection key live:<n> before the socket joins the hub, leaves it when the socket closes, and closes 4429 seat_idle when the seat is released (seats::install routes live: connections to LiveLayers::unseat). Tests: api_live_layers::a_spectators_socket_is_closed_and_relays_nothing and an_idle_seat_closes_its_socket pass; e2e/seats.spec.ts checks the spectator holds no open live socket and Join live opens one","supersedes":"4faa527c83f7d5ae9d5c47728a18c6b3746bf498e83ab629137a1f2e312c3063","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:12:06.158862Z","id":"a65317782e56e23b8b5f53b3da1515f9f3c9292e6a78a905b9d4779180ab42a1","body":{"detail":"Hub::dispatch also runs from tasks spawned off the request path: inbox::listen and approvals::listen consume store change notifications in clax_rt::spawn tasks (crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs:349-392, crates/clax-server/src/approvals.rs:193-200), questions::start_grace closes a question after its grace (crates/clax-server/src/questions.rs:296), flight::drive streams a sample, and agent::verify_layer notes a grant's use (crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs:1620). Their frames reach the queues after that request's drain ran and sit there until the next request, socket message or alarm, which on a quiet artifact can be minutes. Draining every socket after every message also costs O(open sockets) per incoming message; at the rates of docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design.md §16.5 (30 senders at 10 a second, 100 seats) that is most of the object's work.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":87},"end":{"line":97},"content_hash":"be75567dc83870e766b84b32b847dbedaa714e8dee939d3c9ecc8a40dafde3f0"},"suggested_fix":"Have Hub::dispatch mark the subscribers it queued for as dirty and wake one outlet task (a tokio::sync::Notify that a spawn_local'd drain awaits, no timer, so it does not hold the object awake), which drains only the dirty queues.","summary":"The Worker outlet drains only after a request or alarm, so frames dispatched later wait for the next one","tags":["wasm","durable-object","hibernation","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:12:06.159285Z","id":"a5637e4e199a0ed4161facb7054d02f3752e2e189f2aa3593d5eabb1bad8bc4e","body":{"detail":"After an eviction the Hub (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs) is empty: streams, rings, detached streams under GRACE, and the one sequence, which restarts. open_for cannot reopen a stream under the attachment's ID (a new stream always gets new_id(), stream.rs:840), so each socket gets a new stream ID that must be written back with serializeAttachment and announced to the client in a new ready frame. The caller, credential hash and person a StreamEntry is opened with (stream.rs:302-322) must come from the attachment and be checked against the store again before update() re-subscribes, since grants expire, rights change and people are revoked while the object sleeps. What stream::Conn's poll does (Conn::checking's still_live, clear_lag after a resync, detach on close to start GRACE, end; stream.rs:1226-1301) needs equivalents in the outlet. Cloudflare documents a 2,048-byte limit for a socket's serializeAttachment, which bounds the topics an attachment can carry.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":94},"end":{"line":97},"content_hash":"ce04088bc75f75d5d5958d001329e67290f13fcaae98f32e1fbbefa1585f962d"},"suggested_fix":"Add Hub::reopen(attachment) that takes the stream's ID, caller, credential, person and topics, re-checks them, subscribes with resync, and returns the frames to send; have the Worker call it for every socket from getWebSockets() in the constructor before it serves anything.","summary":"Reopening each socket's stream from its attachment and sending resync does not rebuild what the hub held","tags":["wasm","durable-object","hibernation","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:12:06.160038Z","id":"102650cd60e01c897d55cdfc3380a88762416c002b190b4f9694d316970b2cde","body":{"detail":"On akesling/clax-artifacts the streams hold live seats (Hub::use_seats, commit f0be8e1e), keyed stream:<id>. After a wake they come back in whatever order the object re-subscribes its sockets, so with more viewers than seats a seated person can return a spectator (an unseated frame) and a spectator seated, and the idle release's last-input times restart. clax_core::presence::Presence empties too: a presence resync answers with nobody until each tab reports again, so every chip disappears and reappears. Presence reports and seat heartbeats arrive as HTTP requests (PUT /api/viewers/me/presence), each of which wakes a hibernated object, which limits what hibernation saves.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":99},"end":{"line":100},"content_hash":"4060f858cc5fa16e01ff4b68bdf12f179c01e40179ed799a4ead71ca4303ca94"},"suggested_fix":"Keep seat holders with their pools and last input, and presence entries, in the object's storage (or each socket's attachment) and restore them before the first request after a wake; carry presence reports and heartbeats as socket messages, or answer heartbeats with setWebSocketAutoResponse.","summary":"Live seats and presence are lost when the object hibernates, and rebuilding them by re-subscribing reorders who is seated","tags":["wasm","durable-object","hibernation","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:12:06.160331Z","id":"61069320e3db13e3a93b448432143e6b1f1c6e29873f3667b2786566b2bc487d","body":{"detail":"room::Rooms (crates/clax-server/src/room.rs) keeps members, peer labels and a broadcast::Sender per room, and the per-socket relay that turns a Membership into socket frames is routes/room.rs, native only. The Worker needs a drain of each socket's broadcast::Receiver (try_recv, Lagged answered with a peers snapshot) beside the hub's queues. At eviction no Membership is dropped, so no left is sent; on wake the memberships must be rebuilt from attachments without a joined or left for every socket, and the relay's rate budgets restart. The live layers of docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design.md §16.3-16.4 (typing, comment drafts, cursors, agents' drafts served at /c/:id/draft/...) are in memory as well: an agent's draft would be lost at eviction while people still see its Show draft.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":99},"end":{"line":100},"content_hash":"4060f858cc5fa16e01ff4b68bdf12f179c01e40179ed799a4ead71ca4303ca94"},"summary":"Rooms are not drained by the hub's outlet: their frames ride tokio broadcast receivers, and memberships vanish without Drop at eviction","tags":["wasm","durable-object","hibernation","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:12:06.160593Z","id":"dfae291e43fb5c268c73de5ed416822113cdac0f4092efad9c95aae342995d7e","body":{"detail":"start_grace waits s.question_grace on clax_rt::time::sleep (TokioSleeper) inside clax_rt::spawn. In a Durable Object that setTimeout keeps the object from hibernating for the whole grace, and an eviction drops the task, so the question never closes Unwaited. The alarm plan in crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs:68-75 covers the daemon's loops but not this timer.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":296},"end":{"line":299},"content_hash":"63eff0fcd57f234d6f5a115a0b4b0ab9c10ba9c126210a1446609268b8cd3809"},"suggested_fix":"Give AppState a Sleeper for the Worker that records the deadline for the object's alarm (earliest due) instead of sleeping, and close due questions from the alarm.","summary":"A question's grace runs on a timer in a spawned task, which in a Durable Object keeps it awake and is lost at eviction","tags":["wasm","durable-object","hibernation","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:12:06.160789Z","id":"06246bd54686f5f6ec3a9155e7cb96c65c2b3151226cd4f563d783fcf0b7e950","body":{"detail":"AppState is built, and the hub, inbox and approvals listeners are started (hub.listen, inbox::listen, approvals::listen), in crates/clax-server/src/daemon.rs, which is cfg(not(target_arch = \"wasm32\")). The Durable Object needs the same state and listeners with its own clock, sleeper and store; a copy would drift from the daemon's.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":18},"end":{"line":22},"content_hash":"82b55968f4470006f3493c461514a3bf280cfbcb5ffa692248d6266064f36dc9"},"suggested_fix":"Move AppState construction and listener start-up into a function both hosts call, with the host-specific parts (home, bind, port, sleeper, shutdown) as arguments.","summary":"No host-neutral AppState builder: the Worker would copy daemon.rs's wiring","tags":["wasm","durable-object","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:12:06.160881Z","id":"1528f694e37a1dea06b91a2864832b6e3f8b9c518a3081fcca987f9f886c0cab","body":{"detail":"conn_of feeds is_loopback through live::sees_live_pages and identity::peer_of, and api_host_allowed through request_host_allowed's local address. A Durable Object that inserts a Conn built from CF-Connecting-IP, or a placeholder loopback address, would admit token-free callers as local (live pages, the owner cookie route). Nothing in a Worker is local to the owner's machine.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":278},"end":{"line":293},"content_hash":"dbd5285883bcd43277f1327a7f80ab3c3a65e24cb99c315005c2dd49a7b77d29"},"suggested_fix":"Make conn_of answer None on wasm32 until a hosted notion of local exists, so PeerConn always refuses there, or document that the Worker inserts no Conn.","summary":"On wasm32 a Conn in a request's extensions grants this machine's trust","tags":["wasm","auth","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:23:33.190551Z","id":"83c405b680c7ea4901d14b5542ccc92015b3bacc568f6cefe5f311979690247b","body":{"detail":"holds_surface(person) (holds_owner_topics() for the owner) is true while any stream of that person holds questions or inbox, and those topics stay subscribed while the tab is hidden (web/shell/src/stream.ts:23-27). crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create() uses it, for the asking agent's person, to decide whether a hook question waits in Clax or is released to the terminal at once. So a Clax tab left open in the background makes every AskUserQuestion of that person's agents wait in Clax until it is answered there, released, timed out, or Esc is pressed (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:289-302). Decision needed: should 'open' instead mean a tab seen or focused recently, or the extension's side panel being open?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1027},"end":{"line":1052},"content_hash":"ef0267ee57042e6f58c4b3ab575dbe015b81d840852637892266f23d038afb03"},"summary":"A hidden tab counts as an open Clax surface, so the AskUserQuestion hook waits in Clax","supersedes":"9c5c196ec2163b8cf5eb8bb316e1c727a3ed659637182ac166bab1794ef2a54f","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:23:33.193462Z","id":"b9c7c0a32a04cf82a41d0204d2ac01e4154b336e761ace8dffe917365550a1bf","body":{"detail":"Identity::caller makes the token an OwnerAgent whenever a session is named (path or X-Clax-Session), known or not; audit_actor records an agent only for a known session of the token's, the agent marker, or x-clax-via mcp, else the owner. Measured through GET /api/_test/audit/ctx: Authorization Bearer + X-Clax-Session 01JB9S00000000000000000099 (no session) and X-Clax-Session not-a-ulid both give {\"type\":\"owner\"}. Today's clients send the marker, so this bites only an older or third-party agent side; it breaks audit spec section 5.2's rule that one request is never an agent to Caller and the owner to the journal.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":461},"end":{"line":468},"content_hash":"75fc91286c48244768b0a0e9a1d2af39937a039081897bf71644933e706cbb12"},"suggested_fix":"When the token names any session that is not known, record the sessionless agent (channel as named, else mcp) instead of the owner; add the case to the_agent_channel_marker_makes_the_token_an_agent.","summary":"The token naming an unknown or non-ULID session without the agent marker is recorded as the owner, while Caller counts it as OwnerAgent","supersedes":"aad27e37c6fc12484dd639d56fdd0b30bd06e13e6870f9d185cc2bd8f085b86f","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:13:42.713850Z","id":"9954324acf6b480034776987b500687d84e54397e536aabc247b82d726bacd95","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/approvals.rs person() now names an unnamed owner 'The owner' with author.owner true, but WithheldAuthor here still takes clax_core::feedback::display_name(\"\"), which is 'Viewer'. A person's agent reading the owner's artifact without an approval gets withheld.authors [{name: 'Viewer', public_id: <owner>}], indistinguishable from a person named Viewer (POST /api/people/invites {name: 'Viewer'} is accepted). crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs:793 builds the placeholder text from the same name.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1399},"end":{"line":1412},"content_hash":"0b622d8d52ac38e574fa84a9f714a893f935bb9c6f94ceaae66bedd96a89713b"},"suggested_fix":"Share one owner-aware naming helper between approvals.rs person() and the withheld authors (and the placeholder text).","summary":"A withheld field's authors still name an unnamed owner 'Viewer'","supersedes":"f8c3c4ee08fe3807804f06c3a36c3b808d1c558351cee441ee211442100514d0","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:13:42.718645Z","id":"aa81386da3fbbf68a96b53beff991b50a08a006c93e290b2b5cc6888c15ddd11","body":{"detail":"Withhold::approval runs Store::request_state once per thread that withholds anything, so a listing of N such threads makes N indexed reads (plus st.owner() when the owner is withheld). Versions and names are cached per call. vis_threads_ms (Task 25) will show whether it matters.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1424},"end":{"line":1451},"content_hash":"05c56d201c29c0092d6039e9c09166c4bdf07ea63e935e45f87326bf15b12593"},"summary":"Each thread with withheld content costs one approval_requests query in a listing","supersedes":"f559d622c6bcca21daf23cead0ae2af5ffde2cb634ed222851bccf366f273aed","tags":["perf","visibility","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:13:42.756007Z","id":"145c7c1c4fed00eab0f879cdbb41766628a3d8ae0f27906b6302afff57e42058","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1474},"end":{"line":1518},"content_hash":"ddf90a27cffb9eae9f415b9f193ba4f15b3c221446be555e0e4c03e03e2abb50"},"summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","supersedes":"0bff06035fe29526cc9380b595d01a3df710809f0f1822b6cddbb5f5dce777ff","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:19:06.766355Z","id":"e25576b906f628d933df4bbf7db10f0d38e36482284706720948a645be7e081b","body":{"detail":"The TypeScript prototype (hosted/src/content.ts) serves content without a rights check, its capability a 40-hex commit in the URL. Here the address carries only the artifact ID (12 Crockford characters, 60 bits) and a version number, so an unshared page's content is readable by whoever learns its ID (a pasted link, a referrer from inside the page). The sandboxed frame's requests carry no SameSite=Lax cookie, so gating content by session would break pages' own subresources.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":433},"end":{"line":437},"content_hash":"51d5fb7ec42a53581a593068d46717c1f9e0c193095a847442ff8a01ebdbab19"},"suggested_fix":"Serve hosted content at an unguessable per-version address (a content hash or a signed, expiring path) the bootstrap names, and refuse /c/<id>/v/<n>/ in hosted mode.","summary":"A hosted daemon serves artifact content (/c/, /_blob/, content hosts) to anyone who has its address: the 60-bit artifact or asset ID is the capability","tags":["status:needs-decision","hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:19:06.766414Z","id":"f0089fb1aecc2cbcc4556c5d565977af78df63e3eea05efc1b3fedf9e88c6704","body":{"detail":"Multi-person rights (crates/clax-core/src/rights.rs) bind agent channels; browser routes do not check them. The prototype gave each person a role per artifact (viewer to owner) and listed only what they could read. Here every member's gallery lists every artifact, and People's rights (clax:reader, collaborator) narrow nothing in their browser.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":457},"end":{"line":459},"content_hash":"8885b30ad1e959e13ebc57337f3214e46ab5101be409aa3847e2aff50cd0f311"},"suggested_fix":"In the gate, check a member's person rights (Store::person_rights) at the artifact a route names, and filter GET /api/artifacts for persons.","summary":"A signed-in person's browser reads and comments on every artifact, as a LAN viewer does on a local daemon: person rights limit their agents only","tags":["status:needs-decision","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:19:06.766467Z","id":"55cf3a1e2a94d452c0d7e67a1c3b50b816098bac369b622e52331a94ce97b8b5","body":{"detail":"The internet reaches these routes. Codes are 60-bit (invites) or 256-bit (sign-in links, sessions) and the setup secret is compared by hash, so guessing is infeasible, but PUT /api/viewers/me with no session makes a viewer row and a session per call. See also the open record on LAN viewers' writes (crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs:28).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":396},"end":{"line":400},"content_hash":"ee6ab47c7a06d50adbcee91a859a72e5fc784170d2869a31f4650e3f74b7db44"},"suggested_fix":"Cap guests and sessions made per peer address (behind a proxy, a trusted forwarded-for header) per minute.","summary":"Hosted sign-in has no rate limit: guest creation, setup secret and code guesses, and sign-in link redemption are unbounded","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:19:06.766512Z","id":"1f73502c3ad51f7bcd29ac73f51772242fd3101578b9578865989e528cffadf6","body":{"detail":"Only minting an agent token records events (grant.approve and grant.token, crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs mint_agent_token). The hosted routes are merged outside crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs, so its UNAUDITED guard does not see them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":666},"end":{"line":676},"content_hash":"8faf8d3187f04e20070df9ac36200023512eea579c522fc54a0e88b55c8728dd"},"suggested_fix":"Add audit kinds for session.sign_in/sign_out, invite.redeem and artifact.link (crates/clax-core/src/audit.rs, toolpath rendering), or list the routes with reasons in a guard of their own.","summary":"Hosted sign-in events (setup, an invite redeemed in the browser, a sign-in link redeemed, sign out, a guest made, a page shared by link) are not in the audit journal","tags":["hosted","audit","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:19:06.766597Z","id":"ddce075eea172897c0c3ecbe2d8fdf64bdcefa000fa3f00931eb10ebced51cb9","body":{"detail":"The prototype let a commenter resolve or reopen threads they started (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design.md section 7). LinkAccess::rights (crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs) holds no comments resolve; checking a thread's creator in the gate would need a store read per request.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":285},"end":{"line":287},"content_hash":"f8564687d21d97fe5615a5674a21b9444ea4c648abef2584844c61b8e5250507"},"summary":"A guest may not resolve or reopen threads, even their own","tags":["revisit:guests ask to resolve their own threads","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:55:24.307856Z","id":"c0a04b6eb373516881059476333d516b69cf75f4af74ee29543daa73d79d541a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:668d33b2","summary":"Fixed: a hosted daemon serves a version's content only at /c/<aid>/v/<n>/k/<key>/ (and /v/<n>/k/<key>/ on the content host), the key an HMAC of <aid>/<n> under a key made from the daemon token (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs content_key, content_path, serve_content), and an asset only at /_blob/<id>?k=<key> (asset_key); anything else is 404, with Referrer-Policy: no-referrer. The artifact, versions, publish and bootstrap views carry content_key; the shell frames at it. Evidence: cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_hosted::content_is_served_only_at_its_key_and_an_id_alone_reads_nothing passes (the ID alone, a member's cookie, the content host, another version's key, a cut or upper-cased key, an asset's bare ID: 404), as does web/e2e/hosted.spec.ts 'the owner's browser has the owner's surfaces...' (frame src /v/1/k/<32 hex>/, its h1 shown; /c/<aid>/v/1/ 404).","supersedes":"e25576b906f628d933df4bbf7db10f0d38e36482284706720948a645be7e081b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:55:24.309565Z","id":"3406fede53f94618c7eae4bec4c7b70339fecac8892a7c7c6ca5ca1b9f5a7879","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3d133f22","summary":"Fixed: a person's session carries their rights (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs MemberRights, member_need, member_gate; crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs Agent::from_request_parts, read_rights, named_artifact, also_needs): an artifact they may not read (by rights or its link) answers 404 on /a/<aid>, every /api/artifacts/<aid>/ route, viewer marks and stream topics; GET /api/artifacts and approval lists leave it out; each Agent route checks its action's right (403 not_permitted); /api/events is the owner's. Evidence: cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_hosted::a_persons_rights_limit_their_browser_and_the_owner_sees_everything passes (Sam, rights at one artifact, lists and opens it alone and may not resolve; Mia and the owner see both), and web/e2e/hosted.spec.ts shows Sam's gallery with one card and /a/<other> answering 404.","supersedes":"f0089fb1aecc2cbcc4556c5d565977af78df63e3eea05efc1b3fedf9e88c6704","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:55:24.312811Z","id":"7bef1ec95a0be3e02fb01137ad3e0003227bcb6bde213973cfb9411cf53ea339","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3b1cb3e6","summary":"Fixed: setup, invite looks and redemptions, sign-in link redemptions and guest names each take one of the client's attempts from a token bucket on an injected clock (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs Attempt, Limits, Hosted::attempt): setup and guests 5 then one per 120 s, codes 10 then one per 30 s, 429 rate_limited with retry_after_s. The client is the peer, or CF-Connecting-IP with [hosted] behind_cloudflare = true; IPv6 counts by /64. Evidence: api_hosted::setup_sign_in_and_guests_are_limited_per_client_on_the_clock and the unit tests hosted::tests::attempts_come_back_at_their_pace_per_client_and_kind and clients_are_cloudflares_word_only_behind_cloudflare_and_ipv6_counts_by_64 pass.","supersedes":"55cf3a1e2a94d452c0d7e67a1c3b50b816098bac369b622e52331a94ce97b8b5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:55:24.314219Z","id":"cbb0d99fd5fe346d1fc591fdfeb993ce77f71c07ce62ffb75479da9c5b11c833","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c21c6da8","summary":"Fixed in 3b1cb3e6 and c21c6da8 with existing kinds: every browser sign-in records session.start (harness browser, how setup|invite|link|guest, expires_at, invite_id for an invite; ids.session browser-<20 hex of the cookie's SHA-256>) as the person signed in; sign out records session.end reason sign_out (c1b72fdf adds reason replaced when a browser signs in anew); sharing by link records artifact.update with field link_access; minting a token already recorded grant.approve and grant.token. Evidence: cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_hosted::sign_ins_and_sign_outs_are_in_the_audit_journal passes.","supersedes":"1f73502c3ad51f7bcd29ac73f51772242fd3101578b9578865989e528cffadf6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:55:24.322908Z","id":"f0d537be5222e31f8a086c768869694594199ba02dadc3deaf1573567993fe09","body":{"detail":"member_gate drops `gallery` from such a person's subscriptions because gallery events (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs routes, project) carry every artifact's titles and thread summaries; their gallery refreshes on load only.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":727},"end":{"line":727},"content_hash":"cc7f883b42e8d834a7aa6a6e9f0ce461e48a8702065827af2cbdbbf741b80e96"},"suggested_fix":"Gate gallery items per subscriber by artifact (a read filter fixed at subscribe time) instead of dropping the topic.","summary":"A person whose rights do not read every artifact gets no gallery stream topic, so their gallery does not update live","tags":["hosted","ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:55:24.322992Z","id":"2bce94ff6576d3ec534e860ea12a852bdc362b5f8a0dc7e7e051b338b038cba3","body":{"detail":"member_need checks the artifact only when the query names one; without it the routes answer every artifact this viewer has marks on (IDs and counts, no titles). Inbox items addressed to the person stay after their rights narrow.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":647},"end":{"line":651},"content_hash":"658bd678f5f2ca9606250a4a71b16315b8e871172a66044341faa0416f943b70"},"suggested_fix":"Filter those answers with Agent::read_rights as GET /api/artifacts does.","summary":"A person's /api/viewers/me/attention and /api/viewers/me/seen without ?artifact=, and their inbox items, are not filtered by their rights","tags":["hosted","visibility","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:55:24.323067Z","id":"c595bf071c5ca6f57f6b08a0f22c1ed2d8ca9c660ad92c55c2eefcb3ee248772","body":{"detail":"content_key is an HMAC of <aid>/<n> under the daemon token, as the prototype's commit hash (hosted/src/content.ts) never expired either. A person whose rights narrow, or a guest whose page stops being shared, still reads every version address they were handed (not later versions). A new daemon token changes every key.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":397},"end":{"line":399},"content_hash":"cd8d880448cdb31132019e34c90867877b5c99850f7b334415ffebc58c2ce63d"},"suggested_fix":"Mix a per-artifact generation into the key and bump it when the page stops being shared or a person's rights narrow.","summary":"A content key never expires: whoever saw a version's keyed address keeps reading it after losing the right","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:55:24.323132Z","id":"1123c32a59773e59d99faba4f021060318cd288aea97ffe7a9184972baa8f744","body":{"detail":"Limits holds its buckets in a Mutex<HashMap>; a restarted daemon forgets them, and a Cloudflare deployment with several isolates or Durable Objects would count per instance. Past MAX_CLIENTS (10000) clients the map is cleared.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":146},"end":{"line":149},"content_hash":"c3d9cee2df2daa7466bec6f2d7785f46a526e8ffaae9cfc54cec9c2e75b2fe50"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the buckets in the store (or one Durable Object) in the Worker build.","summary":"The abuse limits live in the process's memory: they reset on restart and are per instance","tags":["hosted","security","wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:55:24.323239Z","id":"33f1e34ee8e656541b02f3b4807ab577cb8340ca22680de8563b375de9d03561","body":{"detail":"PUT /api/viewers/me with no session makes a guest viewer row and a session whatever the site shares; Attempt::Guest limits it to five per client and then one per two minutes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1263},"end":{"line":1271},"content_hash":"7b0b50000594786778769269c90c8b6ed7c453ad2d601bcdc1a9e8dbea8ea63c"},"suggested_fix":"Require the page the visitor names (artifact_id in the body) to be shared for commenting.","summary":"A visitor may become a guest without any page being shared by link","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.040003Z","id":"768648273e4265d6daa3cadb3ba327be03e252dda94381a1fa1e1aeb67e572ae","body":{"detail":"Identity::caller makes the token an OwnerAgent whenever a session is named (path or X-Clax-Session), known or not; audit_actor records an agent only for a known session of the token's, the agent marker, or x-clax-via mcp, else the owner. Measured through GET /api/_test/audit/ctx: Authorization Bearer + X-Clax-Session 01JB9S00000000000000000099 (no session) and X-Clax-Session not-a-ulid both give {\"type\":\"owner\"}. Today's clients send the marker, so this bites only an older or third-party agent side; it breaks audit spec section 5.2's rule that one request is never an agent to Caller and the owner to the journal.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":481},"end":{"line":488},"content_hash":"75fc91286c48244768b0a0e9a1d2af39937a039081897bf71644933e706cbb12"},"suggested_fix":"When the token names any session that is not known, record the sessionless agent (channel as named, else mcp) instead of the owner; add the case to the_agent_channel_marker_makes_the_token_an_agent.","summary":"The token naming an unknown or non-ULID session without the agent marker is recorded as the owner, while Caller counts it as OwnerAgent","supersedes":"a9869be6987d1f2b6a51276cda1a106a6d66c980f5e2e8aa7394759981032b3e","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.042582Z","id":"ad52f1115f90250fca33988c43daf0d7004936e0a9c4a559f69114cfe0dc8ed9","body":{"detail":"The prototype let a commenter resolve or reopen threads they started (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design.md section 7). LinkAccess::rights (crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs) holds no comments resolve; checking a thread's creator in the gate would need a store read per request.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":880},"end":{"line":882},"content_hash":"f8564687d21d97fe5615a5674a21b9444ea4c648abef2584844c61b8e5250507"},"summary":"A guest may not resolve or reopen threads, even their own","supersedes":"ddce075eea172897c0c3ecbe2d8fdf64bdcefa000fa3f00931eb10ebced51cb9","tags":["revisit:guests ask to resolve their own threads","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.044825Z","id":"f791bb502e5f532c598858ae8bd107731caabb1634456a0c8a2a30e559ea6875","body":{"detail":"member_gate drops `gallery` from such a person's subscriptions because gallery events (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs routes, project) carry every artifact's titles and thread summaries; their gallery refreshes on load only.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":730},"end":{"line":730},"content_hash":"cc7f883b42e8d834a7aa6a6e9f0ce461e48a8702065827af2cbdbbf741b80e96"},"suggested_fix":"Gate gallery items per subscriber by artifact (a read filter fixed at subscribe time) instead of dropping the topic.","summary":"A person whose rights do not read every artifact gets no gallery stream topic, so their gallery does not update live","supersedes":"f0d537be5222e31f8a086c768869694594199ba02dadc3deaf1573567993fe09","tags":["hosted","ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.047073Z","id":"73f34cb2ed924fa166cd9a2282eda80f55e48921fccb925e342b4cbdaa80dc9d","body":{"detail":"member_need checks the artifact only when the query names one; without it the routes answer every artifact this viewer has marks on (IDs and counts, no titles). Inbox items addressed to the person stay after their rights narrow.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":650},"end":{"line":654},"content_hash":"658bd678f5f2ca9606250a4a71b16315b8e871172a66044341faa0416f943b70"},"suggested_fix":"Filter those answers with Agent::read_rights as GET /api/artifacts does.","summary":"A person's /api/viewers/me/attention and /api/viewers/me/seen without ?artifact=, and their inbox items, are not filtered by their rights","supersedes":"2bce94ff6576d3ec534e860ea12a852bdc362b5f8a0dc7e7e051b338b038cba3","tags":["hosted","visibility","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.050167Z","id":"1453082772e2801382b7cec1de246790613ce9214644b3513a5668ba9e4db5f3","body":{"detail":"content_key is an HMAC of <aid>/<n> under the daemon token, as the prototype's commit hash (hosted/src/content.ts) never expired either. A person whose rights narrow, or a guest whose page stops being shared, still reads every version address they were handed (not later versions). A new daemon token changes every key.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":400},"end":{"line":402},"content_hash":"cd8d880448cdb31132019e34c90867877b5c99850f7b334415ffebc58c2ce63d"},"suggested_fix":"Mix a per-artifact generation into the key and bump it when the page stops being shared or a person's rights narrow.","summary":"A content key never expires: whoever saw a version's keyed address keeps reading it after losing the right","supersedes":"c595bf071c5ca6f57f6b08a0f22c1ed2d8ca9c660ad92c55c2eefcb3ee248772","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.055736Z","id":"44693a7a90e200798dab34cffdcff6aaa9dd5cc09d5dd6d41a4de32ef9c58c5a","body":{"detail":"PUT /api/viewers/me with no session makes a guest viewer row and a session whatever the site shares; Attempt::Guest limits it to five per client and then one per two minutes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1269},"end":{"line":1277},"content_hash":"7b0b50000594786778769269c90c8b6ed7c453ad2d601bcdc1a9e8dbea8ea63c"},"suggested_fix":"Require the page the visitor names (artifact_id in the body) to be shared for commenting.","summary":"A visitor may become a guest without any page being shared by link","supersedes":"33f1e34ee8e656541b02f3b4807ab577cb8340ca22680de8563b375de9d03561","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/audit.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.155278Z","id":"c54728e1ec79e88560e12e784ba8590ae44505df1d12756c26ee4c9fce111ca0","body":{"detail":"The extractor's own job costs one interactive round trip before the handler's. Measured with a scratch test against TestServer (debug build, 4 runtime workers, 300-400 sequential requests, three rounds): GET /api/_test/audit/ctx, which is only the extraction, p50 201-227 us against /healthz 144-157 us at idle (about 60 us per job); with 8 clients looping on GET /api/viewers/me, a one-job route at p50 411-420 us, p95 557-566 us, and the extraction alone p50 426-445 us, p95 572-1316 us, so each audited write pays about one more queue wait. Agent tool calls also add one writer transaction for tool.call and, under Claude Code, one for tool.call_id, read-only tools and each wait_for_feedback included. The perf gates passed on unchanged budgets (docs/verification.md §10). Not fixed in the branch's final round: 23 handlers in seven route modules (artifacts, assets, docs, feedback, live, sites, threads, plus the live refile context) take AuditCtx, each with its own job structure, so moving the resolve into their jobs is a change to every audited route rather than a cheap one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":333},"end":{"line":342},"content_hash":"fde9f6c59006fc734d792edc237fec3e153f53108171e787e2ff1539a90cf319"},"suggested_fix":"Take DeferredAudit in the handlers and resolve it inside the handler's own store job, as the session routes already do with for_session.","summary":"Every request that records an event now takes two interactive store jobs: the AuditCtx extractor resolves the actor in its own store_call before the handler's","supersedes":"f2075a1688947b87c9c407943835d210a623aae8186e884a9276f6af3d98cf04","tags":["review","perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/viewer.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.157765Z","id":"9b8b3a6d7be75ffded915adba181e0e7baa3e8e2c42186e8a5615f63e0a0a56b","body":{"detail":"A Clax-Grant caller writing a thread or a comment without author_kind agent is attributed to its grant's person (author_public_id, display name), as the token's agents are to the owner. Storing it as an agent comment with its session would show it as the agent's in the shell, but a thread's first comment is a viewer comment (NewThread) and a viewer comment forwards the thread, so the semantics would change. Authorship, which the filter needs, is right either way.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":115},"end":{"line":130},"content_hash":"83ee2c4a800f2125d8a2bab39db59a095b257bef4fe8d7cf0c04be3b50037d7d"},"summary":"A person's agent's viewer-kind comment is stored as its person's viewer comment, not as an agent comment","supersedes":"96c44912cb51710b6ff473b0919ef2b0efb660968cef25be8fd6150360a95ee0","tags":["revisit:when the shell shows which agent wrote a person's comment","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.160286Z","id":"c2d26633facd8c19e2713a99febfc52b6920be586a00ed7f2dc694d30b70adbb","body":{"detail":"Every handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1005},"end":{"line":1005},"content_hash":"95e634966fc956bcf03f44fdf7131faa6bc9307f6e163a961719bf6f762fe602"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve Person/Viewer lazily in Agent<N> (only a person's agent needs the store), or fold the read into the handler's own store_call.","summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","supersedes":"b6a13e3d6b72b59d4689d106e1d8a84cd77acf03a583712dcb09cc406b1c7e00","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:17.675984Z","id":"94df2fd69a858c26cc56b8247a49fe136f8b95d8350e933a74b58fc9b1e2c492","body":{"detail":"The native daemon has no per-artifact live socket like the hosted prototype's /api/artifacts/:id/live (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts fetch); the shell's one shared stream subscribing an artifact's artifact, presence or working topic holds the seat (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs use_seats, crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs update). A live relay of pointers, selections and typing on another connection asks LiveSeats::is_seated, or holds a seat itself with LiveSeats::take and leave under its own connection key and hears idle releases through LiveSeats::on_idle; nothing natively takes an agent seat yet, as agents hold no live connection here.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":191},"end":{"line":196},"content_hash":"32ceb5fbc1090c840186b68a86c8d81947c5c3f81c3c2528455f8ab93d97ec23"},"summary":"Seats are held by /api/stream subscriptions, not by a live socket of their own","supersedes":"d3825226cf112efcfc36a387d51f80b930bda0962b48c1247c80c7cb9e805e01","tags":["revisit:a live relay socket lands beside /api/stream","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:17.680094Z","id":"403a40ef7c6e5bf3bbbc1621b5884f75da9560d42fe1ad34d8d833eb36a322eb","body":{"detail":"Hub::detach parks the stream's seats when its Conn is dropped, which happens when hyper sees the connection close (immediate for a closed tab or context in the tests: crates/clax-server/tests/api_seats.rs load_150_people_on_100_seats, web/e2e/seats.spec.ts). A connection that hangs without closing holds the seat until the next keep-alive write fails, or until the idle release (3 minutes without a here presence report).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1164},"end":{"line":1168},"content_hash":"7b970f113a2cab27cc4b859d11385b56033f15cf3a164b9e2cd759395dba038c"},"summary":"A closed browser's seat frees only once the daemon notices its stream's connection dropped","supersedes":"87a97144d0f52632a3922b0b25f75c0bb8a819534306d4a142d54d01024b4fed","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:17.688973Z","id":"f572abaacd082ae49f1f4af7996bed17c37d110fdb47fe3fd7f372e07107a014","body":{"detail":"holds_surface(person) (holds_owner_topics() for the owner) is true while any stream of that person holds questions or inbox, and those topics stay subscribed while the tab is hidden (web/shell/src/stream.ts:23-27). crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create() uses it, for the asking agent's person, to decide whether a hook question waits in Clax or is released to the terminal at once. So a Clax tab left open in the background makes every AskUserQuestion of that person's agents wait in Clax until it is answered there, released, timed out, or Esc is pressed (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:289-302). Decision needed: should 'open' instead mean a tab seen or focused recently, or the extension's side panel being open?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1207},"end":{"line":1232},"content_hash":"ef0267ee57042e6f58c4b3ab575dbe015b81d840852637892266f23d038afb03"},"summary":"A hidden tab counts as an open Clax surface, so the AskUserQuestion hook waits in Clax","supersedes":"166165c60e8eaac9977db1ddc18cabb0452f82ce17fa50345babbbad831451fa","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:17.697613Z","id":"081b90b91ed55e207acff94667eb735d9438be2c975999ce2a4bf1525b1a2f37","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate of 166165c60e8eaac9977db1ddc18cabb0452f82ce17fa50345babbbad831451fa, the other head of the same record; that one is re-anchored to crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs:1207:1232.","supersedes":"36b65d11b1971000e3cdb0f20ae9e7040c808d93cc74786c1c3b91464e419fb4","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:17.705517Z","id":"1e224a8e2fc1d02cbb3b17b0185b4ed49cceb00283eda156a3d5fa9e0b2568d6","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate of 166165c60e8eaac9977db1ddc18cabb0452f82ce17fa50345babbbad831451fa, the other head of the same record; that one is re-anchored to crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs:1207:1232.","supersedes":"83c405b680c7ea4901d14b5542ccc92015b3bacc568f6cefe5f311979690247b","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:17.712365Z","id":"65bd574c262ad2e40a52fca3b6116b2c549980b96883ea910b38baab6764954d","body":{"detail":"With rmcp's local feature, serve_directly spawns with tokio::task::spawn_local, which could run inside a LocalSet polled by the Worker's event loop; rmcp's own timeouts would still need tokio's timer, which has no driver there. Not taken: it relies on tokio internals working without a runtime context. The adapter calls the tools' methods directly (they take no RequestContext; rmcp's Peer::new is pub(crate) in rmcp 3.5's service.rs).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":106},"end":{"line":118},"content_hash":"ae6c2ada9c1d603a2bdb8bf280c66640be7f8f807c57d0d117c50720e5142a1c"},"summary":"Drive rmcp's serve_directly on a tokio LocalSet inside the Worker instead of a JSON-RPC adapter","supersedes":"994422fe5a491ffacb022ee7de02fb59f5c2e088b8acdb610fd19f739f5bfe3f","tags":["wasm","revisit:rmcp offers a runtime-agnostic stateless handler","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:17.737839Z","id":"d65ac3c9757a5b0bc6bb7304c1bf87290ab4401273ed7b4718b0fade08175962","body":{"detail":"crate::seats::subscribe (called by POST /api/stream/<id>, crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs update) takes the artifact's seat for connection stream:<id> when the stream holds none of its live topics yet. If two calls add live topics of the same artifact at once and one then fails (TooMany, Hidden), its rollback leaves the seat the other call's topics rely on. The shell's hub sends one change at a time per stream, so this needs a hand-made client.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":384},"end":{"line":405},"content_hash":"d1bde61f01852bf26b409a8e492815bad85c59a044543e416aeee2aa7d62106e"},"summary":"Two concurrent subscription changes of one stream can leave it on an artifact's live topics without its seat","supersedes":"7ebee36b357f3d98637196f41bb5cc47b4bef1b886c015c83406ff7a34d041d7","tags":["live-seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:17.813075Z","id":"fe8efbba3ae85145f16752e47e4eeab671e583bc9ac2deef5b43a365e3a0347f","body":{"detail":"Every handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1021},"end":{"line":1021},"content_hash":"95e634966fc956bcf03f44fdf7131faa6bc9307f6e163a961719bf6f762fe602"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve Person/Viewer lazily in Agent<N> (only a person's agent needs the store), or fold the read into the handler's own store_call.","summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","supersedes":"196bd6512118a6f1fc57629c67ab742ca64b6d2fac21180afe3b36618c0738e4","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:17.825579Z","id":"fc95c069e1af985b8dd11bc093f3cee8cd6e8f8fe494b695f619d6d5ecc52882","body":{"detail":"Every handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1021},"end":{"line":1021},"content_hash":"95e634966fc956bcf03f44fdf7131faa6bc9307f6e163a961719bf6f762fe602"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve Person/Viewer lazily in Agent<N> (only a person's agent needs the store), or fold the read into the handler's own store_call.","summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","supersedes":"c2d26633facd8c19e2713a99febfc52b6920be586a00ed7f2dc694d30b70adbb","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:17.879801Z","id":"49dd098d72633ea6cc57eac751a80e47495fecb208b9f98e3add76573bfb43f9","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/approvals.rs person() now names an unnamed owner 'The owner' with author.owner true, but WithheldAuthor here still takes clax_core::feedback::display_name(\"\"), which is 'Viewer'. A person's agent reading the owner's artifact without an approval gets withheld.authors [{name: 'Viewer', public_id: <owner>}], indistinguishable from a person named Viewer (POST /api/people/invites {name: 'Viewer'} is accepted). crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs:793 builds the placeholder text from the same name.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1404},"end":{"line":1417},"content_hash":"0b622d8d52ac38e574fa84a9f714a893f935bb9c6f94ceaae66bedd96a89713b"},"suggested_fix":"Share one owner-aware naming helper between approvals.rs person() and the withheld authors (and the placeholder text).","summary":"A withheld field's authors still name an unnamed owner 'Viewer'","supersedes":"424c90c6e6637f18fc8a5ec97a4ecc708479be82d93628d9b7dff079b81d4a5c","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:17.895062Z","id":"529e8e6eb3f3421bc5e5d621bd2c689b2cdfb917995255003b39563dcb863a03","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate of 424c90c6e6637f18fc8a5ec97a4ecc708479be82d93628d9b7dff079b81d4a5c, the other head of the same record; that one is re-anchored to crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:1404:1417.","supersedes":"9954324acf6b480034776987b500687d84e54397e536aabc247b82d726bacd95","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:17.942476Z","id":"3e78b3784ac0f22563381c0f518f3933dd908a26a70af56c7e7c1e8999f64422","body":{"detail":"Withhold::approval runs Store::request_state once per thread that withholds anything, so a listing of N such threads makes N indexed reads (plus st.owner() when the owner is withheld). Versions and names are cached per call. vis_threads_ms (Task 25) will show whether it matters.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1429},"end":{"line":1456},"content_hash":"05c56d201c29c0092d6039e9c09166c4bdf07ea63e935e45f87326bf15b12593"},"summary":"Each thread with withheld content costs one approval_requests query in a listing","supersedes":"08a77c123acb2ba1176c0041fb5713a6435022ad3b93b2bf1a598b81901c9641","tags":["perf","visibility","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:17.958027Z","id":"ac0fed683b78ab3567c1bd70e32ccce5b6b37dd548619b43fdd5f2fee3b0c08e","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate of 08a77c123acb2ba1176c0041fb5713a6435022ad3b93b2bf1a598b81901c9641, the other head of the same record; that one is re-anchored to crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:1429:1456.","supersedes":"aa81386da3fbbf68a96b53beff991b50a08a006c93e290b2b5cc6888c15ddd11","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.022036Z","id":"843a59b4bea8bba0ab47ec232d6824ae4f3cf94e13f49c54b6089325bcfc7eb1","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1479},"end":{"line":1523},"content_hash":"ddf90a27cffb9eae9f415b9f193ba4f15b3c221446be555e0e4c03e03e2abb50"},"summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","supersedes":"e5630b5298781b0e651ec41353d08b673b45072704b7d5bda4d4ff05ac5a7a52","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.024939Z","id":"e4101508a783f53cd0a919d3f031a9d6fac901f0e6b61c99d25d764636b19ce9","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate of e5630b5298781b0e651ec41353d08b673b45072704b7d5bda4d4ff05ac5a7a52, the other head of the same record; that one is re-anchored to crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:1479:1523.","supersedes":"145c7c1c4fed00eab0f879cdbb41766628a3d8ae0f27906b6302afff57e42058","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.048189Z","id":"a93ab102251c3eba4b97832a2e0680ed653b495f5bca2907af7dbd64bd8c94e7","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate of 768648273e4265d6daa3cadb3ba327be03e252dda94381a1fa1e1aeb67e572ae, the other head of the same record; that one stays at crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs:481:488.","supersedes":"b9c7c0a32a04cf82a41d0204d2ac01e4154b336e761ace8dffe917365550a1bf","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.078840Z","id":"c76b1a73dcc62299940d392d94afef14366011d81297390ad376fe566e35e5a0","body":{"detail":"Limits holds its buckets in a Mutex<HashMap>; a restarted daemon forgets them, and a Cloudflare deployment with several isolates or Durable Objects would count per instance. Past MAX_CLIENTS (10000) clients the map is cleared.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":150},"end":{"line":153},"content_hash":"c3d9cee2df2daa7466bec6f2d7785f46a526e8ffaae9cfc54cec9c2e75b2fe50"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the buckets in the store (or one Durable Object) in the Worker build.","summary":"The abuse limits live in the process's memory: they reset on restart and are per instance","supersedes":"1123c32a59773e59d99faba4f021060318cd288aea97ffe7a9184972baa8f744","tags":["hosted","security","wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.081872Z","id":"7c0fa639b7afef99835773a10f352dd73d4f594bfb8605b552410154e40a6e69","body":{"detail":"The prototype let a commenter resolve or reopen threads they started (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design.md section 7). LinkAccess::rights (crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs) holds no comments resolve; checking a thread's creator in the gate would need a store read per request.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":898},"end":{"line":900},"content_hash":"f8564687d21d97fe5615a5674a21b9444ea4c648abef2584844c61b8e5250507"},"summary":"A guest may not resolve or reopen threads, even their own","supersedes":"ad52f1115f90250fca33988c43daf0d7004936e0a9c4a559f69114cfe0dc8ed9","tags":["revisit:guests ask to resolve their own threads","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.084827Z","id":"a733fb7947e0ea9d5c28f14d4fb497b62f36b0918e9ece49737913032c6d136d","body":{"detail":"member_gate drops `gallery` from such a person's subscriptions because gallery events (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs routes, project) carry every artifact's titles and thread summaries; their gallery refreshes on load only.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":743},"end":{"line":743},"content_hash":"cc7f883b42e8d834a7aa6a6e9f0ce461e48a8702065827af2cbdbbf741b80e96"},"suggested_fix":"Gate gallery items per subscriber by artifact (a read filter fixed at subscribe time) instead of dropping the topic.","summary":"A person whose rights do not read every artifact gets no gallery stream topic, so their gallery does not update live","supersedes":"f791bb502e5f532c598858ae8bd107731caabb1634456a0c8a2a30e559ea6875","tags":["hosted","ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.147173Z","id":"1059e72634ed9a3423124744b4e1bdd6b119b2f3c96ea7715db8c98e12fc7cf9","body":{"detail":"member_need checks the artifact only when the query names one; without it the routes answer every artifact this viewer has marks on (IDs and counts, no titles). Inbox items addressed to the person stay after their rights narrow.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":663},"end":{"line":667},"content_hash":"658bd678f5f2ca9606250a4a71b16315b8e871172a66044341faa0416f943b70"},"suggested_fix":"Filter those answers with Agent::read_rights as GET /api/artifacts does.","summary":"A person's /api/viewers/me/attention and /api/viewers/me/seen without ?artifact=, and their inbox items, are not filtered by their rights","supersedes":"73f34cb2ed924fa166cd9a2282eda80f55e48921fccb925e342b4cbdaa80dc9d","tags":["hosted","visibility","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.186586Z","id":"5701e6275ed5f060462a65c7d3183f5224d99463425bd758a92bd854eb7a1550","body":{"detail":"content_key is an HMAC of <aid>/<n> under the daemon token, as the prototype's commit hash (hosted/src/content.ts) never expired either. A person whose rights narrow, or a guest whose page stops being shared, still reads every version address they were handed (not later versions). A new daemon token changes every key.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":404},"end":{"line":406},"content_hash":"cd8d880448cdb31132019e34c90867877b5c99850f7b334415ffebc58c2ce63d"},"suggested_fix":"Mix a per-artifact generation into the key and bump it when the page stops being shared or a person's rights narrow.","summary":"A content key never expires: whoever saw a version's keyed address keeps reading it after losing the right","supersedes":"1453082772e2801382b7cec1de246790613ce9214644b3513a5668ba9e4db5f3","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.215116Z","id":"0e1fe424364639f0fd7d1771d53a30fed056e4fe2643c65bb1f476027b7820ed","body":{"detail":"PUT /api/viewers/me with no session makes a guest viewer row and a session whatever the site shares; Attempt::Guest limits it to five per client and then one per two minutes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1287},"end":{"line":1295},"content_hash":"7b0b50000594786778769269c90c8b6ed7c453ad2d601bcdc1a9e8dbea8ea63c"},"suggested_fix":"Require the page the visitor names (artifact_id in the body) to be shared for commenting.","summary":"A visitor may become a guest without any page being shared by link","supersedes":"44693a7a90e200798dab34cffdcff6aaa9dd5cc09d5dd6d41a4de32ef9c58c5a","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:19.073517Z","id":"51900b9697bf3dfc9d4cc279993a8506672a8f2f402b8e6c52d4042ac26cdcb0","body":{"detail":"A LAN viewer (the clax_viewer cookie) can create viewers, threads, comments, sends and db documents without limit. Decision needed: add rate limits for LAN writes, and at what rates.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":28},"end":{"line":29},"content_hash":"b1af0cd8867a4f59d11928f5b6bc91ec050b31c1c0962ba44425b10f430d2c0c"},"summary":"LAN viewers' writes have no rate limit","supersedes":"0bcf4f587cf928d2e3c178b4c665dd3ef96b626dc96bcdc039c83c93d78d459f","tags":["status:needs-decision","security","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:51.118097Z","id":"c40e19f2288778315ddb8f1eeb655c14d6a14c375ef3cf3920a18fe332ec7c4a","body":{"detail":"The gate could require /c/<aid>/draft/k/<content key of the base version>/<agent>/<token>/…, so a draft URL is also bound to a key the daemon derives. Not taken: the draft token is already 128 random bits minted per revision (clax_core::drafts::new_token), handed only to people who may read the artifact, and it expires with the revision, which a content key never does; a second key adds a path segment the shell's draftSrc (web/shell/src/view/draft-model.ts) and the artifact host rewrite (crates/clax-server/src/host.rs) would carry for no capability the token lacks.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":482},"end":{"line":487},"content_hash":"1eb3ba02e9270a952f8677687cf948c44e4be183b4f1fcf9567e9067d50f00f4"},"summary":"Draft URLs keyed by the version's content key as well as the draft token","tags":["hosted","drafts","revisit:a draft token is logged, persisted or handed to anyone who may not read the artifact","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:17:08.819204Z","id":"63b6e60d8bab111d6bbec4a5424b5a787cce7c6ba8e24d11975521842b4e9ff2","body":{"detail":"conn_of is None on wasm32 (no request in a Worker has the owner machine's trust), so api_host_allowed has no local address to compare and admits only is_local_host names. Under wrangler dev the browser and e2e (crates/clax-worker/e2e.mjs) reach http://localhost:<port>, which passes; a deployed instance on its own hostname gets forbidden_host on every /api path, and the shell's /a/ bootstrap is served bare (shell::artifact_page checks request_host_allowed). Hosted mode needs the instance's public host (crates/clax-worker/wrangler.jsonc PUBLIC_ORIGIN, or the rust-hosted-signin branch's configuration) to count as an API host, keeping DNS-rebinding protection for every other name.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":380},"end":{"line":400},"content_hash":"6f4e75568821b760e0b95ed5d39418eb537bd8983168c20479afb039e11d0a8e"},"summary":"On wasm32 /api answers only Host names localhost, 127.0.0.1 and [::1], so a deployed Worker refuses every API request 403 forbidden_host","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:17:08.819290Z","id":"8304b25148ff5397b6bfce372e953a0d35735c6077c74738c426efc3bd92da64","body":{"detail":"artifact_host accepts <12-char ID>.localhost[:port] alone. Under wrangler dev --local browsers resolve *.localhost to the machine, so crates/clax-worker/e2e.mjs sees the frame at http://<id>.localhost:<port>/v/1/ exactly as on the daemon. A deployed Worker needs a content domain of its own (a wildcard like <id>.content.example), as the TypeScript prototype's CONTENT_ORIGIN and PUBLIC_ORIGIN do (hosted/wrangler.jsonc, hosted/src/index.ts), in artifact_host, boot::frame_origin and the shell's origin check (web/shell/src/origin.ts).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":12},"end":{"line":25},"content_hash":"e76ac4cf4a6c8d2778e4441b2d8b516a96e4b7c82616a50483460ee2d6f4e9a4"},"summary":"Artifact content origins are only <id>.localhost, so a deployed Worker has no content origin and every frame falls back to the sandboxed path","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:17:33.964028Z","id":"e111f87d4f17582fc2679695c4d4fe44a3c70d6c9f14befebabeaade2ed6f6c9","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"a65317782e56e23b8b5f53b3da1515f9f3c9292e6a78a905b9d4779180ab42a1","summary":"Addressed on rust-worker-host (1aac7b97, 81645e13): Hub::on_queue calls a listener after any change that queued frames, outside the hub's lock (dispatch, unseat); crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs wakes a spawn_local drain task from it, so frames dispatched by spawned listeners go out at once, not at the next request. Only sockets whose Conn::pending is set are drained (an atomic load per socket, no queue work for the others). Evidence: stream::tests::a_drained_connection_takes_its_frames_without_waiting_and_ends_with_its_stream; node crates/clax-worker/e2e.mjs prints 'ok   the comment reaches the second browser live, over its WebSocket'. A dirty set of stream IDs would make the per-dispatch scan O(changed) instead of O(sockets) atomic loads; proposed close.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:17:33.964121Z","id":"948e1a376a509441d86a73b9f30e635adaa39e37019ed233e693bd871b455682","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"a5637e4e199a0ed4161facb7054d02f3752e2e189f2aa3593d5eabb1bad8bc4e","summary":"Taken on rust-worker-host (81645e13) as the record suggests: after a wake each kept socket gets a new stream (routes::stream::open_stream) with a new ID, written back with serializeAttachment, and its own ready (resumed false), so the shell's hub clears what it thought the stream carried, subscribes again over POST /api/stream/<id> with every admission rule, and refetches. The caller is resolved from the store again from identity::SocketCredentials (the viewer cookie's ULID and whether the token was presented, never the token), so a revoked person or a renamed viewer is seen. The attachment is the socket key, the stream ID and those credentials, well under 2,048 bytes; topics are not carried, as the new stream starts with none. Conn::drain does what Conn::next's poll did (clear_lag after resync, end on a newer connection or a lapsed credential check); a closed socket drops its Conn, which detaches. Not reproduced: a stream's extension credential (no extension pairs with a Worker: extension_id is empty) and local (always false there). Evidence: node crates/clax-worker/e2e.mjs, after POST /_worker/hibernate rebuilds the server on the same storage: 'ok   the woken server opens the kept socket a new stream, on the same socket' and 'ok   a comment after the rebuild still arrives live'. Proposed close.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:17:33.964188Z","id":"0fd170ef931faf11adbc5b2060399f3e7d10212c0c3cd3e03d640283183751f2","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"102650cd60e01c897d55cdfc3380a88762416c002b190b4f9694d316970b2cde","summary":"Unchanged by rust-worker-host: after a wake each socket's new stream is subscribed again by its shell in whatever order the shells ask, so seat order and idle clocks restart and presence is empty until tabs report. Presence PUTs still wake the object; and the alarm wakes it every 5 s while a socket is open (recorded on crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs alarm).","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:17:33.964246Z","id":"0e871836dbf79ab0000b1851667cb7103aabe123f01f35a20d01ce8425cebbea","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"61069320e3db13e3a93b448432143e6b1f1c6e29873f3667b2786566b2bc487d","summary":"Still open after rust-worker-host: the Worker serves no room socket (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}/room stays native only in routes/mod.rs), so a page using the room capability on a Worker gets a 404 there. The outlet pieces it needs are not built: a per-socket drain of the room's broadcast::Receiver beside Conn::drain, and rebuilding memberships from attachments on wake.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:17:33.964309Z","id":"3e057c25c1e40695d33d20f8b38dad7853bd5f9abd161abc1525b6d2b5b87975","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"dfae291e43fb5c268c73de5ed416822113cdac0f4092efad9c95aae342995d7e","summary":"Still open after rust-worker-host: crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs gives AppState questions::TokioSleeper (setTimeout on wasm32), so the grace still keeps the object awake and is lost at eviction; the alarm runs only AppState::sweep, grant expiry and the planner refresh.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:17:41.584847Z","id":"53d3708cad320347c9fbdc6bc57de0733651df3c726d5bca7a42778fc12da6de","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1b4ec4c","summary":"Fixed in f1b4ec4c: on wasm32 auth::conn_of returns None whatever a request's extensions hold, so no request in a Worker gets loopback or LAN trust. Evidence: scripts/check-wasm.sh passes; node crates/clax-worker/e2e.mjs prints 'ok   GET /api/token serves no one' (403 from the Durable Object under wrangler dev --local).","supersedes":"1528f694e37a1dea06b91a2864832b6e3f8b9c518a3081fcca987f9f886c0cab","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:17:41.663035Z","id":"2c41fac6c7073105b45d1641de415d5b8b36ad1b5611b3ce082e9636701d6ef7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e98778ac","summary":"Fixed in e98778ac: AppState::assemble(StateParts) builds the state, start_listeners starts the hub, seats, inbox, approvals and people listeners, and sweep runs the in-memory sweeps; daemon.rs and crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs (81645e13) both use them. Evidence: cargo nextest run -p clax-server -p clax-core: 1680 of 1681 passed, the one failure api_canary passing alone once plugins/pi had its node_modules (13 passed); node crates/clax-worker/e2e.mjs passes.","supersedes":"06246bd54686f5f6ec3a9155e7cb96c65c2b3151226cd4f563d783fcf0b7e950","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:18:39.889006Z","id":"334b6c7c98d0ff850b744bbc23921ad085228092b82a5fe64ead5e8e17d027f1","body":{"detail":"Identity::caller makes the token an OwnerAgent whenever a session is named (path or X-Clax-Session), known or not; audit_actor records an agent only for a known session of the token's, the agent marker, or x-clax-via mcp, else the owner. Measured through GET /api/_test/audit/ctx: Authorization Bearer + X-Clax-Session 01JB9S00000000000000000099 (no session) and X-Clax-Session not-a-ulid both give {\"type\":\"owner\"}. Today's clients send the marker, so this bites only an older or third-party agent side; it breaks audit spec section 5.2's rule that one request is never an agent to Caller and the owner to the journal.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":503},"end":{"line":510},"content_hash":"75fc91286c48244768b0a0e9a1d2af39937a039081897bf71644933e706cbb12"},"suggested_fix":"When the token names any session that is not known, record the sessionless agent (channel as named, else mcp) instead of the owner; add the case to the_agent_channel_marker_makes_the_token_an_agent.","summary":"The token naming an unknown or non-ULID session without the agent marker is recorded as the owner, while Caller counts it as OwnerAgent","supersedes":"b9c7c0a32a04cf82a41d0204d2ac01e4154b336e761ace8dffe917365550a1bf","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:18:39.897181Z","id":"46a7bb0f76a24ff52bd22d0102218bd12bf72cb97aef90e7a80d949b9ef22647","body":{"detail":"Hub::detach parks the stream's seats when its Conn is dropped, which happens when hyper sees the connection close (immediate for a closed tab or context in the tests: crates/clax-server/tests/api_seats.rs load_150_people_on_100_seats, web/e2e/seats.spec.ts). A connection that hangs without closing holds the seat until the next keep-alive write fails, or until the idle release (3 minutes without a here presence report).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1185},"end":{"line":1189},"content_hash":"7b970f113a2cab27cc4b859d11385b56033f15cf3a164b9e2cd759395dba038c"},"summary":"A closed browser's seat frees only once the daemon notices its stream's connection dropped","supersedes":"87a97144d0f52632a3922b0b25f75c0bb8a819534306d4a142d54d01024b4fed","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:18:39.899182Z","id":"2b69aca3dfe727b1a12aeb35e4d478959f8477474fd1d9e0b174e0283a75d20e","body":{"detail":"holds_surface(person) (holds_owner_topics() for the owner) is true while any stream of that person holds questions or inbox, and those topics stay subscribed while the tab is hidden (web/shell/src/stream.ts:23-27). crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create() uses it, for the asking agent's person, to decide whether a hook question waits in Clax or is released to the terminal at once. So a Clax tab left open in the background makes every AskUserQuestion of that person's agents wait in Clax until it is answered there, released, timed out, or Esc is pressed (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:289-302). Decision needed: should 'open' instead mean a tab seen or focused recently, or the extension's side panel being open?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1093},"end":{"line":1118},"content_hash":"a2b02b2b71f4a27bc5f328e4623e7558f286e20e1f5a94df181084462cd4d9f5"},"summary":"A hidden tab counts as an open Clax surface, so the AskUserQuestion hook waits in Clax","supersedes":"83c405b680c7ea4901d14b5542ccc92015b3bacc568f6cefe5f311979690247b","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:51:57.372183Z","id":"9469923eed51d08c70a4ad47f754c9d489033b35216898790837ac33bf648b7e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"102650cd60e01c897d55cdfc3380a88762416c002b190b4f9694d316970b2cde","summary":"The alarm no longer wakes the object every 5 s (874a9e5b): it is set for the first presence report, seat, detached stream, working record or grant that lapses, and none is set with nothing due. Seats and presence are still lost at a wake, as this record says.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:51:57.372293Z","id":"25108bea62c04fd1a6b82f0d33baa3ea54c6b1db345fbb6b66c08f61cb508c49","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"a5637e4e199a0ed4161facb7054d02f3752e2e189f2aa3593d5eabb1bad8bc4e","summary":"Since 7f722d29 SocketCredentials keeps a 16-hex-digit SHA-256 tag of the token presented instead of a bool, and identity() presents the token again only when the tag is the current token's: after a token change a woken socket reopens as no owner (identity::tests::socket_credentials_keep_no_token_and_reopen_with_no_more_than_they_had). Since f3e3459c the upgrade is refused 403 forbidden_origin unless Origin is the request's own non-artifact host.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/viewer.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:51:57.372476Z","id":"f6feaeeb0a961309ba4a544ae21622cdf0183fd56acad294b7370bd97878d215","body":{"detail":"The stream's WebSocket check (routes::stream::socket_origin_allowed) accepts http:// and https:// with the request's own Host; the viewer routes' SameOrigin does not. Not hit under wrangler dev (http); a deploy is also refused by the API's host rule (record 63b6e60d).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":76},"end":{"line":85},"content_hash":"793b9c3d198dd81e3b8f5593e1b8cd467fe6dcbe79fbe81eefb86575ffbb6244"},"summary":"SameOrigin admits only http:// origins, so on a Worker served over https every viewer route from the shell is 403 forbidden_origin","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:52:45.704363Z","id":"02805c8d6f3e2f453dde4095289d08247904fa15ca657de6fcfd1c02ba2106c3","body":{"detail":"Identity::caller makes the token an OwnerAgent whenever a session is named (path or X-Clax-Session), known or not; audit_actor records an agent only for a known session of the token's, the agent marker, or x-clax-via mcp, else the owner. Measured through GET /api/_test/audit/ctx: Authorization Bearer + X-Clax-Session 01JB9S00000000000000000099 (no session) and X-Clax-Session not-a-ulid both give {\"type\":\"owner\"}. Today's clients send the marker, so this bites only an older or third-party agent side; it breaks audit spec section 5.2's rule that one request is never an agent to Caller and the owner to the journal.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":518},"end":{"line":525},"content_hash":"75fc91286c48244768b0a0e9a1d2af39937a039081897bf71644933e706cbb12"},"suggested_fix":"When the token names any session that is not known, record the sessionless agent (channel as named, else mcp) instead of the owner; add the case to the_agent_channel_marker_makes_the_token_an_agent.","summary":"The token naming an unknown or non-ULID session without the agent marker is recorded as the owner, while Caller counts it as OwnerAgent","supersedes":"334b6c7c98d0ff850b744bbc23921ad085228092b82a5fe64ead5e8e17d027f1","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:52:45.716047Z","id":"ae6c12d304e92bb682a6063c40c186d2817c04ffab731da9d146ff558950ded0","body":{"detail":"The native daemon has no per-artifact live socket like the hosted prototype's /api/artifacts/:id/live (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts fetch); the shell's one shared stream subscribing an artifact's artifact, presence or working topic holds the seat (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs use_seats, crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs update). A live relay of pointers, selections and typing on another connection asks LiveSeats::is_seated, or holds a seat itself with LiveSeats::take and leave under its own connection key and hears idle releases through LiveSeats::on_idle; nothing natively takes an agent seat yet, as agents hold no live connection here.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":198},"end":{"line":203},"content_hash":"32ceb5fbc1090c840186b68a86c8d81947c5c3f81c3c2528455f8ab93d97ec23"},"summary":"Seats are held by /api/stream subscriptions, not by a live socket of their own","supersedes":"d3825226cf112efcfc36a387d51f80b930bda0962b48c1247c80c7cb9e805e01","tags":["revisit:a live relay socket lands beside /api/stream","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:52:45.718228Z","id":"834eb422277d8e55ca28156bd09616e8ddd40b144102651cc8193ba901e292f9","body":{"detail":"crate::seats::subscribe (called by POST /api/stream/<id>, crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs update) takes the artifact's seat for connection stream:<id> when the stream holds none of its live topics yet. If two calls add live topics of the same artifact at once and one then fails (TooMany, Hidden), its rollback leaves the seat the other call's topics rely on. The shell's hub sends one change at a time per stream, so this needs a hand-made client.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":391},"end":{"line":412},"content_hash":"d1bde61f01852bf26b409a8e492815bad85c59a044543e416aeee2aa7d62106e"},"summary":"Two concurrent subscription changes of one stream can leave it on an artifact's live topics without its seat","supersedes":"7ebee36b357f3d98637196f41bb5cc47b4bef1b886c015c83406ff7a34d041d7","tags":["live-seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:52:53.236516Z","id":"67dfbb93787504727ff8b76c3d0e25e464b1478409ca97be0fe6a8f52aa82659","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"9469923eed51d08c70a4ad47f754c9d489033b35216898790837ac33bf648b7e","summary":"The alarm commit is a03f663c; 874a9e5b named above is not on the branch.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:06:00.599724Z","id":"9b82c3b52fcabf760c0d5dba8af60074057ab1368158a9746d39e0ff4ffba249","body":{"detail":"With rmcp's local feature, serve_directly spawns with tokio::task::spawn_local, which could run inside a LocalSet polled by the Worker's event loop; rmcp's own timeouts would still need tokio's timer, which has no driver there. Not taken: it relies on tokio internals working without a runtime context. The adapter calls the tools' methods directly (they take no RequestContext; rmcp's Peer::new is pub(crate) in rmcp 3.5's service.rs).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":105},"end":{"line":120},"content_hash":"67ec541010bad6b266922dfa88431aa7b67a7638afae8ff33659215395dca1f4"},"summary":"Drive rmcp's serve_directly on a tokio LocalSet inside the Worker instead of a JSON-RPC adapter","supersedes":"994422fe5a491ffacb022ee7de02fb59f5c2e088b8acdb610fd19f739f5bfe3f","tags":["wasm","revisit:rmcp offers a runtime-agnostic stateless handler","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/loopback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:06:55.453764Z","id":"2fa307e31a09490b4d18e32a5f05302541708b7af2ada9dd54eb379706e050f5","body":{"detail":"Loopback gives every request a Conn from 127.0.0.1:0 to the address self_base names (127.0.0.1:0 when it names a host, not an address), and attempt_in_process in crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs sets Host from self_base. auth::require_api_host admits localhost, 127.0.0.1, [::1] or the connection's own address, so a Worker whose AppState::self_base is its public origin (https://clax.dev) would have every tool call refused 403 forbidden_host. The Worker crate, which builds AppState, should set self_base to http://localhost (browser_base carries the public origin), or the Conn should be what the object puts on its own requests.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":26},"end":{"line":42},"content_hash":"d58b6c1ed28101106e88610c957f86bd1b97e5c4adb49a0c8b6776f92e735ef2"},"summary":"In-process requests arrive as loopback to self_base, so on a Durable Object self_base must be a host the /api check admits","tags":["worker","mcp","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/loopback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:06:55.454711Z","id":"c922719e89602722894e7e0b77e869f9f77495af7e6c9268d9dd651c1228b9e6","body":{"detail":"axum::body::to_bytes(body, usize::MAX): a read of a large version file or asset holds it in memory twice (the router's body and the tool's copy) before the read tool's own max_bytes cut. The HTTP path of the local daemon is uncapped too; the remote path caps at clax_core::remote::MAX_RESPONSE_BYTES. In a Durable Object's 128 MB isolate this is the bound that matters.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":44},"end":{"line":74},"content_hash":"b46825ef617c45c0915174f75b878f0ef240dc4bf96f487ebcf8149497d412c6"},"summary":"An in-process response is read whole with no cap","tags":["worker","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/loopback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:38:15.944011Z","id":"d834408a1caca922ef0ff4c00e12602bab9c6be2eac61dec70f980509ccaf5b2","body":{"detail":"Fixed in git:74708bc9: Loopback::call sets Host to loopback::HOST (localhost), which auth::api_host_allowed admits without a connection (asserted in Loopback::new), and inserts no Conn on either target. Evidence: `cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_mcp_http::an_in_process_request_has_only_its_callers_rights` (self_base set to https://clax.example; GET /api/artifacts with the token answers 200) -> test result: ok. 1 passed.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:74708bc9","summary":"In-process requests carry Host: localhost and no connection, admitted whatever self_base names; checked when the Loopback is made","supersedes":"2fa307e31a09490b4d18e32a5f05302541708b7af2ada9dd54eb379706e050f5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/loopback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:38:15.950769Z","id":"4f4cfef24c9b73ea50d8654a3fcf16223495aa299190687a387ce2a300c508df","body":{"detail":"Fixed in git:74708bc9: axum::body::to_bytes(body, limit) with loopback::RESPONSE_LIMIT, settable with Loopback::with_response_limit. Evidence: `cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_mcp_http::an_in_process_response_is_capped` (a 64-byte limit answers 502 response_too_large; the default answers 200) -> test result: ok. 1 passed.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:74708bc9","summary":"An in-process response is read up to RESPONSE_LIMIT (32 MiB), else 502 response_too_large","supersedes":"c922719e89602722894e7e0b77e869f9f77495af7e6c9268d9dd651c1228b9e6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/loopback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:38:15.952768Z","id":"6d815ec5c0d0b52448c79b4eebe15d30c8cc49df365af0773e00b63b0bfe811a","body":{"detail":"The read tool fetches a whole version file (client.rs file_bytes) before cutting it at max_bytes. In-process that answer stops at RESPONSE_LIMIT (32 MiB) and becomes 502 response_too_large; rmcp's /mcp tools go over HTTP, uncapped, so a native publish of a larger file (PUBLISH_BODY_LIMIT is 96 MiB) reads there and not at /mcp/json. Hosted files are at most 10 MiB, so a Durable Object is not affected. A ranged read of the first max_bytes would remove the gap.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":27},"end":{"line":30},"content_hash":"df66880f5cd833efff28682dab9f5aba2fdba32a5f21728083cbad31918a0058"},"summary":"A native version file over 32 MiB cannot be read through the adapter's tools, though /mcp's can","tags":["mcp","parity","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:46:07.725895Z","id":"1f8be26236b43f3d282bb2f9abecfb0ee025a5c4bc6a285a78d7f447ec129aeb","body":{"detail":"Identity::caller makes the token an OwnerAgent whenever a session is named (path or X-Clax-Session), known or not; audit_actor records an agent only for a known session of the token's, the agent marker, or x-clax-via mcp, else the owner. Measured through GET /api/_test/audit/ctx: Authorization Bearer + X-Clax-Session 01JB9S00000000000000000099 (no session) and X-Clax-Session not-a-ulid both give {\"type\":\"owner\"}. Today's clients send the marker, so this bites only an older or third-party agent side; it breaks audit spec section 5.2's rule that one request is never an agent to Caller and the owner to the journal.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":538},"end":{"line":545},"content_hash":"75fc91286c48244768b0a0e9a1d2af39937a039081897bf71644933e706cbb12"},"suggested_fix":"When the token names any session that is not known, record the sessionless agent (channel as named, else mcp) instead of the owner; add the case to the_agent_channel_marker_makes_the_token_an_agent.","summary":"The token naming an unknown or non-ULID session without the agent marker is recorded as the owner, while Caller counts it as OwnerAgent","supersedes":"768648273e4265d6daa3cadb3ba327be03e252dda94381a1fa1e1aeb67e572ae","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:46:07.748958Z","id":"f6ea243dddd50fc9aa0b735b0be246b54d70a7861d8c4a79f93b9372bb0c3ac1","body":{"detail":"The native daemon has no per-artifact live socket like the hosted prototype's /api/artifacts/:id/live (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts fetch); the shell's one shared stream subscribing an artifact's artifact, presence or working topic holds the seat (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs use_seats, crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs update). A live relay of pointers, selections and typing on another connection asks LiveSeats::is_seated, or holds a seat itself with LiveSeats::take and leave under its own connection key and hears idle releases through LiveSeats::on_idle; nothing natively takes an agent seat yet, as agents hold no live connection here.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":199},"end":{"line":204},"content_hash":"32ceb5fbc1090c840186b68a86c8d81947c5c3f81c3c2528455f8ab93d97ec23"},"summary":"Seats are held by /api/stream subscriptions, not by a live socket of their own","supersedes":"94df2fd69a858c26cc56b8247a49fe136f8b95d8350e933a74b58fc9b1e2c492","tags":["revisit:a live relay socket lands beside /api/stream","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:46:07.752785Z","id":"029eb17a4338924cc93d8994a917dec7cef9e2d3579d8338c61e187c0aafd566","body":{"detail":"crate::seats::subscribe (called by POST /api/stream/<id>, crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs update) takes the artifact's seat for connection stream:<id> when the stream holds none of its live topics yet. If two calls add live topics of the same artifact at once and one then fails (TooMany, Hidden), its rollback leaves the seat the other call's topics rely on. The shell's hub sends one change at a time per stream, so this needs a hand-made client.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":392},"end":{"line":413},"content_hash":"d1bde61f01852bf26b409a8e492815bad85c59a044543e416aeee2aa7d62106e"},"summary":"Two concurrent subscription changes of one stream can leave it on an artifact's live topics without its seat","supersedes":"d65ac3c9757a5b0bc6bb7304c1bf87290ab4401273ed7b4718b0fade08175962","tags":["live-seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:46:07.756699Z","id":"a544830103a4ebcfe7cbda812c747f3bdd4964cee95a59f9c9781a07e4231754","body":{"detail":"Hub::detach parks the stream's seats when its Conn is dropped, which happens when hyper sees the connection close (immediate for a closed tab or context in the tests: crates/clax-server/tests/api_seats.rs load_150_people_on_100_seats, web/e2e/seats.spec.ts). A connection that hangs without closing holds the seat until the next keep-alive write fails, or until the idle release (3 minutes without a here presence report).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1230},"end":{"line":1234},"content_hash":"7b970f113a2cab27cc4b859d11385b56033f15cf3a164b9e2cd759395dba038c"},"summary":"A closed browser's seat frees only once the daemon notices its stream's connection dropped","supersedes":"403a40ef7c6e5bf3bbbc1621b5884f75da9560d42fe1ad34d8d833eb36a322eb","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:46:07.760621Z","id":"9fa483ae149b813d992787142e1cfa53fd6cdac6b4bbe1e0f12636b4e1a3eac6","body":{"detail":"holds_surface(person) (holds_owner_topics() for the owner) is true while any stream of that person holds questions or inbox, and those topics stay subscribed while the tab is hidden (web/shell/src/stream.ts:23-27). crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create() uses it, for the asking agent's person, to decide whether a hook question waits in Clax or is released to the terminal at once. So a Clax tab left open in the background makes every AskUserQuestion of that person's agents wait in Clax until it is answered there, released, timed out, or Esc is pressed (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:289-302). Decision needed: should 'open' instead mean a tab seen or focused recently, or the extension's side panel being open?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1273},"end":{"line":1298},"content_hash":"ef0267ee57042e6f58c4b3ab575dbe015b81d840852637892266f23d038afb03"},"summary":"A hidden tab counts as an open Clax surface, so the AskUserQuestion hook waits in Clax","supersedes":"f572abaacd082ae49f1f4af7996bed17c37d110fdb47fe3fd7f372e07107a014","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:16:47.745138Z","id":"d60ce43133c7db2ad3ee5a1728a230c0b35fe605f6b31d34049a0927fe0d93a3","body":{"detail":"hosted/src/git/tokens.ts refused write tokens to anyone but the owner (403 owner_only) because there every pushed commit was credited to the owner. Here a push is recorded as a version published by the token's holder (clax_core::store::pushes, Store::standing rechecks the pusher's update right at record time), so pushing is publishing and the route asks for the same right a publish does: under clax:collaborator that is the person's own artifacts, under clax:full every artifact. The alternative is owner and owner's agents only (Caller::Owner / OwnerAgent), refusing every person's write token.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":20},"end":{"line":24},"content_hash":"792b8370120f2208d45982dbd147ea71c46773f73ddc25d1a98b5166c9499f7a"},"summary":"A write token needs clax-artifacts update (the publish right), not the prototype's owner-only push","tags":["status:needs-decision","revisit:a person with update rights should not be able to push","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:16:47.745426Z","id":"65d931f9200de9ef01bebc5bff5358550f0cc47a40aa06fb7aa4c8af72f21534","body":{"detail":"ContentStore::fork (crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs) gives a fork's repository the original's history behind its version 1, but withheld_history walks Store::list_versions of the fork alone, so an agent's read token on a fork would clone the original's commits whatever their authors. Nothing calls fork yet; when the store does, the check must include the original's versions (or refuse, as hosted/src/git/tokens.ts did with complete: false).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":334},"end":{"line":354},"content_hash":"487a756228b8eb81b672445996ed88c3781dfe38dcd2ef20f48b97042479b062"},"summary":"The history check reads only this artifact's recorded versions: a forked repository's inherited commits are not checked","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:16:47.745588Z","id":"2b64693a08860532629120465e795529c26a75184fd47b4272773476eb836796","body":{"detail":"The store revokes blind agents' tokens before recording a pushed commit (clax_core::store::pushes::revoke_blind_tokens), but a publish through the API commits first and listen's recheck revokes on the Version event, so for that window (a recheck's round trip to RepoDO) a blind token can fetch the new commit. The hosted spec (§9 Tokens) has the publish revoke before its commit and refuse with repo_unavailable when the revoke fails. The recheck is also one RepoDO listing plus a history walk per held token on every relevant event, which is fine for a handful of tokens and not for many.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":768},"end":{"line":800},"content_hash":"5e754a16b4202079eae8a823d4d795588061b652276aa850fe8dcbcfdb8bbd09"},"summary":"A published version an agent's person may not see revokes that agent's token only after the version lands, not before its commit","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:16:47.745721Z","id":"47b67b0e4f476d272715b4064b681c248ba135702e5738a5764298572daad248","body":{"detail":"revoke_session_soon runs from feedback::sessions_stop, which is synchronous on the store's thread, so it spawns the RepoDO call. test-repos.mjs ('an ended session's token clones nothing') sees it revoked under wrangler dev; nothing guarantees the task runs if the object is evicted first. listen's recheck on the Agents event covers the next wake, and AGENT_TTL_S bounds the rest.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":715},"end":{"line":725},"content_hash":"f6fc1d493add33c70214ecaca1d9c7da22e8ab2addd3b84d9b47409b861fd4cc"},"summary":"An ended session's tokens are revoked from a spawned task: on the Worker a Durable Object evicted before it runs leaves them live until the recheck or their 15 minutes","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:25.956067Z","id":"99a042ac45d79e62841b6c39d0b895df49f43c7263ef17617110cef518c5c105","body":{"detail":"api_agent_auth::the_extractor_refuses_a_persons_agent_on_an_owner_agents_route now asserts that every Filtered need in ROUTES is live. The not_yet branches (agent.rs Agent<N> extraction and the body gate) stay for a Filtered route added later; remove them, with FILTERED_LIVE, once no task plans one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":526},"end":{"line":526},"content_hash":"e07bad372e55913af9df7b2c800d2741a700fd885fb02cc043d3e30bf32f99fd"},"summary":"Every Filtered need is now in FILTERED_LIVE, so the 503 not_yet path serves no route","supersedes":"a0367be36216f8709f164acb2554bbca8f8a5a65a37630d6675a44f48fa2d932","tags":["people","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:25.960260Z","id":"854f3a34f17d9849db749f583141d7773d453d0bcb551c989be4487d649e2bbf","body":{"detail":"Every handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1028},"end":{"line":1028},"content_hash":"95e634966fc956bcf03f44fdf7131faa6bc9307f6e163a961719bf6f762fe602"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve Person/Viewer lazily in Agent<N> (only a person's agent needs the store), or fold the read into the handler's own store_call.","summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","supersedes":"fe8efbba3ae85145f16752e47e4eeab671e583bc9ac2deef5b43a365e3a0347f","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:25.964384Z","id":"b89764e25b62b35248d219d5b75a544545758bbc4ac7bf7785fd7664e41be66e","body":{"detail":"Every handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1028},"end":{"line":1028},"content_hash":"95e634966fc956bcf03f44fdf7131faa6bc9307f6e163a961719bf6f762fe602"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve Person/Viewer lazily in Agent<N> (only a person's agent needs the store), or fold the read into the handler's own store_call.","summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","supersedes":"fc95c069e1af985b8dd11bc093f3cee8cd6e8f8fe494b695f619d6d5ecc52882","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:25.968559Z","id":"55570b4b94efbe5ea245e2316b975dfa632f69f6f6e5c35b28d93ec73c5d0e1d","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/approvals.rs person() now names an unnamed owner 'The owner' with author.owner true, but WithheldAuthor here still takes clax_core::feedback::display_name(\"\"), which is 'Viewer'. A person's agent reading the owner's artifact without an approval gets withheld.authors [{name: 'Viewer', public_id: <owner>}], indistinguishable from a person named Viewer (POST /api/people/invites {name: 'Viewer'} is accepted). crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs:793 builds the placeholder text from the same name.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1408},"end":{"line":1421},"content_hash":"0b622d8d52ac38e574fa84a9f714a893f935bb9c6f94ceaae66bedd96a89713b"},"suggested_fix":"Share one owner-aware naming helper between approvals.rs person() and the withheld authors (and the placeholder text).","summary":"A withheld field's authors still name an unnamed owner 'Viewer'","supersedes":"49dd098d72633ea6cc57eac751a80e47495fecb208b9f98e3add76573bfb43f9","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:25.972926Z","id":"93c1e71be55982a6aa270fb74e40a4a84bfb703fde1720b9c4be019f2f596f1d","body":{"detail":"Withhold::approval runs Store::request_state once per thread that withholds anything, so a listing of N such threads makes N indexed reads (plus st.owner() when the owner is withheld). Versions and names are cached per call. vis_threads_ms (Task 25) will show whether it matters.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1433},"end":{"line":1460},"content_hash":"05c56d201c29c0092d6039e9c09166c4bdf07ea63e935e45f87326bf15b12593"},"summary":"Each thread with withheld content costs one approval_requests query in a listing","supersedes":"3e78b3784ac0f22563381c0f518f3933dd908a26a70af56c7e7c1e8999f64422","tags":["perf","visibility","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:25.977148Z","id":"981ce89e0658234682dbd77838540caa48de81af5dfb02e113d5e827094131f6","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1483},"end":{"line":1527},"content_hash":"ddf90a27cffb9eae9f415b9f193ba4f15b3c221446be555e0e4c03e03e2abb50"},"summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","supersedes":"843a59b4bea8bba0ab47ec232d6824ae4f3cf94e13f49c54b6089325bcfc7eb1","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:25.981367Z","id":"747df39e076a2b34ffbcee4d43d557212f3db7bed26f8ddd2abcedf4c228b910","body":{"detail":"The host is chosen by cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\") alone, with native-only dependencies under target tables, so `scripts/check-wasm.sh -p clax-server` needs no flags and a native build cannot select Worker code by mistake. A `native` default feature plus a `worker` feature would let a native build compile the Worker paths (for instance to test the Durable Object glue natively) at the cost of a second axis to keep consistent.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":3},"end":{"line":12},"content_hash":"af187b6abf3de351adebdddf2a7a44787a8851256c7a2b3b1ef00d11f4e0dbef"},"summary":"A `worker` cargo feature to pick the host, beside the target","supersedes":"f6296fb72cf1a973606e71b99878501a3f59985239091066bebfc91cc6a273e9","tags":["wasm","revisit:the Worker glue needs native tests","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:25.985546Z","id":"e8713431f830a9106ae44be9ae18fc81b075da3aac87785866abb5e19104188b","body":{"detail":"Hub::dispatch also runs from tasks spawned off the request path: inbox::listen and approvals::listen consume store change notifications in clax_rt::spawn tasks (crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs:349-392, crates/clax-server/src/approvals.rs:193-200), questions::start_grace closes a question after its grace (crates/clax-server/src/questions.rs:296), flight::drive streams a sample, and agent::verify_layer notes a grant's use (crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs:1620). Their frames reach the queues after that request's drain ran and sit there until the next request, socket message or alarm, which on a quiet artifact can be minutes. Draining every socket after every message also costs O(open sockets) per incoming message; at the rates of docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design.md §16.5 (30 senders at 10 a second, 100 seats) that is most of the object's work.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":87},"end":{"line":97},"content_hash":"bd4c73af62822f0512f511921d10c9927a60727230fef892622d28f960a2b8c4"},"suggested_fix":"Have Hub::dispatch mark the subscribers it queued for as dirty and wake one outlet task (a tokio::sync::Notify that a spawn_local'd drain awaits, no timer, so it does not hold the object awake), which drains only the dirty queues.","summary":"The Worker outlet drains only after a request or alarm, so frames dispatched later wait for the next one","supersedes":"a65317782e56e23b8b5f53b3da1515f9f3c9292e6a78a905b9d4779180ab42a1","tags":["wasm","durable-object","hibernation","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:25.989666Z","id":"28e989c32f9a660f099c8d87f3f828fdbb48fbe5c84769fd7e7537b6573b0f47","body":{"detail":"After an eviction the Hub (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs) is empty: streams, rings, detached streams under GRACE, and the one sequence, which restarts. open_for cannot reopen a stream under the attachment's ID (a new stream always gets new_id(), stream.rs:840), so each socket gets a new stream ID that must be written back with serializeAttachment and announced to the client in a new ready frame. The caller, credential hash and person a StreamEntry is opened with (stream.rs:302-322) must come from the attachment and be checked against the store again before update() re-subscribes, since grants expire, rights change and people are revoked while the object sleeps. What stream::Conn's poll does (Conn::checking's still_live, clear_lag after a resync, detach on close to start GRACE, end; stream.rs:1226-1301) needs equivalents in the outlet. Cloudflare documents a 2,048-byte limit for a socket's serializeAttachment, which bounds the topics an attachment can carry.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":94},"end":{"line":97},"content_hash":"c44a497bab44a784875aa55481dd0a5a0badcd944451aa549f162ed9f6151528"},"suggested_fix":"Add Hub::reopen(attachment) that takes the stream's ID, caller, credential, person and topics, re-checks them, subscribes with resync, and returns the frames to send; have the Worker call it for every socket from getWebSockets() in the constructor before it serves anything.","summary":"Reopening each socket's stream from its attachment and sending resync does not rebuild what the hub held","supersedes":"a5637e4e199a0ed4161facb7054d02f3752e2e189f2aa3593d5eabb1bad8bc4e","tags":["wasm","durable-object","hibernation","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:25.993817Z","id":"95b95242d29e3b5c674d3f7f39cf9d3a7fd503d921f55ed8c662fe47c9984a62","body":{"detail":"On akesling/clax-artifacts the streams hold live seats (Hub::use_seats, commit f0be8e1e), keyed stream:<id>. After a wake they come back in whatever order the object re-subscribes its sockets, so with more viewers than seats a seated person can return a spectator (an unseated frame) and a spectator seated, and the idle release's last-input times restart. clax_core::presence::Presence empties too: a presence resync answers with nobody until each tab reports again, so every chip disappears and reappears. Presence reports and seat heartbeats arrive as HTTP requests (PUT /api/viewers/me/presence), each of which wakes a hibernated object, which limits what hibernation saves.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":99},"end":{"line":100},"content_hash":"aff97135bd692bb0081c9ef5c25bf2bb70b08e4108cd8a2b225b71bf8aefc6ad"},"suggested_fix":"Keep seat holders with their pools and last input, and presence entries, in the object's storage (or each socket's attachment) and restore them before the first request after a wake; carry presence reports and heartbeats as socket messages, or answer heartbeats with setWebSocketAutoResponse.","summary":"Live seats and presence are lost when the object hibernates, and rebuilding them by re-subscribing reorders who is seated","supersedes":"102650cd60e01c897d55cdfc3380a88762416c002b190b4f9694d316970b2cde","tags":["wasm","durable-object","hibernation","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:25.997965Z","id":"98c28fba188969c2b99bb7d4e98e9dd1d2f041539d886c082e37d9fac153ac25","body":{"detail":"room::Rooms (crates/clax-server/src/room.rs) keeps members, peer labels and a broadcast::Sender per room, and the per-socket relay that turns a Membership into socket frames is routes/room.rs, native only. The Worker needs a drain of each socket's broadcast::Receiver (try_recv, Lagged answered with a peers snapshot) beside the hub's queues. At eviction no Membership is dropped, so no left is sent; on wake the memberships must be rebuilt from attachments without a joined or left for every socket, and the relay's rate budgets restart. The live layers of docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design.md §16.3-16.4 (typing, comment drafts, cursors, agents' drafts served at /c/:id/draft/...) are in memory as well: an agent's draft would be lost at eviction while people still see its Show draft.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":99},"end":{"line":100},"content_hash":"aff97135bd692bb0081c9ef5c25bf2bb70b08e4108cd8a2b225b71bf8aefc6ad"},"summary":"Rooms are not drained by the hub's outlet: their frames ride tokio broadcast receivers, and memberships vanish without Drop at eviction","supersedes":"61069320e3db13e3a93b448432143e6b1f1c6e29873f3667b2786566b2bc487d","tags":["wasm","durable-object","hibernation","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.002284Z","id":"5c0d0685efefe6342ab097d0f5e66c590b6d21283bc72b8fb0f61c32b1a7020a","body":{"detail":"With rmcp's local feature, serve_directly spawns with tokio::task::spawn_local, which could run inside a LocalSet polled by the Worker's event loop; rmcp's own timeouts would still need tokio's timer, which has no driver there. Not taken: it relies on tokio internals working without a runtime context. The adapter calls the tools' methods directly (they take no RequestContext; rmcp's Peer::new is pub(crate) in rmcp 3.5's service.rs).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":105},"end":{"line":120},"content_hash":"58a789437143175753fe1d4fb8f8e95e828b2b48d375e94a5637324cff6cccd8"},"summary":"Drive rmcp's serve_directly on a tokio LocalSet inside the Worker instead of a JSON-RPC adapter","supersedes":"9b82c3b52fcabf760c0d5dba8af60074057ab1368158a9746d39e0ff4ffba249","tags":["wasm","revisit:rmcp offers a runtime-agnostic stateless handler","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.006436Z","id":"d1f406711e31a4fc814bd5da7db704f7571724679eddd525c4d6e3156c08eecc","body":{"detail":"With rmcp's local feature, serve_directly spawns with tokio::task::spawn_local, which could run inside a LocalSet polled by the Worker's event loop; rmcp's own timeouts would still need tokio's timer, which has no driver there. Not taken: it relies on tokio internals working without a runtime context. The adapter calls the tools' methods directly (they take no RequestContext; rmcp's Peer::new is pub(crate) in rmcp 3.5's service.rs).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":106},"end":{"line":118},"content_hash":"e07fbdf5f22b0429a62b48f5055ec871c719d4b981ba7cfd7729f94ac0b2a1a9"},"summary":"Drive rmcp's serve_directly on a tokio LocalSet inside the Worker instead of a JSON-RPC adapter","supersedes":"65bd574c262ad2e40a52fca3b6116b2c549980b96883ea910b38baab6764954d","tags":["wasm","revisit:rmcp offers a runtime-agnostic stateless handler","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:44:32.467858Z","id":"02e4795113e019b3fd20102f7c609dd7d063ed64c9cf714867edb81ebed5dcf9","body":{"detail":"is_grant_request includes Bearer cxa_…, and verify_layer admits it wherever a route's need! admits grants, so a script holding an agent token can call the API directly with the same rights its MCP tools have. The prototype (hosted/src/mcp/server.ts) took the token only at /mcp. The rights are identical either way; restricting it to in-process requests from the adapter would need a marker the loopback sets.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":150},"end":{"line":168},"content_hash":"78c6d61d43621b4e72f96b0129c56d3d615b995ec1453af1a1cc7714ddde1a45"},"summary":"An agent token is an agent credential on every route a grant may reach, not only through the MCP adapter","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:45:22.356067Z","id":"62e99047eaa6c30795c1863af850b17eb9448750031c4dec296699efb190ac4e","body":{"detail":"Limits holds its buckets in a Mutex<HashMap>; a restarted daemon forgets them, and a Cloudflare deployment with several isolates or Durable Objects would count per instance. Past MAX_CLIENTS (10000) clients the map is cleared.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":148},"end":{"line":151},"content_hash":"c3d9cee2df2daa7466bec6f2d7785f46a526e8ffaae9cfc54cec9c2e75b2fe50"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the buckets in the store (or one Durable Object) in the Worker build.","summary":"The abuse limits live in the process's memory: they reset on restart and are per instance","supersedes":"1123c32a59773e59d99faba4f021060318cd288aea97ffe7a9184972baa8f744","tags":["hosted","security","wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:45:22.358707Z","id":"4d672f978ca36bd2d847326b7de570b4318f420da99083534b84ccd9c8f20954","body":{"detail":"content_key is an HMAC of <aid>/<n> under the daemon token, as the prototype's commit hash (hosted/src/content.ts) never expired either. A person whose rights narrow, or a guest whose page stops being shared, still reads every version address they were handed (not later versions). A new daemon token changes every key.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":402},"end":{"line":404},"content_hash":"cd8d880448cdb31132019e34c90867877b5c99850f7b334415ffebc58c2ce63d"},"suggested_fix":"Mix a per-artifact generation into the key and bump it when the page stops being shared or a person's rights narrow.","summary":"A content key never expires: whoever saw a version's keyed address keeps reading it after losing the right","supersedes":"1453082772e2801382b7cec1de246790613ce9214644b3513a5668ba9e4db5f3","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:45:22.361098Z","id":"6566470a5c46e38761301a73ffa8265d95bb057727c6203bac254964fe698371","body":{"detail":"member_need checks the artifact only when the query names one; without it the routes answer every artifact this viewer has marks on (IDs and counts, no titles). Inbox items addressed to the person stay after their rights narrow.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":652},"end":{"line":656},"content_hash":"658bd678f5f2ca9606250a4a71b16315b8e871172a66044341faa0416f943b70"},"suggested_fix":"Filter those answers with Agent::read_rights as GET /api/artifacts does.","summary":"A person's /api/viewers/me/attention and /api/viewers/me/seen without ?artifact=, and their inbox items, are not filtered by their rights","supersedes":"73f34cb2ed924fa166cd9a2282eda80f55e48921fccb925e342b4cbdaa80dc9d","tags":["hosted","visibility","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:45:22.363456Z","id":"9455a4e5d6645edbd8de70f108fcb71f9b2ca5187cd5151478c7d39b9b8492e7","body":{"detail":"member_gate drops `gallery` from such a person's subscriptions because gallery events (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs routes, project) carry every artifact's titles and thread summaries; their gallery refreshes on load only.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":732},"end":{"line":732},"content_hash":"cc7f883b42e8d834a7aa6a6e9f0ce461e48a8702065827af2cbdbbf741b80e96"},"suggested_fix":"Gate gallery items per subscriber by artifact (a read filter fixed at subscribe time) instead of dropping the topic.","summary":"A person whose rights do not read every artifact gets no gallery stream topic, so their gallery does not update live","supersedes":"f791bb502e5f532c598858ae8bd107731caabb1634456a0c8a2a30e559ea6875","tags":["hosted","ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:45:22.365830Z","id":"5cc17b9868b81618ed2c7837ccda38d08bb3822fd5791d8efccce07bd725b997","body":{"detail":"The prototype let a commenter resolve or reopen threads they started (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design.md section 7). LinkAccess::rights (crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs) holds no comments resolve; checking a thread's creator in the gate would need a store read per request.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":882},"end":{"line":884},"content_hash":"f8564687d21d97fe5615a5674a21b9444ea4c648abef2584844c61b8e5250507"},"summary":"A guest may not resolve or reopen threads, even their own","supersedes":"ad52f1115f90250fca33988c43daf0d7004936e0a9c4a559f69114cfe0dc8ed9","tags":["revisit:guests ask to resolve their own threads","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:45:22.368239Z","id":"6c0cf7a49775888219c3b1012969021ccd168c6d943ddd4cb4914274588c99b6","body":{"detail":"PUT /api/viewers/me with no session makes a guest viewer row and a session whatever the site shares; Attempt::Guest limits it to five per client and then one per two minutes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1271},"end":{"line":1279},"content_hash":"7b0b50000594786778769269c90c8b6ed7c453ad2d601bcdc1a9e8dbea8ea63c"},"suggested_fix":"Require the page the visitor names (artifact_id in the body) to be shared for commenting.","summary":"A visitor may become a guest without any page being shared by link","supersedes":"44693a7a90e200798dab34cffdcff6aaa9dd5cc09d5dd6d41a4de32ef9c58c5a","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:19:33.546039Z","id":"02421b8bea8cb2a2e9f6b9c6989e00f4eb4ceacd73abc33dd89b2d3d26a07105","body":{"detail":"verify_bearer hands the body on unread, so a bearer grant's requests are bounded only by each route's DefaultBodyLimit (axum's 2 MiB default, PUBLISH_BODY_LIMIT on publishes) and the request timeout layers, as the daemon token's are. A signed Clax-Grant body goes through read_unverified (agent_gate: one large body per key at a time, a shared byte budget, MIN_RATE after GRACE, read_deadline). On an internet-facing hosted daemon one leaked or abused agent token can hold many concurrent 16 MiB publishes or slow bodies. The MCP adapter (routes/mcp_http.rs) reads its body with to_bytes(PUBLISH_BODY_LIMIT) outside the timeout layers, also ungated.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1756},"end":{"line":1785},"content_hash":"58fed090faeceed1ac30b6a967492e6825d85fed24ca506e5ebb7aed2fe98c61"},"suggested_fix":"Read a bearer body with read_unverified(&s.agent_gate, sha256(grant_id), headers, body, need.limit) before handing it on, and give the adapter's body read the same gate.","summary":"An agent token's request body is read outside the agent gate: no per-key permit, shared budget, minimum rate or read deadline","tags":["security","hosted","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:04:47.118856Z","id":"3d62cf7046203bee72207504d380f64f166549740b62c75172fcb1cfa917be08","body":{"detail":"conn_of is None on wasm32 (no request in a Worker has the owner machine's trust), so api_host_allowed has no local address to compare and admits only is_local_host names. Under wrangler dev the browser and e2e (crates/clax-worker/e2e.mjs) reach http://localhost:<port>, which passes; a deployed instance on its own hostname gets forbidden_host on every /api path, and the shell's /a/ bootstrap is served bare (shell::artifact_page checks request_host_allowed). Hosted mode needs the instance's public host (crates/clax-worker/wrangler.jsonc PUBLIC_ORIGIN, or the rust-hosted-signin branch's configuration) to count as an API host, keeping DNS-rebinding protection for every other name.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":384},"end":{"line":404},"content_hash":"0311925661d5b5f1dfd503fdfe969fed4cf0e7e25d1c9e8d8ffcb52f798e31f0"},"summary":"On wasm32 /api answers only Host names localhost, 127.0.0.1 and [::1], so a deployed Worker refuses every API request 403 forbidden_host","supersedes":"63b6e60d8bab111d6bbec4a5424b5a787cce7c6ba8e24d11975521842b4e9ff2","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:04:47.123553Z","id":"60f34db5d3381b7ab85bfc1be2c3a1363dbcc38bd57bae9ecc21d028b9fb606f","body":{"detail":"Limits holds its buckets in a Mutex<HashMap>; a restarted daemon forgets them, and a Cloudflare deployment with several isolates or Durable Objects would count per instance. Past MAX_CLIENTS (10000) clients the map is cleared.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":152},"end":{"line":155},"content_hash":"c3d9cee2df2daa7466bec6f2d7785f46a526e8ffaae9cfc54cec9c2e75b2fe50"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the buckets in the store (or one Durable Object) in the Worker build.","summary":"The abuse limits live in the process's memory: they reset on restart and are per instance","supersedes":"62e99047eaa6c30795c1863af850b17eb9448750031c4dec296699efb190ac4e","tags":["hosted","security","wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:04:47.127929Z","id":"b8e18181a0277265ae574d0bcffc8dc10211710da02e04f243912a42f62666f0","body":{"detail":"content_key is an HMAC of <aid>/<n> under the daemon token, as the prototype's commit hash (hosted/src/content.ts) never expired either. A person whose rights narrow, or a guest whose page stops being shared, still reads every version address they were handed (not later versions). A new daemon token changes every key.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":406},"end":{"line":408},"content_hash":"cd8d880448cdb31132019e34c90867877b5c99850f7b334415ffebc58c2ce63d"},"suggested_fix":"Mix a per-artifact generation into the key and bump it when the page stops being shared or a person's rights narrow.","summary":"A content key never expires: whoever saw a version's keyed address keeps reading it after losing the right","supersedes":"4d672f978ca36bd2d847326b7de570b4318f420da99083534b84ccd9c8f20954","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:04:47.132254Z","id":"c50614a61354a4952ebfad0463f8fbc9021f234c3c6a6736600a5586cc8ffa89","body":{"detail":"The gate could require /c/<aid>/draft/k/<content key of the base version>/<agent>/<token>/…, so a draft URL is also bound to a key the daemon derives. Not taken: the draft token is already 128 random bits minted per revision (clax_core::drafts::new_token), handed only to people who may read the artifact, and it expires with the revision, which a content key never does; a second key adds a path segment the shell's draftSrc (web/shell/src/view/draft-model.ts) and the artifact host rewrite (crates/clax-server/src/host.rs) would carry for no capability the token lacks.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":494},"end":{"line":499},"content_hash":"1784c2024ba3d1b89730649afd8e4da2b8bb437c88275427391e1e49fcc54dd8"},"summary":"Draft URLs keyed by the version's content key as well as the draft token","supersedes":"c40e19f2288778315ddb8f1eeb655c14d6a14c375ef3cf3920a18fe332ec7c4a","tags":["hosted","drafts","revisit:a draft token is logged, persisted or handed to anyone who may not read the artifact","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:04:47.136567Z","id":"d119d9ace103f244ffaaa55fee86c2cac074387a3a63d0634ef7ab74f25c8659","body":{"detail":"member_need checks the artifact only when the query names one; without it the routes answer every artifact this viewer has marks on (IDs and counts, no titles). Inbox items addressed to the person stay after their rights narrow.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":665},"end":{"line":669},"content_hash":"658bd678f5f2ca9606250a4a71b16315b8e871172a66044341faa0416f943b70"},"suggested_fix":"Filter those answers with Agent::read_rights as GET /api/artifacts does.","summary":"A person's /api/viewers/me/attention and /api/viewers/me/seen without ?artifact=, and their inbox items, are not filtered by their rights","supersedes":"6566470a5c46e38761301a73ffa8265d95bb057727c6203bac254964fe698371","tags":["hosted","visibility","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:04:47.140906Z","id":"d73bf973a30ee13967209163d6487b70e64da2ed0c003205d38c47822b39083b","body":{"detail":"member_gate drops `gallery` from such a person's subscriptions because gallery events (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs routes, project) carry every artifact's titles and thread summaries; their gallery refreshes on load only.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":745},"end":{"line":745},"content_hash":"cc7f883b42e8d834a7aa6a6e9f0ce461e48a8702065827af2cbdbbf741b80e96"},"suggested_fix":"Gate gallery items per subscriber by artifact (a read filter fixed at subscribe time) instead of dropping the topic.","summary":"A person whose rights do not read every artifact gets no gallery stream topic, so their gallery does not update live","supersedes":"9455a4e5d6645edbd8de70f108fcb71f9b2ca5187cd5151478c7d39b9b8492e7","tags":["hosted","ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:04:47.145205Z","id":"a78775d9f6e025c45ecfab715052ec49291488ebd013822b3ebd7d735391cb0d","body":{"detail":"The prototype let a commenter resolve or reopen threads they started (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design.md section 7). LinkAccess::rights (crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs) holds no comments resolve; checking a thread's creator in the gate would need a store read per request.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":900},"end":{"line":902},"content_hash":"f8564687d21d97fe5615a5674a21b9444ea4c648abef2584844c61b8e5250507"},"summary":"A guest may not resolve or reopen threads, even their own","supersedes":"5cc17b9868b81618ed2c7837ccda38d08bb3822fd5791d8efccce07bd725b997","tags":["revisit:guests ask to resolve their own threads","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:04:47.149533Z","id":"e959fccd8de5e34c4d95e18da567fda71eb2608f4c26539c339424477822fade","body":{"detail":"PUT /api/viewers/me with no session makes a guest viewer row and a session whatever the site shares; Attempt::Guest limits it to five per client and then one per two minutes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1289},"end":{"line":1297},"content_hash":"7b0b50000594786778769269c90c8b6ed7c453ad2d601bcdc1a9e8dbea8ea63c"},"suggested_fix":"Require the page the visitor names (artifact_id in the body) to be shared for commenting.","summary":"A visitor may become a guest without any page being shared by link","supersedes":"6c0cf7a49775888219c3b1012969021ccd168c6d943ddd4cb4914274588c99b6","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:05:09.570113Z","id":"6824747e969e399cfa11b892f8c58ad89d481250153aa275bfc12c7734dc36de","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:68bae229","summary":"verify_bearer (crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs) reads an agent token's body through read_unverified under bearer_key(grant_id) before handing it on, on the API within the route's limit and on the MCP adapter within PUBLISH_BODY_LIMIT; in-process loopback bodies too. cargo test -p clax-server --test integration an_agent_tokens_bodies_are_bounded_like_a_signed_grants passes (one large body per token across /api/artifacts and /mcp/json, four queued, a sixth 429 limit_reached, another token's held beside them, 408 at the read deadline, 413 past 96 MiB, two concurrent 1.5 MiB publishes through the adapter both land); with the agent.rs change reverted it fails at 'the holder within 5 s'.","supersedes":"02421b8bea8cb2a2e9f6b9c6989e00f4eb4ceacd73abc33dd89b2d3d26a07105","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:05:09.574545Z","id":"a2cc933341baec6f8043aa6b0cc84020c60d6bae327c335a67414848b5df15e6","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"a544830103a4ebcfe7cbda812c747f3bdd4964cee95a59f9c9781a07e4231754","summary":"Seen in web/e2e/hosted-demo.spec.ts: after the guest's browser context closes, Jo is offered Join live within 30 s in most runs (seats_free 1 about 5 s after), but in about one batch of three run in parallel (--repeat-each 3) the anonymous snapshot still reports seats_free 0 after 40 s and Jo is not offered Join live within 80 s; on rust-demo's tip (ee759fbc) one of three batches failed the same way, so it predates the live layers merge. Serially (--workers 1) three runs passed.","tags":["flaky","seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:35:32.220022Z","id":"10f8284074af7dffe6be7d478622cf59443ebe71f5500d801101569eadfd0be5","body":{"detail":"ArtifactsFork declares (clax-artifacts, read), so the Agent extractor answers a person's agent lacking read 403 not_permitted, as every agent read route does (GET /api/artifacts/<aid> too), while a hosted member's browser gets 404 from the member gate and a local connected person's browser 404 from routes/artifacts.rs fork_refusal. Tests: crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted.rs a_member_forks_what_they_may_read_into_their_own_artifact (404), api_forks.rs (404 for a local person).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":150},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"84ab821874e5fae80fe4de0740363b3be77453a82a1cb90633dc4a0b975bfed8"},"summary":"A person's agent without read on the source is refused fork with 403 not_permitted, a person's browser with 404","tags":["forks","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/boot.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:35:32.220178Z","id":"0847a9c30c7d921867630bc1d8d1423175e56636b3466db32b5bdcef95f14c41","body":{"detail":"GET /api/artifacts/<aid> computes artifact.may_fork from the Caller (routes/artifacts.rs fork_refusal); boot::assemble has only the Identity and the hosted member, so it leaves may_fork out. The shell shows Fork for the owner's shell at once (it holds the token, web/shell/src/ui/TopbarIsland.svelte) and for anyone else once the stream's first ready reloads the artifact.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":190},"end":{"line":196},"content_hash":"28495b9733e1530f8c99ca8aa8e82e040c1de11ebb2234c69ff6398089562f15"},"summary":"The page bootstrap carries forked_from but not may_fork, so Fork shows for a connected person only after the artifact reloads","tags":["forks","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:48:56.223392Z","id":"ce214a431984dfc7506d8591466ec90b487b6365225200309af7e3dd1cebb0cf","body":{"detail":"api_agent_auth::the_extractor_refuses_a_persons_agent_on_an_owner_agents_route now asserts that every Filtered need in ROUTES is live. The not_yet branches (agent.rs Agent<N> extraction and the body gate) stay for a Filtered route added later; remove them, with FILTERED_LIVE, once no task plans one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":524},"end":{"line":524},"content_hash":"e07bad372e55913af9df7b2c800d2741a700fd885fb02cc043d3e30bf32f99fd"},"summary":"Every Filtered need is now in FILTERED_LIVE, so the 503 not_yet path serves no route","supersedes":"a0367be36216f8709f164acb2554bbca8f8a5a65a37630d6675a44f48fa2d932","tags":["people","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:48:56.226905Z","id":"7983c5ba3a8a00e95f824c8d4fa5d289438c244e305f601d811f214043861760","body":{"detail":"Every handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1051},"end":{"line":1051},"content_hash":"95e634966fc956bcf03f44fdf7131faa6bc9307f6e163a961719bf6f762fe602"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve Person/Viewer lazily in Agent<N> (only a person's agent needs the store), or fold the read into the handler's own store_call.","summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","supersedes":"fc95c069e1af985b8dd11bc093f3cee8cd6e8f8fe494b695f619d6d5ecc52882","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/boot.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:49:02.082081Z","id":"08cdda7869fc46b2be62727f1f3d4b7a23d915277066eb98a7f49be727f9c976","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e935e9fa","summary":"Fixed: boot::assemble now computes artifact.may_fork with routes::artifacts::fork_refusal as GET /api/artifacts/<id> does; cargo nextest -p clax-server -E 'test(/shell_boot::|hosted_pages::|api_forks::/)' passes 15 of 15, including shell_boot::embeds_what_the_api_answers_and_never_the_token, which compares the two.","supersedes":"0847a9c30c7d921867630bc1d8d1423175e56636b3466db32b5bdcef95f14c41","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:12:40.326907Z","id":"463d3d7def989b6581eba93c1211b4a4c9da654807ffccfa9eda29a3d2fe7b7b","body":{"detail":"Every handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1039},"end":{"line":1039},"content_hash":"95e634966fc956bcf03f44fdf7131faa6bc9307f6e163a961719bf6f762fe602"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve Person/Viewer lazily in Agent<N> (only a person's agent needs the store), or fold the read into the handler's own store_call.","summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","supersedes":"7983c5ba3a8a00e95f824c8d4fa5d289438c244e305f601d811f214043861760","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:53:18.911193Z","id":"c71e3f23361279a67c9d2761f1f0032fde286938525f6ad095926ef42925d93a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:529dad9c","summary":"The object keeps the seats held (Seats::kept, with each seat's latest input) and the live presence reports (Presence::kept) in its storage after each event that changed them, and restores them before anyone can take a seat (Seats::restore holds each under a restored: placeholder until its holder's connection takes it). Evidence: clax-core seats::restore_tests passes; node crates/clax-worker/e2e-hosted.mjs prints 'ok   after the wake the guest's seat is still held: Sam is still a spectator' (the first request after POST /_worker/hibernate, before any browser subscribes again), 'ok   after the wake the snapshot still counts no free seat' and 'ok   after the wake presence still lists the owner and the guest'.","supersedes":"102650cd60e01c897d55cdfc3380a88762416c002b190b4f9694d316970b2cde","tags":["reason:fixed","worker","seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:53:18.915510Z","id":"61cfd01422c5b8ee40404b8b012954e963b03a8d3c175851ef94a8a72b8ff2a9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:77bb5c7f","summary":"The Worker serves the room socket (routes::room::room_socket on wasm32): RoomSocket::drain takes each membership's broadcast frames with try_recv after every event, and routes::room::reopen rebuilds the lobby and the named rooms kept in the socket's attachment after a wake. Evidence: scripts/check-wasm.sh and cargo clippy --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -p clax-server --no-deps -D warnings pass; the room protocol on the Worker is not covered by a browser check yet (recorded on crates/clax-server/src/routes/room.rs).","supersedes":"61069320e3db13e3a93b448432143e6b1f1c6e29873f3667b2786566b2bc487d","tags":["reason:fixed","worker","room","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:53:18.924355Z","id":"a2d8235073fa58bc9206abe3bc6fdb38cd789f145696dcddd24c59f2858b97bb","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5e47fcdb","summary":"With questions::SweptGraces (the Worker's sleeper) start_grace records a due time, AppState::sweep withdraws what is due and next_sweep_in names it, so the alarm runs it; a server built anew starts a grace for each open hook question no poll holds (arm_open_hooks). Evidence: cargo test -p clax-server --lib questions passes, including a_swept_grace_is_due_at_its_time_unless_a_poll_held_it.","supersedes":"dfae291e43fb5c268c73de5ed416822113cdac0f4092efad9c95aae342995d7e","tags":["reason:fixed","worker","questions","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/viewer.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:53:18.934682Z","id":"4f1568aa6e1b19ce911dedf1f74be71d069f8f6fba202db4b2a66792a89e1108","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d6f500a2","summary":"SameOrigin takes https://<Host> as well as http://<Host> (a hosted daemon's requests already passed by the gate's origin check). Evidence: cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_viewers::the_shells_own_https_origin_is_its_own_and_another_https_one_is_not passes.","supersedes":"f6feaeeb0a961309ba4a544ae21622cdf0183fd56acad294b7370bd97878d215","tags":["reason:fixed","worker","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:53:18.938989Z","id":"95704bd169cc79b9dece225f7c05106e499bede60f6798d3beb48403d33c49c9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b0633a0a","summary":"A hosted daemon takes a content origin of its own (Hosted::with_content_origin; CONTENT_ORIGIN on the Worker): content is served there at its key, framed sandboxed, its bridge naming the public origin (data-origin), and never on the public origin; <id>.localhost still serves under wrangler dev. Evidence: cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_hosted::with_a_content_origin_content_is_served_there_alone_and_its_pages_name_the_shell passes; node crates/clax-worker/e2e-hosted.mjs prints 'ok   the frame loads the page on the content origin at its key', 'ok   the keyed URL is not served on the public origin' and 'ok   the owner's page draws the guest's pointer, through the bridge on the content origin'.","supersedes":"8304b25148ff5397b6bfce372e953a0d35735c6077c74738c426efc3bd92da64","tags":["reason:fixed","worker","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:53:18.943367Z","id":"a9c88382a4615db132c2894696949fe9a6c35b81a17ac6ae46af2fc62a3f3720","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:529dad9c","summary":"A deployed Worker runs hosted (HOSTED=1), where the hosted gate stands in for this rule (crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs wrap) and answers PUBLIC_ORIGIN's host. A non-hosted Worker keeps the loopback names only, by design (it has no sign-in). Evidence: node crates/clax-worker/e2e-hosted.mjs, on public origin http://localhost:<port>, exits 0 with every API route the shell calls answering.","supersedes":"63b6e60d8bab111d6bbec4a5424b5a787cce7c6ba8e24d11975521842b4e9ff2","tags":["reason:fixed","worker","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:53:18.947807Z","id":"387ba71d44750cd6d4956cd43fdf970f201622cb380d1e2e005fcc667870aed4","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"c76b1a73dcc62299940d392d94afef14366011d81297390ad376fe566e35e5a0","summary":"On the Worker the limits live in the instance object's memory: one instance object serves every client, so they are counted per site, and they reset at every wake or eviction as at a daemon restart.","tags":["worker","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.019366Z","id":"eb0c49b236a1d110fe348870b969e8f3d1cb35b955431a2a09b45716e0e89aa3","body":{"detail":"Hub::dispatch also runs from tasks spawned off the request path: inbox::listen and approvals::listen consume store change notifications in clax_rt::spawn tasks (crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs:349-392, crates/clax-server/src/approvals.rs:193-200), questions::start_grace closes a question after its grace (crates/clax-server/src/questions.rs:296), flight::drive streams a sample, and agent::verify_layer notes a grant's use (crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs:1620). Their frames reach the queues after that request's drain ran and sit there until the next request, socket message or alarm, which on a quiet artifact can be minutes. Draining every socket after every message also costs O(open sockets) per incoming message; at the rates of docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design.md §16.5 (30 senders at 10 a second, 100 seats) that is most of the object's work.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":89},"end":{"line":99},"content_hash":"bd4c73af62822f0512f511921d10c9927a60727230fef892622d28f960a2b8c4"},"suggested_fix":"Have Hub::dispatch mark the subscribers it queued for as dirty and wake one outlet task (a tokio::sync::Notify that a spawn_local'd drain awaits, no timer, so it does not hold the object awake), which drains only the dirty queues.","summary":"The Worker outlet drains only after a request or alarm, so frames dispatched later wait for the next one","supersedes":"a65317782e56e23b8b5f53b3da1515f9f3c9292e6a78a905b9d4779180ab42a1","tags":["wasm","durable-object","hibernation","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.023572Z","id":"6f3ecf6daab9ec174ef0d1138779b9f43c70f1a20dbcc75433306f4b392a7537","body":{"detail":"After an eviction the Hub (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs) is empty: streams, rings, detached streams under GRACE, and the one sequence, which restarts. open_for cannot reopen a stream under the attachment's ID (a new stream always gets new_id(), stream.rs:840), so each socket gets a new stream ID that must be written back with serializeAttachment and announced to the client in a new ready frame. The caller, credential hash and person a StreamEntry is opened with (stream.rs:302-322) must come from the attachment and be checked against the store again before update() re-subscribes, since grants expire, rights change and people are revoked while the object sleeps. What stream::Conn's poll does (Conn::checking's still_live, clear_lag after a resync, detach on close to start GRACE, end; stream.rs:1226-1301) needs equivalents in the outlet. Cloudflare documents a 2,048-byte limit for a socket's serializeAttachment, which bounds the topics an attachment can carry.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":96},"end":{"line":99},"content_hash":"c44a497bab44a784875aa55481dd0a5a0badcd944451aa549f162ed9f6151528"},"suggested_fix":"Add Hub::reopen(attachment) that takes the stream's ID, caller, credential, person and topics, re-checks them, subscribes with resync, and returns the frames to send; have the Worker call it for every socket from getWebSockets() in the constructor before it serves anything.","summary":"Reopening each socket's stream from its attachment and sending resync does not rebuild what the hub held","supersedes":"a5637e4e199a0ed4161facb7054d02f3752e2e189f2aa3593d5eabb1bad8bc4e","tags":["wasm","durable-object","hibernation","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/viewer.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.027810Z","id":"51025cde9ef902083fd82e66a81f4c0457fd1e3702dbd81b720fbe5165753978","body":{"detail":"A Clax-Grant caller writing a thread or a comment without author_kind agent is attributed to its grant's person (author_public_id, display name), as the token's agents are to the owner. Storing it as an agent comment with its session would show it as the agent's in the shell, but a thread's first comment is a viewer comment (NewThread) and a viewer comment forwards the thread, so the semantics would change. Authorship, which the filter needs, is right either way.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":119},"end":{"line":134},"content_hash":"83ee2c4a800f2125d8a2bab39db59a095b257bef4fe8d7cf0c04be3b50037d7d"},"summary":"A person's agent's viewer-kind comment is stored as its person's viewer comment, not as an agent comment","supersedes":"9b8b3a6d7be75ffded915adba181e0e7baa3e8e2c42186e8a5615f63e0a0a56b","tags":["revisit:when the shell shows which agent wrote a person's comment","people","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.032166Z","id":"71370ce2afcd803145d8eb079aa47fc783287b911100c94eccb085d444870154","body":{"detail":"Limits holds its buckets in a Mutex<HashMap>; a restarted daemon forgets them, and a Cloudflare deployment with several isolates or Durable Objects would count per instance. Past MAX_CLIENTS (10000) clients the map is cleared.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":162},"end":{"line":165},"content_hash":"c3d9cee2df2daa7466bec6f2d7785f46a526e8ffaae9cfc54cec9c2e75b2fe50"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the buckets in the store (or one Durable Object) in the Worker build.","summary":"The abuse limits live in the process's memory: they reset on restart and are per instance","supersedes":"c76b1a73dcc62299940d392d94afef14366011d81297390ad376fe566e35e5a0","tags":["hosted","security","wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.036468Z","id":"ff6db32197d5ff3820dce9f12e9ea3c19c7c6b638c8621b22b99cc5f9b08ba5a","body":{"detail":"The prototype let a commenter resolve or reopen threads they started (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design.md section 7). LinkAccess::rights (crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs) holds no comments resolve; checking a thread's creator in the gate would need a store read per request.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":990},"end":{"line":992},"content_hash":"f8564687d21d97fe5615a5674a21b9444ea4c648abef2584844c61b8e5250507"},"summary":"A guest may not resolve or reopen threads, even their own","supersedes":"7c0fa639b7afef99835773a10f352dd73d4f594bfb8605b552410154e40a6e69","tags":["revisit:guests ask to resolve their own threads","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.040753Z","id":"a3926ab4b74bf9e91ddc4e5d70bc5e05e02aeb768c5c1c8cfe94fbc7a9363414","body":{"detail":"member_gate drops `gallery` from such a person's subscriptions because gallery events (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs routes, project) carry every artifact's titles and thread summaries; their gallery refreshes on load only.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":835},"end":{"line":835},"content_hash":"cc7f883b42e8d834a7aa6a6e9f0ce461e48a8702065827af2cbdbbf741b80e96"},"suggested_fix":"Gate gallery items per subscriber by artifact (a read filter fixed at subscribe time) instead of dropping the topic.","summary":"A person whose rights do not read every artifact gets no gallery stream topic, so their gallery does not update live","supersedes":"a733fb7947e0ea9d5c28f14d4fb497b62f36b0918e9ece49737913032c6d136d","tags":["hosted","ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.045048Z","id":"de397d2c872772d5ff3d350bfb3e2563f7561e28cec5a0049274e5cdca4de0b2","body":{"detail":"member_need checks the artifact only when the query names one; without it the routes answer every artifact this viewer has marks on (IDs and counts, no titles). Inbox items addressed to the person stay after their rights narrow.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":755},"end":{"line":759},"content_hash":"658bd678f5f2ca9606250a4a71b16315b8e871172a66044341faa0416f943b70"},"suggested_fix":"Filter those answers with Agent::read_rights as GET /api/artifacts does.","summary":"A person's /api/viewers/me/attention and /api/viewers/me/seen without ?artifact=, and their inbox items, are not filtered by their rights","supersedes":"1059e72634ed9a3423124744b4e1bdd6b119b2f3c96ea7715db8c98e12fc7cf9","tags":["hosted","visibility","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.049273Z","id":"e0b8c927e7f22e7c0ff498455d78dd8cc068cdb8c910c1297290dca18184afd3","body":{"detail":"content_key is an HMAC of <aid>/<n> under the daemon token, as the prototype's commit hash (hosted/src/content.ts) never expired either. A person whose rights narrow, or a guest whose page stops being shared, still reads every version address they were handed (not later versions). A new daemon token changes every key.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":456},"end":{"line":458},"content_hash":"cd8d880448cdb31132019e34c90867877b5c99850f7b334415ffebc58c2ce63d"},"suggested_fix":"Mix a per-artifact generation into the key and bump it when the page stops being shared or a person's rights narrow.","summary":"A content key never expires: whoever saw a version's keyed address keeps reading it after losing the right","supersedes":"5701e6275ed5f060462a65c7d3183f5224d99463425bd758a92bd854eb7a1550","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.053513Z","id":"4aa5d6991cc2aaf0b8b10d6bcd47f702c8cd5461b0e40e631ae63c6a77a9af8d","body":{"detail":"PUT /api/viewers/me with no session makes a guest viewer row and a session whatever the site shares; Attempt::Guest limits it to five per client and then one per two minutes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1406},"end":{"line":1414},"content_hash":"7b0b50000594786778769269c90c8b6ed7c453ad2d601bcdc1a9e8dbea8ea63c"},"suggested_fix":"Require the page the visitor names (artifact_id in the body) to be shared for commenting.","summary":"A visitor may become a guest without any page being shared by link","supersedes":"0e1fe424364639f0fd7d1771d53a30fed056e4fe2643c65bb1f476027b7820ed","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.057797Z","id":"09b428eab287960073bcdfc3fedce8c854fcedf06593086fa372e2d0d9835718","body":{"detail":"The gate could require /c/<aid>/draft/k/<content key of the base version>/<agent>/<token>/…, so a draft URL is also bound to a key the daemon derives. Not taken: the draft token is already 128 random bits minted per revision (clax_core::drafts::new_token), handed only to people who may read the artifact, and it expires with the revision, which a content key never does; a second key adds a path segment the shell's draftSrc (web/shell/src/view/draft-model.ts) and the artifact host rewrite (crates/clax-server/src/host.rs) would carry for no capability the token lacks.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":544},"end":{"line":549},"content_hash":"1eb3ba02e9270a952f8677687cf948c44e4be183b4f1fcf9567e9067d50f00f4"},"summary":"Draft URLs keyed by the version's content key as well as the draft token","supersedes":"c40e19f2288778315ddb8f1eeb655c14d6a14c375ef3cf3920a18fe332ec7c4a","tags":["hosted","drafts","revisit:a draft token is logged, persisted or handed to anyone who may not read the artifact","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.062048Z","id":"0d60f7addeac422df9b45e698dd052f03f2ed7d97abe3e5f76a31187c5aa6040","body":{"detail":"Identity::caller makes the token an OwnerAgent whenever a session is named (path or X-Clax-Session), known or not; audit_actor records an agent only for a known session of the token's, the agent marker, or x-clax-via mcp, else the owner. Measured through GET /api/_test/audit/ctx: Authorization Bearer + X-Clax-Session 01JB9S00000000000000000099 (no session) and X-Clax-Session not-a-ulid both give {\"type\":\"owner\"}. Today's clients send the marker, so this bites only an older or third-party agent side; it breaks audit spec section 5.2's rule that one request is never an agent to Caller and the owner to the journal.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":575},"end":{"line":582},"content_hash":"2db1b19798e5ac1c9d3e05ceea096fd3a29342166c6fa288a0e708c6112fd607"},"suggested_fix":"When the token names any session that is not known, record the sessionless agent (channel as named, else mcp) instead of the owner; add the case to the_agent_channel_marker_makes_the_token_an_agent.","summary":"The token naming an unknown or non-ULID session without the agent marker is recorded as the owner, while Caller counts it as OwnerAgent","supersedes":"02805c8d6f3e2f453dde4095289d08247904fa15ca657de6fcfd1c02ba2106c3","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.066321Z","id":"e7c9a8c043719761fcaa5b79e9f269f12f841231e9f00b9803c2eb07cabde214","body":{"detail":"The native daemon has no per-artifact live socket like the hosted prototype's /api/artifacts/:id/live (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts fetch); the shell's one shared stream subscribing an artifact's artifact, presence or working topic holds the seat (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs use_seats, crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs update). A live relay of pointers, selections and typing on another connection asks LiveSeats::is_seated, or holds a seat itself with LiveSeats::take and leave under its own connection key and hears idle releases through LiveSeats::on_idle; nothing natively takes an agent seat yet, as agents hold no live connection here.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":209},"end":{"line":214},"content_hash":"6765f425d3da579fb7d4c499dcd98eaa910d354d2aacaa27e916982be6cb746c"},"summary":"Seats are held by /api/stream subscriptions, not by a live socket of their own","supersedes":"ae6c12d304e92bb682a6063c40c186d2817c04ffab731da9d146ff558950ded0","tags":["revisit:a live relay socket lands beside /api/stream","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.070598Z","id":"3980c46d4d5420d13b98f554ab8e636ae3a8a6ee821df1343eedec052d67d4f3","body":{"detail":"crate::seats::subscribe (called by POST /api/stream/<id>, crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs update) takes the artifact's seat for connection stream:<id> when the stream holds none of its live topics yet. If two calls add live topics of the same artifact at once and one then fails (TooMany, Hidden), its rollback leaves the seat the other call's topics rely on. The shell's hub sends one change at a time per stream, so this needs a hand-made client.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":402},"end":{"line":423},"content_hash":"9dc19e2a7ab13c89b2a98d0989be38a0f0d1323baad96b057991869175787a91"},"summary":"Two concurrent subscription changes of one stream can leave it on an artifact's live topics without its seat","supersedes":"834eb422277d8e55ca28156bd09616e8ddd40b144102651cc8193ba901e292f9","tags":["live-seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.074889Z","id":"9200c1708a3b330af8b6bc7587653268266825c7b3128f976d7c7b98e4c2085b","body":{"detail":"Identity::caller makes the token an OwnerAgent whenever a session is named (path or X-Clax-Session), known or not; audit_actor records an agent only for a known session of the token's, the agent marker, or x-clax-via mcp, else the owner. Measured through GET /api/_test/audit/ctx: Authorization Bearer + X-Clax-Session 01JB9S00000000000000000099 (no session) and X-Clax-Session not-a-ulid both give {\"type\":\"owner\"}. Today's clients send the marker, so this bites only an older or third-party agent side; it breaks audit spec section 5.2's rule that one request is never an agent to Caller and the owner to the journal.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":595},"end":{"line":602},"content_hash":"75fc91286c48244768b0a0e9a1d2af39937a039081897bf71644933e706cbb12"},"suggested_fix":"When the token names any session that is not known, record the sessionless agent (channel as named, else mcp) instead of the owner; add the case to the_agent_channel_marker_makes_the_token_an_agent.","summary":"The token naming an unknown or non-ULID session without the agent marker is recorded as the owner, while Caller counts it as OwnerAgent","supersedes":"1f8be26236b43f3d282bb2f9abecfb0ee025a5c4bc6a285a78d7f447ec129aeb","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.079282Z","id":"d5a80748dd72fc2b21592e75c300b1eda3f1b2bfab27cc6dc8a86915d380ea65","body":{"detail":"The native daemon has no per-artifact live socket like the hosted prototype's /api/artifacts/:id/live (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts fetch); the shell's one shared stream subscribing an artifact's artifact, presence or working topic holds the seat (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs use_seats, crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs update). A live relay of pointers, selections and typing on another connection asks LiveSeats::is_seated, or holds a seat itself with LiveSeats::take and leave under its own connection key and hears idle releases through LiveSeats::on_idle; nothing natively takes an agent seat yet, as agents hold no live connection here.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":210},"end":{"line":215},"content_hash":"32ceb5fbc1090c840186b68a86c8d81947c5c3f81c3c2528455f8ab93d97ec23"},"summary":"Seats are held by /api/stream subscriptions, not by a live socket of their own","supersedes":"f6ea243dddd50fc9aa0b735b0be246b54d70a7861d8c4a79f93b9372bb0c3ac1","tags":["revisit:a live relay socket lands beside /api/stream","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.083680Z","id":"7aa11f30cefab2800c883cac68d2e5f3828bc9ebd75e7ff8d91972e24c02bd33","body":{"detail":"crate::seats::subscribe (called by POST /api/stream/<id>, crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs update) takes the artifact's seat for connection stream:<id> when the stream holds none of its live topics yet. If two calls add live topics of the same artifact at once and one then fails (TooMany, Hidden), its rollback leaves the seat the other call's topics rely on. The shell's hub sends one change at a time per stream, so this needs a hand-made client.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":403},"end":{"line":424},"content_hash":"d1bde61f01852bf26b409a8e492815bad85c59a044543e416aeee2aa7d62106e"},"summary":"Two concurrent subscription changes of one stream can leave it on an artifact's live topics without its seat","supersedes":"029eb17a4338924cc93d8994a917dec7cef9e2d3579d8338c61e187c0aafd566","tags":["live-seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:55:47.339154Z","id":"17eb75b5abd9cdc366ef34948716a5db31f0d6f7ab69a86aa29b63531017bbd8","body":{"detail":"With rmcp's local feature, serve_directly spawns with tokio::task::spawn_local, which could run inside a LocalSet polled by the Worker's event loop; rmcp's own timeouts would still need tokio's timer, which has no driver there. Not taken: it relies on tokio internals working without a runtime context. The adapter calls the tools' methods directly (they take no RequestContext; rmcp's Peer::new is pub(crate) in rmcp 3.5's service.rs).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":120},"end":{"line":135},"content_hash":"67ec541010bad6b266922dfa88431aa7b67a7638afae8ff33659215395dca1f4"},"summary":"Drive rmcp's serve_directly on a tokio LocalSet inside the Worker instead of a JSON-RPC adapter","supersedes":"9b82c3b52fcabf760c0d5dba8af60074057ab1368158a9746d39e0ff4ffba249","tags":["wasm","revisit:rmcp offers a runtime-agnostic stateless handler","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:55:47.344122Z","id":"68678ccb28a3d84a67b1393468f94eeb89de50b64e61473b49b1f9182f21723d","body":{"detail":"With rmcp's local feature, serve_directly spawns with tokio::task::spawn_local, which could run inside a LocalSet polled by the Worker's event loop; rmcp's own timeouts would still need tokio's timer, which has no driver there. Not taken: it relies on tokio internals working without a runtime context. The adapter calls the tools' methods directly (they take no RequestContext; rmcp's Peer::new is pub(crate) in rmcp 3.5's service.rs).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":120},"end":{"line":135},"content_hash":"67ec541010bad6b266922dfa88431aa7b67a7638afae8ff33659215395dca1f4"},"summary":"Drive rmcp's serve_directly on a tokio LocalSet inside the Worker instead of a JSON-RPC adapter","supersedes":"65bd574c262ad2e40a52fca3b6116b2c549980b96883ea910b38baab6764954d","tags":["wasm","revisit:rmcp offers a runtime-agnostic stateless handler","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:20:28.275994Z","id":"91d912cc8d163e248ff5272450df5f7686ce72c65fc6dafdfcc89c04c5138819","body":{"detail":"Both branches admit Authorization: Bearer cxa_... as a person's agent. Take rust-demo's for: agent::BearerGrant/bearer_head/verify_bearer (this branch's BearerHead/bearer_verified, lines 1527:1546 and 1704:1732); auth::is_bearer_grant_request/bearer_agent_token (this branch's is_bearer_agent); mcp_http.rs's McpCaller and serve_agent, with one harness session per MCP client answered as Mcp-Session-Id, validated, heartbeated and capped at 16 per token by end_bearer_sessions_beyond (this branch's TokenOrBearer and bearer_session, which put every call of a token in one session named mcp:<grant> and write the store on every call, records e71a21f9 and 0e23d200); clax-mcp's DaemonClient::in_session/register_session/heartbeat_session and ClaxTools::in_session/for_remote_agent (this branch's DaemonClient::as_caller_in and ClaxTools::for_caller_in, mcp_http.rs:244, which carry no local-path refusal: see the blocker on mcp_http.rs); no daemon log path in remote errors; participants carrying the agent's name. Keep from this branch, as rust-demo lacks them: bearer_head's refusal of agent tokens on a daemon that is not hosted (.filter(|_| s.hosted.is_some()), line 1539), so a hosted database opened by a local daemon admits no bearer; the wasm32 routes for /api/artifacts/{aid}/room and /live (routes/mod.rs, room::room_socket, live_layers::live_socket) and every Worker-side piece (crates/clax-worker); the l10 gate test's checks, rewritten for rust-demo's McpCaller. The mcp:<grant> session naming need not survive: rust-demo's sessions are per MCP client by Mcp-Session-Id. After the merge, crates/clax-worker/e2e-hosted.mjs's mcp() helper sends no Mcp-Session-Id: it must carry the one initialize answers if rust-demo's adapter requires it, and the Worker's /mcp (PATH on wasm32) must be checked to run rust-demo's serve_agent there.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1527},"end":{"line":1546},"content_hash":"d7b581c73d5cb5e873521761487931789ca26bf64c5543112e50cd92586ac2d7"},"summary":"At merge with rust-demo, keep rust-demo's agent tokens (7c2c595e and its fixes) and drop this branch's 9b39d68a/94849514 except the pieces listed here","tags":["merge","agent-token","rust-demo","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:21:25.560493Z","id":"cb9fad8307d17b202a64a15a4d96b54700b3826c09a7de301c7438aa527b6ef8","body":{"detail":"Identity::caller makes the token an OwnerAgent whenever a session is named (path or X-Clax-Session), known or not; audit_actor records an agent only for a known session of the token's, the agent marker, or x-clax-via mcp, else the owner. Measured through GET /api/_test/audit/ctx: Authorization Bearer + X-Clax-Session 01JB9S00000000000000000099 (no session) and X-Clax-Session not-a-ulid both give {\"type\":\"owner\"}. Today's clients send the marker, so this bites only an older or third-party agent side; it breaks audit spec section 5.2's rule that one request is never an agent to Caller and the owner to the journal.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":576},"end":{"line":583},"content_hash":"2db1b19798e5ac1c9d3e05ceea096fd3a29342166c6fa288a0e708c6112fd607"},"suggested_fix":"When the token names any session that is not known, record the sessionless agent (channel as named, else mcp) instead of the owner; add the case to the_agent_channel_marker_makes_the_token_an_agent.","summary":"The token naming an unknown or non-ULID session without the agent marker is recorded as the owner, while Caller counts it as OwnerAgent","supersedes":"0d60f7addeac422df9b45e698dd052f03f2ed7d97abe3e5f76a31187c5aa6040","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:21:25.571607Z","id":"4871c8921b7d5dc6ac0053d138249b7f6c859cd5724cab51292049df68caf7cc","body":{"detail":"Identity::caller makes the token an OwnerAgent whenever a session is named (path or X-Clax-Session), known or not; audit_actor records an agent only for a known session of the token's, the agent marker, or x-clax-via mcp, else the owner. Measured through GET /api/_test/audit/ctx: Authorization Bearer + X-Clax-Session 01JB9S00000000000000000099 (no session) and X-Clax-Session not-a-ulid both give {\"type\":\"owner\"}. Today's clients send the marker, so this bites only an older or third-party agent side; it breaks audit spec section 5.2's rule that one request is never an agent to Caller and the owner to the journal.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":596},"end":{"line":603},"content_hash":"75fc91286c48244768b0a0e9a1d2af39937a039081897bf71644933e706cbb12"},"suggested_fix":"When the token names any session that is not known, record the sessionless agent (channel as named, else mcp) instead of the owner; add the case to the_agent_channel_marker_makes_the_token_an_agent.","summary":"The token naming an unknown or non-ULID session without the agent marker is recorded as the owner, while Caller counts it as OwnerAgent","supersedes":"9200c1708a3b330af8b6bc7587653268266825c7b3128f976d7c7b98e4c2085b","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:01:07.843248Z","id":"96b83bb5dbebab5ded371a67ad8f0458f3405451110453ffeb1c1ab59163202d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:878d299f","summary":"Done as suggested in the merge of rust-worker-hosted into rust-int (878d299f): rust-int's (rust-demo's) BearerGrant, bearer_head, verify_bearer, is_bearer_grant_request, bearer_agent_token, McpCaller, serve_agent and for_remote_agent kept; BearerHead, bearer_verified, is_bearer_agent, TokenOrBearer, bearer_session, as_caller_in and for_caller_in not taken (git grep finds none); bearer_head refuses agent tokens on a daemon that is not hosted (.filter(|_| s.hosted.is_some())); the wasm32 room and live routes and the Worker code taken; the l10 gate test checks McpCaller's extractor (super::agents::mcp_caller). Evidence: cargo nextest run --workspace, 2453 passed; node e2e-hosted.mjs 47 ok, node e2e.mjs 19 ok.","supersedes":"91d912cc8d163e248ff5272450df5f7686ce72c65fc6dafdfcc89c04c5138819","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:30:15.172615Z","id":"1b9bdc1bbd476189ad411fff999b572892b9b823c82a371e04dc395bfe2d94ec","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:8eceadaf","summary":"Fixed in web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts (8eceadaf): the seat was not the guest's. Seat traces showed the guest's stream detached and parked within milliseconds of its context closing; the seat went to Jo, whose stream hub had split a request refused no_live_seat into one request per topic, so a request for working:<id> landing after the guest left took the seat while artifact:<id> stayed refused (Jo's view half-live, snapshot seats_free 0, no Join live). The hub now keeps an artifact's live topics in one request and refuses them together. Evidence: the new web/shell/src/stream-hub.test.ts case 'splits a request refused a seat by artifact' fails on d27147ca and passes after; web/e2e/hosted-demo.spec.ts --repeat-each 6 --workers 3 passed 8 batches of 6 (48/48), and with the old hub failed 1 of 18 runs at its live-comment check.","supersedes":"a544830103a4ebcfe7cbda812c747f3bdd4964cee95a59f9c9781a07e4231754","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/auth.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:12:33.139751Z","id":"286f8c4e1e141d28a052218f4aa11bc0496a1503cb4566bf0de6b1068feeab7f","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"02e4795113e019b3fd20102f7c609dd7d063ed64c9cf714867edb81ebed5dcf9","summary":"The hosted/ files this record cites were removed in 60298c1d (the TypeScript prototype's retirement); read one at its parent with git show 60298c1d^:hosted/<path>","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:12:33.139834Z","id":"64b78889daf5ac0c2dcc258e996664df99289ce31b7a702f3bfcbd735e1fe82a","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"b8e18181a0277265ae574d0bcffc8dc10211710da02e04f243912a42f62666f0","summary":"The hosted/ files this record cites were removed in 60298c1d (the TypeScript prototype's retirement); read one at its parent with git show 60298c1d^:hosted/<path>","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:12:33.140088Z","id":"2c765b047fd16a43f990996bc2c602464f57d71a5f0ae40210fd2826dcebbf53","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"d5a80748dd72fc2b21592e75c300b1eda3f1b2bfab27cc6dc8a86915d380ea65","summary":"The hosted/ files this record cites were removed in 60298c1d (the TypeScript prototype's retirement); read one at its parent with git show 60298c1d^:hosted/<path>","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:58:01.484506Z","id":"00ad3144f125bca53f06ff2a515d335ca22c243911a8f11015187d68a4507e12","body":{"detail":"A pasted command lands in the shell's history with the token, and while git runs any user of the machine can read its -c argument in the process list. The GIT_CONFIG_COUNT/GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0/GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0 form (what jj_clone_command and the jj commands use) keeps it out of other users' process list but not out of the history, and does not work as pasted in PowerShell or cmd; a credential helper given inline (-c credential.helper=...) is on the command line the same way. Keeping it out of the history needs two steps (read the token into a variable, then run the command with it), which a one-paste flow does not have. docs/contract.md 'Git remotes' states the trade; the tokens' lives (3600 s, 900 s for agents) bound it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":647},"end":{"line":667},"content_hash":"6b54dbed5895c129171356cda07b70b28b4862cb13ea6c3e866d6a1beb86530f"},"summary":"The commands carry the token on git's command line (-c http.extraHeader), as the hosted spec's section 9 and hosted/src/git/commands.ts do, not in the environment or a credential helper","tags":["security","revisit:shared multi-user machines are a target, or the dialog grows a two-step flow","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:58:01.484767Z","id":"52d6af27afcb77f3fad96e1c4143e7977002a500236076ece314f19671dbcb64","body":{"detail":"recheck asks the host for every live held token (RepoDO token/held on the Worker) and, per token, builds a Visibility and reads Store::repo_history (the artifact's and its lineage's versions and refused pushers). listen runs it after every Version, ArtifactDeleted, People and Agents event burst; settle_layer before answering a request that moved the generation; and listen once when a server is built (each Durable Object wake). Fine for a handful of tokens; with many, a recheck per artifact and a per-reader Visibility cache would bound it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":839},"end":{"line":870},"content_hash":"b17df665b58dc5c49d825e15cc8d73520f3048d38ecd43a929bfefa2ebed202b"},"summary":"A recheck lists every held token from the host and walks each one's repository history: run on every relevant event, every request that moves the visibility generation, and every server built anew","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:58:01.484871Z","id":"faaed9d6ca7b483b7bfef632f58f226223c0a26fde3eac95e0a1a8adc6b3e7ac","body":{"detail":"set_link rechecks the artifact's held tokens before it answers so a person whose rights there came from the page's link loses them (git_remotes::recheck, and recheck_soon when the host fails). A member's preset rights read every artifact, so a test needs a member whose rights do not read it, a git host (TestServer git_remotes) and hosted mode; crates/clax-server/tests/api_git_tokens.rs covers the other paths.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1925},"end":{"line":1931},"content_hash":"c1569eca0d75eadc3a06808818ba5742f7cb3e307db7ef60ad77678c06ec729f"},"summary":"No test covers set_link's recheck of the artifact's git tokens","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:58:17.337303Z","id":"9f7b1b0d1a92bb58d9349673d65a120df2ae989d89a8c91052e06b6cf73f9024","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d025c062","summary":"Fixed: the router's settle_layer revokes the sessions a request ended (and rechecks after a visibility change) before it answers, the Worker's alarm settles after the grants' expiry, a failed revocation stays due for the sweep (next_sweep_in sets the alarm), and a server built anew rechecks first. cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_git_tokens: 11 passed, including a_withdrawn_approval_or_an_ended_grant_revokes_tokens_before_its_route_answers, which fails 3 of 3 runs with the layer's settle disabled.","supersedes":"47b67b0e4f476d272715b4064b681c248ba135702e5738a5764298572daad248","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:58:17.346483Z","id":"5ffa139e22ba614fb35f5752fe5d8e4ed247294efa9bea6ffd4ef0f671481233","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:96e086dd","summary":"Fixed: withheld_history reads Store::repo_history, the fork's lineage's versions up to each forked version (deleted artifacts included) and refused pushers; an ancestor gone refuses as withheld. Tests pass: store::forks::tests::a_forks_repository_history_carries_its_lineage_up_to_each_forked_version and api_git_tokens::an_agent_whose_person_may_not_see_an_author_of_a_forks_source_gets_no_token_for_the_fork.","supersedes":"65d931f9200de9ef01bebc5bff5358550f0cc47a40aa06fb7aa4c8af72f21534","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:58:17.353296Z","id":"1d64bff3d7da92add384ffb1c31c804ae50d7d280cacfe47cfcfe550c98d48ee","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4e08d09a","summary":"Fixed: record_version_locked revokes agents' tokens blind to the publisher before a publish writes its commit, refusing it 503 repo_unavailable with nothing written when one cannot be. Test passes: clax-content-git pushes::a_publish_revokes_the_agents_tokens_blind_to_its_publisher_before_its_commit. The recheck's cost is now its own record on git_remotes.rs recheck.","supersedes":"2b64693a08860532629120465e795529c26a75184fd47b4272773476eb836796","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:18:42.800922Z","id":"cb4161519ccae68ce6c3608965e5383f03f1bc69b38fec32544fe17a0dd79653","body":{"detail":"Withhold::approval runs Store::request_state once per thread that withholds anything, so a listing of N such threads makes N indexed reads (plus st.owner() when the owner is withheld). Versions and names are cached per call. vis_threads_ms (Task 25) will show whether it matters.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1452},"end":{"line":1479},"content_hash":"05c56d201c29c0092d6039e9c09166c4bdf07ea63e935e45f87326bf15b12593"},"summary":"Each thread with withheld content costs one approval_requests query in a listing","supersedes":"f559d622c6bcca21daf23cead0ae2af5ffde2cb634ed222851bccf366f273aed","tags":["perf","visibility","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:18:42.801773Z","id":"777f73035d7a5f9161487b888cffb6089b5d3d309dfee4e420a23e273c5ba40b","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1502},"end":{"line":1546},"content_hash":"ddf90a27cffb9eae9f415b9f193ba4f15b3c221446be555e0e4c03e03e2abb50"},"summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","supersedes":"0bff06035fe29526cc9380b595d01a3df710809f0f1822b6cddbb5f5dce777ff","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:18:42.803114Z","id":"1dbaca65d457ad88989dc8d993b5022ec4e332eeaecb78ee1415ecae35148d88","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ff136528","summary":"GET /api/approvals now runs each approval's artifact_title through the caller's visibility (Vis::filter_approval in crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs, called from routes/approvals.rs list): null for an agent where the title's authors are withheld. Evidence: cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_approvals::an_agents_approvals_withhold_a_page_title_it_may_not_see passes (Sam approves Mia in one thread only; Sam's agent gets title null from GET /api/artifacts/<aid> and artifact_title null from GET /api/approvals; Sam's browser still gets 'Quarterly Review'). With the filter_approval call removed the test fails at its artifact_title assertion.","supersedes":"83810fedd6a750637b449b77443a262f55d2b2dc836826409ce2299c2da4c590","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:18:42.803772Z","id":"c8d0794f84fb243f01b0cbdf6c48f8be81deec2364bfe8a14e744a0898184914","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ab0148c9","summary":"Withhold::named now names authors with clax_core::feedback::person_name, which gives an unnamed owner 'The owner' (approvals.rs person() uses the same helper). Evidence: cargo test -p clax-core feedback::tests::an_unnamed_owner_is_the_owner_and_never_viewer passes, and the integration test api_approvals::an_agents_approvals_withhold_a_page_title_it_may_not_see asserts the withheld title's author is named 'The owner'; with the owner flag forced false in named() that assertion fails.","supersedes":"f8c3c4ee08fe3807804f06c3a36c3b808d1c558351cee441ee211442100514d0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:02:11.811532Z","id":"2ae02d68fad89e229d1f085e2a7d878aa76bd4d7e415b4ca5bfd07fbeac1e6d7","body":{"detail":"approves_first is computed when a thread view is built (Store::approves_first, crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs). Deciding a request or revoking an approval publishes no thread event for the threads it covers, so an open artifact view keeps the old list: its Send menu can still say \"Sam approves first\" after Sam approved (or omit it after a revocation) until the thread changes or the page reloads. The send itself is unaffected: routing decides on the server.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":564},"end":{"line":618},"content_hash":"3f89c468b27ef89b09658edbaafcfb85c123211de772ab9bf8138ef6657609f3"},"suggested_fix":"Republish the covered open threads' views (or a lighter approves_first delta) on approval.made and approval.revoke, or have the Send menu ask the daemon when it opens.","summary":"A thread's approves_first is not refreshed when an approval is made or revoked","tags":["task:22","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:13:39.982743Z","id":"c4e1e5509a11a8d4a4db8f5642456bc3e3252a6bf259b31bcc2ea7952fc3b22c","body":{"detail":"Identity::caller makes the token an OwnerAgent whenever a session is named (path or X-Clax-Session), known or not; audit_actor records an agent only for a known session of the token's, the agent marker, or x-clax-via mcp, else the owner. Measured through GET /api/_test/audit/ctx: Authorization Bearer + X-Clax-Session 01JB9S00000000000000000099 (no session) and X-Clax-Session not-a-ulid both give {\"type\":\"owner\"}. Today's clients send the marker, so this bites only an older or third-party agent side; it breaks audit spec section 5.2's rule that one request is never an agent to Caller and the owner to the journal.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":492},"end":{"line":499},"content_hash":"75fc91286c48244768b0a0e9a1d2af39937a039081897bf71644933e706cbb12"},"suggested_fix":"When the token names any session that is not known, record the sessionless agent (channel as named, else mcp) instead of the owner; add the case to the_agent_channel_marker_makes_the_token_an_agent.","summary":"The token naming an unknown or non-ULID session without the agent marker is recorded as the owner, while Caller counts it as OwnerAgent","supersedes":"aad27e37c6fc12484dd639d56fdd0b30bd06e13e6870f9d185cc2bd8f085b86f","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:22:22.163984Z","id":"a67749104601409aa8ec1df771eb336e5bbcbd4ca4828b9d692efd5ab3f0ce60","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"2ae02d68fad89e229d1f085e2a7d878aa76bd4d7e415b4ca5bfd07fbeac1e6d7","summary":"Assessed: the stale hint does not lead to a wrong send. After an approval the menu still says 'Sam approves first' and the send goes straight through; after a revocation the menu omits it, the send makes the request, and the card reads 'waiting for Sam's approval' at once. Low priority, behind the default-target and hidden-request concerns on web/shell/src/view/send-target.ts and web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte.","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:36.259291Z","id":"d89d3e273efa3aef3e7d52aac1b4ddca657c2d5a6604f66e14e572e5fa15da58","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:bb547990","summary":"No thread view carries approves_first any more; the Send menu asks the daemon each time it opens, so it reflects approvals made or revoked since. Evidence: api_approvals::the_send_menu_names_agents_their_people_and_who_approves_first asks again after Sam approves and gets [null]; send-menu.test.ts checks the request as the menu opens.","supersedes":"2ae02d68fad89e229d1f085e2a7d878aa76bd4d7e415b4ca5bfd07fbeac1e6d7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:08:21.317563Z","id":"8bc1837908de86df96bdc183a8a50684f5c78c5d50d87c4e2fe9c2394ebd658d","body":{"detail":"Failure: an anonymous GET /api/events?artifact=<aid> receives feedback_state {state: withheld, approver: 'Sam'} after the owner sends a LAN viewer's thread to Sam's agent; a LAN viewer's thread card reads 'waiting for Sam's approval'. Spec 2026-10-08 section 18 gives a LAN viewer no approvals view; section 10 asks for the delivery state to read 'waiting for Sam's approval' without saying for whom. This predates bb547990, which makes the state more frequent (state_of now reads any held row). A question for the owner whether LAN viewers should see 'waiting for approval' without the name.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":598},"end":{"line":598},"content_hash":"108c411ff5f9a69e269b9f90111cda9fbfea883bc64d7e320e898a9686d499e0"},"summary":"feedback_state.approver names whose approval a thread waits for to LAN viewers and anonymous event subscribers","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:13:10.748592Z","id":"b2ae5d41e1ed5cd37e9280fc90158c238af5d0c8e1eb6606bdafb0c089cd8796","body":{"detail":"A version published from the CLI or the browser has no session, but a bearer agent's write on the public Clax needs one, and a session's harness must be one of claude, codex, grok or pi (crates/clax-server/src/routes/sessions.rs HARNESSES). The session is named for this machine (own_agent_name), but the shell's by-line shows the harness. Observed in a browser check of a pushed artifact: 'published by claude'. A harness value for another Clax's pushes (accepted from bearer grants only) would fix it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":459},"end":{"line":467},"content_hash":"b77b808550f3c2256e2f583ee2f5a5b7f2e223627b503d2defc25ecd8c7b95cf"},"summary":"The owner's own versions reach the public copy under the harness `claude`, so its by-line reads 'published by claude'","tags":["authorship","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:13:10.748634Z","id":"052ac088487da9efc9ef129aad75c107e0a03773098972d23251df575d912d8d","body":{"detail":"Assets belong to the artifact, not to a version, and the public Clax gives an uploaded asset a new ID and URL, so pushing them means uploading each and rewriting the pages' asset URLs. The push only counts them (assets_not_pushed), which clax push prints and publish_public returns.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":25},"end":{"line":26},"content_hash":"32a4c9faadd67424e9450d84a5bbe4ab696ae593e2a7da3e2191050cab7733be"},"summary":"Assets are not pushed: a page that loads one from the local daemon breaks on the public copy","tags":["deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:13:10.748672Z","id":"adde17bb291d08a59ab5afa47dc120d9ac7f354ff9dc2628d67154a44331ffa0","body":{"detail":"The link records a version only once the public Clax answers 201. If the version landed but the answer did not arrive, the next push sees the public copy one version ahead and refuses as if someone else had published. The public API has no idempotency key. A fix: on a conflict, compare the public copy's newest version's files (content_sha256) with the version that was being sent, and record it as pushed when they match.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":652},"end":{"line":663},"content_hash":"b08a57b0c83a9efc513abb305ec2d8152475359960fd5fe607ae2c506f215698"},"summary":"A push whose answer was lost (a timeout after the public Clax took the version) is refused remote_moved on retry","tags":["robustness","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/public.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:13:10.748702Z","id":"e07e241a3257bc53fc2a489d2fcfabeb6c14fcd4a3837cf00470cf6fab5d5bf3","body":{"detail":"after_publish pushes each new version of a link with auto set, in the background; a refusal (remote_moved, the remote down, a revoked token) is a tracing warning. The artifact's Publish button then shows Push v<N> again, but nothing reaches the inbox. An inbox item for a refused automatic push would surface it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":715},"end":{"line":743}},"summary":"An automatic push that is refused is only logged: the owner is not told the public copy stopped following","tags":["ux","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:13:10.749046Z","id":"3a0ac495fd367f51d55c751ff61bf4f84c70fad75abef5394b3d012cf5172986","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"60f34db5d3381b7ab85bfc1be2c3a1363dbcc38bd57bae9ecc21d028b9fb606f","summary":"The device sign-in limits (Attempt::Device, Attempt::DevicePoll) are counted in the same in-memory Limits; the store bounds what survives a restart: codes expire after 600 s, at most 1,000 wait at once (crates/clax-core/src/store/device.rs MAX_PENDING_DEVICES), and polls are slowed by polled_at on the store clock","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:07.372515Z","id":"ea3a8c17f6cc590fd63dce21d2f536f63042f21803965ba796f6e0daf6e8a8de","body":{"detail":"set_link (and list_links) accept the owner or the artifact's creator (artifact_created_by) and never ask Rights::allows. A person whose rights the owner narrowed (to read only, or none at their own artifacts) can still share their artifact by a viewer or commenter link, readable by anyone with it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1898},"end":{"line":1925},"content_hash":"be5cf915153fb068b6b6f08039715db923dae64d4f38ffad9466a3a036760b90"},"suggested_fix":"For anyone but the owner, also require MemberRights::allows_at with (clax-artifacts, update) at the artifact.","summary":"A person shares their own artifact by link whatever their current rights at it","tags":["security","rights","hosted","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:07.372991Z","id":"13efa0c82e55c729152554861ec0b9828f3ced8bee58e889fe8a8746689f5d28","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"d60ce43133c7db2ad3ee5a1728a230c0b35fe605f6b31d34049a0927fe0d93a3","summary":"Since 4f1f7191 this holds only where the host names pushers (GitRemotes::names_pushers): with REPO_STORE=artifacts a push is recorded as the owner's, so there write tokens go to the owner and the owner's agents alone (403 push_unattributed), as the prototype's owner_only did. The decision this record asks for stands for the stand-in.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:19:46.871914Z","id":"6b5ed51df820dc2040e6720175ee8e679d5ca9e000ed6570fe3cef88eb500231","body":{"detail":"hosted/src/git/tokens.ts refused write tokens to anyone but the owner (403 owner_only) because there every pushed commit was credited to the owner. Here a push is recorded as a version published by the token's holder (clax_core::store::pushes, Store::standing rechecks the pusher's update right at record time), so pushing is publishing and the route asks for the same right a publish does: under clax:collaborator that is the person's own artifacts, under clax:full every artifact. The alternative is owner and owner's agents only (Caller::Owner / OwnerAgent), refusing every person's write token.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":20},"end":{"line":28},"content_hash":"0e98812e150e2b9f3b12d9a5ac43ff8060532f49329002c749240d788fffbe66"},"summary":"A write token needs clax-artifacts update (the publish right), not the prototype's owner-only push","supersedes":"d60ce43133c7db2ad3ee5a1728a230c0b35fe605f6b31d34049a0927fe0d93a3","tags":["status:needs-decision","revisit:a person with update rights should not be able to push","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:19:46.878068Z","id":"a255cdc193251af7d839814b95f876b11243eb074f4e8682004470ad17720971","body":{"detail":"A pasted command lands in the shell's history with the token, and while git runs any user of the machine can read its -c argument in the process list. The GIT_CONFIG_COUNT/GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0/GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0 form (what jj_clone_command and the jj commands use) keeps it out of other users' process list but not out of the history, and does not work as pasted in PowerShell or cmd; a credential helper given inline (-c credential.helper=...) is on the command line the same way. Keeping it out of the history needs two steps (read the token into a variable, then run the command with it), which a one-paste flow does not have. docs/contract.md 'Git remotes' states the trade; the tokens' lives (3600 s, 900 s for agents) bound it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":693},"end":{"line":713},"content_hash":"6b54dbed5895c129171356cda07b70b28b4862cb13ea6c3e866d6a1beb86530f"},"summary":"The commands carry the token on git's command line (-c http.extraHeader), as the hosted spec's section 9 and hosted/src/git/commands.ts do, not in the environment or a credential helper","supersedes":"00ad3144f125bca53f06ff2a515d335ca22c243911a8f11015187d68a4507e12","tags":["security","revisit:shared multi-user machines are a target, or the dialog grows a two-step flow","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:19:46.884455Z","id":"12a201e39f64127e9ac763131ba81bbe75dfe6fa9b6eee31112759ebc082c2c9","body":{"detail":"recheck asks the host for every live held token (RepoDO token/held on the Worker) and, per token, builds a Visibility and reads Store::repo_history (the artifact's and its lineage's versions and refused pushers). listen runs it after every Version, ArtifactDeleted, People and Agents event burst; settle_layer before answering a request that moved the generation; and listen once when a server is built (each Durable Object wake). Fine for a handful of tokens; with many, a recheck per artifact and a per-reader Visibility cache would bound it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":908},"end":{"line":939},"content_hash":"b17df665b58dc5c49d825e15cc8d73520f3048d38ecd43a929bfefa2ebed202b"},"summary":"A recheck lists every held token from the host and walks each one's repository history: run on every relevant event, every request that moves the visibility generation, and every server built anew","supersedes":"52d6af27afcb77f3fad96e1c4143e7977002a500236076ece314f19671dbcb64","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:19:46.890690Z","id":"d1fb9735a9bd3002efddf9268964ac1acb173b031b07ddb92e184d6c40ef1332","body":{"detail":"set_link rechecks the artifact's held tokens before it answers so a person whose rights there came from the page's link loses them (git_remotes::recheck, and recheck_soon when the host fails). A member's preset rights read every artifact, so a test needs a member whose rights do not read it, a git host (TestServer git_remotes) and hosted mode; crates/clax-server/tests/api_git_tokens.rs covers the other paths.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1937},"end":{"line":1943},"content_hash":"c1569eca0d75eadc3a06808818ba5742f7cb3e307db7ef60ad77678c06ec729f"},"summary":"No test covers set_link's recheck of the artifact's git tokens","supersedes":"faaed9d6ca7b483b7bfef632f58f226223c0a26fde3eac95e0a1a8adc6b3e7ac","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:04:35.029041Z","id":"bf1f3bb5ff97b76df0982bb1622d8b45431c0612ef2cf18bfd33c080aa7f61ad","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"6b5ed51df820dc2040e6720175ee8e679d5ca9e000ed6570fe3cef88eb500231","summary":"The owner's decision: 'Anyone with update' — a write token needs clax-artifacts update at the artifact, the right a publish needs, as implemented here. With the exception the review added (4f1f7191): where the host cannot name pushers (GitRemotes::names_pushers false, Cloudflare Artifacts) write tokens stay owner-only (403 push_unattributed) until pushers can be attributed.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:04:35.038923Z","id":"0caf9cae1eb5ce354cbc3dfab666557f3bfc41d42b0407c05b13c5756dad55a9","body":{"detail":"Asker::Link has no reader (Asker::reader is None, as for people), so check_history does not run for it: no 503 while pushed commits wait (clax_core::store::pushes), and Store::repo_history's refused_pushers' commits stay reachable from main. A member's clone carries the same, but a link reaches anyone who has it. Narrowing would need a host that serves only version tags to link tokens.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":532},"end":{"line":543},"content_hash":"0d09c7764a8f34cc69851914496389ab09377c6c3b88d93e1f64ff0a1f6de19e"},"summary":"A page link's read token clones main whole: pushed commits not yet recorded as versions, and refused pushes left on main, reach whoever holds the link, though the page shows them only its versions","tags":["git","hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/socket_caps.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:11:42.825735Z","id":"b4bd61b2df11e9a3ab6b430bc229bfd43541b28d54e5e928b862c80609f721da","body":{"detail":"SocketClient::of_request answers no keys without [hosted], so SocketCaps::admit always admits there: the realtime load gate (scripts/perf-clients.py) drives thousands of /api/stream connections from one address. A LAN viewer of a daemon bound beyond loopback is as unbounded as before (see also record 51900b96 on LAN viewers' writes). Capping LAN viewers by address while exempting loopback and the token would close it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":11},"end":{"line":13},"content_hash":"fcc46cbaa0c5dcf6b1417b3b8271de27f1e7468bb5695a3c027b5d5b3f968b41"},"summary":"A local daemon caps no client's streams or sockets: a LAN viewer may open any number","tags":["security","resource","streams","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:14:09.404178Z","id":"e7847ec290755a3f74558eec53f2abf47a30a166c792e2ff12224a9aa11ded7c","body":{"detail":"inbox.rs views() renders a Reply item's thread summary and reply body for its recipient as stored; on a hosted daemon, crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs reads_comments (clax-comments read at the artifact) withholds comment text from a member on GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/threads, the stream, the snapshot and live layers, but not here. A member whose comment read at an artifact is taken away after their thread was answered still reads the agent's reply in GET /api/inbox. Approval cards (content.comments) are the member's own agent's withheld content and are a separate question.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":144},"end":{"line":158},"content_hash":"958622b22fde39306c3416c3c4883a0015ba88fbda3814c901b0507a682bbb84"},"suggested_fix":"On a hosted daemon, null reply.body and thread.summary in a member recipient's view where reads_comments is false, as the other routes do.","summary":"A hosted member's inbox reply items carry comment text without the comment-read check the threads, stream, snapshot and live routes apply","tags":["hosted","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"fabba150fcd67ebd0d145e6abb1c8491a8cdb987675a4615ff26c8579e5a0045","body":{"detail":"holds_surface(person) (holds_owner_topics() for the owner) is true while any stream of that person holds questions or inbox, and those topics stay subscribed while the tab is hidden (web/shell/src/stream.ts:23-27). crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create() uses it, for the asking agent's person, to decide whether a hook question waits in Clax or is released to the terminal at once. So a Clax tab left open in the background makes every AskUserQuestion of that person's agents wait in Clax until it is answered there, released, timed out, or Esc is pressed (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:289-302). Decision needed: should 'open' instead mean a tab seen or focused recently, or the extension's side panel being open?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1318},"end":{"line":1343},"content_hash":"ef0267ee57042e6f58c4b3ab575dbe015b81d840852637892266f23d038afb03"},"summary":"A hidden tab counts as an open Clax surface, so the AskUserQuestion hook waits in Clax","supersedes":"9fa483ae149b813d992787142e1cfa53fd6cdac6b4bbe1e0f12636b4e1a3eac6","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"2b9834089ab6131eec164addebf62ee1cba97cb83d22bb0b2599974534cb0f15","body":{"detail":"Withhold::approval runs Store::request_state once per thread that withholds anything, so a listing of N such threads makes N indexed reads (plus st.owner() when the owner is withheld). Versions and names are cached per call. vis_threads_ms (Task 25) will show whether it matters.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1486},"end":{"line":1513},"content_hash":"05c56d201c29c0092d6039e9c09166c4bdf07ea63e935e45f87326bf15b12593"},"summary":"Each thread with withheld content costs one approval_requests query in a listing","supersedes":"cb4161519ccae68ce6c3608965e5383f03f1bc69b38fec32544fe17a0dd79653","tags":["perf","visibility","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"f695f0110edce8ac50793f99fc5e7e04d6917287b048afb3d79fda6aa7dcd354","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1536},"end":{"line":1580},"content_hash":"ddf90a27cffb9eae9f415b9f193ba4f15b3c221446be555e0e4c03e03e2abb50"},"summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","supersedes":"777f73035d7a5f9161487b888cffb6089b5d3d309dfee4e420a23e273c5ba40b","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"8262e0f07be29cfa0e2f99e0ec76a7f9ea1fe367144adc7ca56d8ba15dc4101d","body":{"detail":"Identity::caller makes the token an OwnerAgent whenever a session is named (path or X-Clax-Session), known or not; audit_actor records an agent only for a known session of the token's, the agent marker, or x-clax-via mcp, else the owner. Measured through GET /api/_test/audit/ctx: Authorization Bearer + X-Clax-Session 01JB9S00000000000000000099 (no session) and X-Clax-Session not-a-ulid both give {\"type\":\"owner\"}. Today's clients send the marker, so this bites only an older or third-party agent side; it breaks audit spec section 5.2's rule that one request is never an agent to Caller and the owner to the journal.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":630},"end":{"line":637},"content_hash":"75fc91286c48244768b0a0e9a1d2af39937a039081897bf71644933e706cbb12"},"suggested_fix":"When the token names any session that is not known, record the sessionless agent (channel as named, else mcp) instead of the owner; add the case to the_agent_channel_marker_makes_the_token_an_agent.","summary":"The token naming an unknown or non-ULID session without the agent marker is recorded as the owner, while Caller counts it as OwnerAgent","supersedes":"c4e1e5509a11a8d4a4db8f5642456bc3e3252a6bf259b31bcc2ea7952fc3b22c","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"077718a793f295ece42e6924e14dedb1fbf2eb1a6663343e1f77d30f0ba0a66c","body":{"detail":"api_agent_auth::the_extractor_refuses_a_persons_agent_on_an_owner_agents_route now asserts that every Filtered need in ROUTES is live. The not_yet branches (agent.rs Agent<N> extraction and the body gate) stay for a Filtered route added later; remove them, with FILTERED_LIVE, once no task plans one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":531},"end":{"line":531},"content_hash":"e07bad372e55913af9df7b2c800d2741a700fd885fb02cc043d3e30bf32f99fd"},"summary":"Every Filtered need is now in FILTERED_LIVE, so the 503 not_yet path serves no route","supersedes":"99a042ac45d79e62841b6c39d0b895df49f43c7263ef17617110cef518c5c105","tags":["people","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"d3467ffcd21274f0ed17c8cb3025dce304bc8aa4e5248f984a71e8b49bd1597c","body":{"detail":"Every handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1046},"end":{"line":1046},"content_hash":"95e634966fc956bcf03f44fdf7131faa6bc9307f6e163a961719bf6f762fe602"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve Person/Viewer lazily in Agent<N> (only a person's agent needs the store), or fold the read into the handler's own store_call.","summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","supersedes":"b89764e25b62b35248d219d5b75a544545758bbc4ac7bf7785fd7664e41be66e","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"7e78b30ae313437d51c0a6eedb40f1bb60b0f2c0e259812838028c3b789a7584","body":{"detail":"Limits holds its buckets in a Mutex<HashMap>; a restarted daemon forgets them, and a Cloudflare deployment with several isolates or Durable Objects would count per instance. Past MAX_CLIENTS (10000) clients the map is cleared.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":175},"end":{"line":178},"content_hash":"c3d9cee2df2daa7466bec6f2d7785f46a526e8ffaae9cfc54cec9c2e75b2fe50"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the buckets in the store (or one Durable Object) in the Worker build.","summary":"The abuse limits live in the process's memory: they reset on restart and are per instance","supersedes":"60f34db5d3381b7ab85bfc1be2c3a1363dbcc38bd57bae9ecc21d028b9fb606f","tags":["hosted","security","wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"6a856c88dacacc0cd564edb3fb8debab0f8222517c7a4149c32911b5679c938a","body":{"detail":"content_key is an HMAC of <aid>/<n> under the daemon token, as the prototype's commit hash (hosted/src/content.ts) never expired either. A person whose rights narrow, or a guest whose page stops being shared, still reads every version address they were handed (not later versions). A new daemon token changes every key.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":479},"end":{"line":481},"content_hash":"cd8d880448cdb31132019e34c90867877b5c99850f7b334415ffebc58c2ce63d"},"suggested_fix":"Mix a per-artifact generation into the key and bump it when the page stops being shared or a person's rights narrow.","summary":"A content key never expires: whoever saw a version's keyed address keeps reading it after losing the right","supersedes":"b8e18181a0277265ae574d0bcffc8dc10211710da02e04f243912a42f62666f0","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"11916570150370956ef353e1a1bd661c5d34b08c1f6a4e83eceb59211cbe6a9d","body":{"detail":"The gate could require /c/<aid>/draft/k/<content key of the base version>/<agent>/<token>/…, so a draft URL is also bound to a key the daemon derives. Not taken: the draft token is already 128 random bits minted per revision (clax_core::drafts::new_token), handed only to people who may read the artifact, and it expires with the revision, which a content key never does; a second key adds a path segment the shell's draftSrc (web/shell/src/view/draft-model.ts) and the artifact host rewrite (crates/clax-server/src/host.rs) would carry for no capability the token lacks.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":577},"end":{"line":582},"content_hash":"1784c2024ba3d1b89730649afd8e4da2b8bb437c88275427391e1e49fcc54dd8"},"summary":"Draft URLs keyed by the version's content key as well as the draft token","supersedes":"c50614a61354a4952ebfad0463f8fbc9021f234c3c6a6736600a5586cc8ffa89","tags":["hosted","drafts","revisit:a draft token is logged, persisted or handed to anyone who may not read the artifact","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"08ac048387266cd2bb928126e6b6e4052ebff6d7982d2644f9c29c96fc519543","body":{"detail":"member_need checks the artifact only when the query names one; without it the routes answer every artifact this viewer has marks on (IDs and counts, no titles). Inbox items addressed to the person stay after their rights narrow.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":819},"end":{"line":823},"content_hash":"658bd678f5f2ca9606250a4a71b16315b8e871172a66044341faa0416f943b70"},"suggested_fix":"Filter those answers with Agent::read_rights as GET /api/artifacts does.","summary":"A person's /api/viewers/me/attention and /api/viewers/me/seen without ?artifact=, and their inbox items, are not filtered by their rights","supersedes":"d119d9ace103f244ffaaa55fee86c2cac074387a3a63d0634ef7ab74f25c8659","tags":["hosted","visibility","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"c9ab20512e515827c65422e29061c4c54e810be2f8e39a232797ebb15228ac5e","body":{"detail":"member_gate drops `gallery` from such a person's subscriptions because gallery events (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs routes, project) carry every artifact's titles and thread summaries; their gallery refreshes on load only.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":899},"end":{"line":899},"content_hash":"cc7f883b42e8d834a7aa6a6e9f0ce461e48a8702065827af2cbdbbf741b80e96"},"suggested_fix":"Gate gallery items per subscriber by artifact (a read filter fixed at subscribe time) instead of dropping the topic.","summary":"A person whose rights do not read every artifact gets no gallery stream topic, so their gallery does not update live","supersedes":"d73bf973a30ee13967209163d6487b70e64da2ed0c003205d38c47822b39083b","tags":["hosted","ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"c58b033348ff00c73f0cc78f0a1bccaae061e4dc2d70cf4e28423185449e7695","body":{"detail":"The prototype let a commenter resolve or reopen threads they started (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design.md section 7). LinkAccess::rights (crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs) holds no comments resolve; checking a thread's creator in the gate would need a store read per request.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1060},"end":{"line":1062},"content_hash":"f8564687d21d97fe5615a5674a21b9444ea4c648abef2584844c61b8e5250507"},"summary":"A guest may not resolve or reopen threads, even their own","supersedes":"a78775d9f6e025c45ecfab715052ec49291488ebd013822b3ebd7d735391cb0d","tags":["revisit:guests ask to resolve their own threads","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"9bcf0380fb4fa6531995f18637bbb012e2d39efaeb42770983a749870228ffe0","body":{"detail":"PUT /api/viewers/me with no session makes a guest viewer row and a session whatever the site shares; Attempt::Guest limits it to five per client and then one per two minutes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1476},"end":{"line":1484},"content_hash":"7b0b50000594786778769269c90c8b6ed7c453ad2d601bcdc1a9e8dbea8ea63c"},"suggested_fix":"Require the page the visitor names (artifact_id in the body) to be shared for commenting.","summary":"A visitor may become a guest without any page being shared by link","supersedes":"e959fccd8de5e34c4d95e18da567fda71eb2608f4c26539c339424477822fade","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"b9b36f2eb38a562bb7967e3be7018b89c045732c94b85fa80f90e29939a7ee1b","body":{"detail":"Failure: an anonymous GET /api/events?artifact=<aid> receives feedback_state {state: withheld, approver: 'Sam'} after the owner sends a LAN viewer's thread to Sam's agent; a LAN viewer's thread card reads 'waiting for Sam's approval'. Spec 2026-10-08 section 18 gives a LAN viewer no approvals view; section 10 asks for the delivery state to read 'waiting for Sam's approval' without saying for whom. This predates bb547990, which makes the state more frequent (state_of now reads any held row). A question for the owner whether LAN viewers should see 'waiting for approval' without the name.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":610},"end":{"line":610},"content_hash":"108c411ff5f9a69e269b9f90111cda9fbfea883bc64d7e320e898a9686d499e0"},"summary":"feedback_state.approver names whose approval a thread waits for to LAN viewers and anonymous event subscribers","supersedes":"8bc1837908de86df96bdc183a8a50684f5c78c5d50d87c4e2fe9c2394ebd658d","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"668f8f3a47771314472960808072c22ccdbdfce019544e2bf490ba0f39b094f0","body":{"detail":"hosted/src/git/tokens.ts refused write tokens to anyone but the owner (403 owner_only) because there every pushed commit was credited to the owner. Here a push is recorded as a version published by the token's holder (clax_core::store::pushes, Store::standing rechecks the pusher's update right at record time), so pushing is publishing and the route asks for the same right a publish does: under clax:collaborator that is the person's own artifacts, under clax:full every artifact. The alternative is owner and owner's agents only (Caller::Owner / OwnerAgent), refusing every person's write token.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":23},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"0e98812e150e2b9f3b12d9a5ac43ff8060532f49329002c749240d788fffbe66"},"summary":"A write token needs clax-artifacts update (the publish right), not the prototype's owner-only push","supersedes":"6b5ed51df820dc2040e6720175ee8e679d5ca9e000ed6570fe3cef88eb500231","tags":["status:needs-decision","revisit:a person with update rights should not be able to push","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"c906a64174f197a4225370378ddc94dff5091f80e6fee512912bf83a7b095512","body":{"detail":"A pasted command lands in the shell's history with the token, and while git runs any user of the machine can read its -c argument in the process list. The GIT_CONFIG_COUNT/GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0/GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0 form (what jj_clone_command and the jj commands use) keeps it out of other users' process list but not out of the history, and does not work as pasted in PowerShell or cmd; a credential helper given inline (-c credential.helper=...) is on the command line the same way. Keeping it out of the history needs two steps (read the token into a variable, then run the command with it), which a one-paste flow does not have. docs/contract.md 'Git remotes' states the trade; the tokens' lives (3600 s, 900 s for agents) bound it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":730},"end":{"line":750},"content_hash":"6b54dbed5895c129171356cda07b70b28b4862cb13ea6c3e866d6a1beb86530f"},"summary":"The commands carry the token on git's command line (-c http.extraHeader), as the hosted spec's section 9 and hosted/src/git/commands.ts do, not in the environment or a credential helper","supersedes":"a255cdc193251af7d839814b95f876b11243eb074f4e8682004470ad17720971","tags":["security","revisit:shared multi-user machines are a target, or the dialog grows a two-step flow","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"273412582e980c19d7153f66026038faf323b94fe875b165b2eaaa7b970f767d","body":{"detail":"recheck asks the host for every live held token (RepoDO token/held on the Worker) and, per token, builds a Visibility and reads Store::repo_history (the artifact's and its lineage's versions and refused pushers). listen runs it after every Version, ArtifactDeleted, People and Agents event burst; settle_layer before answering a request that moved the generation; and listen once when a server is built (each Durable Object wake). Fine for a handful of tokens; with many, a recheck per artifact and a per-reader Visibility cache would bound it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":948},"end":{"line":979},"content_hash":"b17df665b58dc5c49d825e15cc8d73520f3048d38ecd43a929bfefa2ebed202b"},"summary":"A recheck lists every held token from the host and walks each one's repository history: run on every relevant event, every request that moves the visibility generation, and every server built anew","supersedes":"12a201e39f64127e9ac763131ba81bbe75dfe6fa9b6eee31112759ebc082c2c9","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"ebe93fe2768eda2ad0f2666c77b8d11afb6fbe251bd7ea027653cd8c5c4a1c5f","body":{"detail":"set_link (and list_links) accept the owner or the artifact's creator (artifact_created_by) and never ask Rights::allows. A person whose rights the owner narrowed (to read only, or none at their own artifacts) can still share their artifact by a viewer or commenter link, readable by anyone with it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2036},"end":{"line":2063},"content_hash":"be5cf915153fb068b6b6f08039715db923dae64d4f38ffad9466a3a036760b90"},"suggested_fix":"For anyone but the owner, also require MemberRights::allows_at with (clax-artifacts, update) at the artifact.","summary":"A person shares their own artifact by link whatever their current rights at it","supersedes":"ea3a8c17f6cc590fd63dce21d2f536f63042f21803965ba796f6e0daf6e8a8de","tags":["security","rights","hosted","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:31:11.709153Z","id":"bdd021e74dcf61c0667fc1d878a8beb4cfc76bbe33bd368a2fb60ba52a3cd200","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate head left by a merge: the same record as 9fa483ae149b813d992787142e1cfa53fd6cdac6b4bbe1e0f12636b4e1a3eac6 (kept), re-anchored on a parallel branch.","supersedes":"2b69aca3dfe727b1a12aeb35e4d478959f8477474fd1d9e0b174e0283a75d20e","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:31:11.715814Z","id":"0f11c6425d905fa8d1b0b55ff0fdbde499a99c16bba7fa954008b06ac350b813","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate head left by a merge: this is a parallel branch's re-anchor of the record that c8d0794f84fb243f01b0cbdf6c48f8be81deec2364bfe8a14e744a0898184914 closed (Withhold::named now names authors with clax_core::feedback::person_name, which gives an unnamed owner 'The owner' (approvals.rs person() uses the same helper). ). That close stands in the merged code; this head carries no new content.","supersedes":"55570b4b94efbe5ea245e2316b975dfa632f69f6f6e5c35b28d93ec73c5d0e1d","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:31:11.722435Z","id":"407c91968af74d9c3f9849b55033a01780a0b00d26bc4188f4eba3108ee7d6fc","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate head left by a merge: the same record as cb4161519ccae68ce6c3608965e5383f03f1bc69b38fec32544fe17a0dd79653 (kept), re-anchored on a parallel branch.","supersedes":"93c1e71be55982a6aa270fb74e40a4a84bfb703fde1720b9c4be019f2f596f1d","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
